('Alfredo Sauce', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1/2 cup butter", "1 (8 oz) cream cheese", "2 teas. garlic powder", "6 ounces Parmesan cheese", "1/8 teas. black pepper", "? teas. Italian seasoning", "? tbls. garlic minced", "? cups milk", "1/4 c. parsley", "1 teas. basil", "1/4 Romano cheese"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '["sauce", "alfredo", "pasta", "cheese"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten notebook page. The amounts for Italian seasoning, minced garlic and milk are hidden under a folded/taped strip at the left edge. Ingredients only, no directions. "1/4 Romano cheese" has no unit.

Couldn''t read for sure: amounts hidden for Italian seasoning, minced garlic and milk; 1 teas. basil', NULL),
('Angel Chicken Rice', NULL, 8, 10, 25, '["3 cups cooked chicken, diced or shredded", "3 cups cooked rice", "1/2 cup butter, room temperature and cubed", "8 ounces cream cheese, room temperature and cubed", "10.5 ounces cream of chicken soup", "3 cloves garlic, minced", "0.7 ounce Italian dressing mix (I used Good Seasons)", "1 cup chicken stock", "2 cups shredded Colby Jack cheese, divided use", "salt and pepper to taste", "fresh parsley for garnish", "cooking spray"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat oven to 350 degrees F, and generously spray a 9x13\" casserole dish with cooking spray.", "In a microwave-safe bowl, soften the cream cheese and butter in the microwave for 20-30 seconds. Whisk until smooth.", "In a large mixing bowl, combine the cooked chicken, rice, butter and cream cheese ...", "Top with the remaining shredded cheese.", "Cover the dish with foil, and bake in the preheated oven for 20-25 minutes, until the cheese is melted and the casserole is bubbling.", "Remove from oven, and allow the casserole to cool for 5 minutes. Remove foil.", "Garnish with fresh parsley, and enjoy."]'::jsonb, '["Ashley''s Recipes", "chicken", "rice", "casserole", "comfort food"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'From Ashley''s Recipes (Facebook post, phone screenshots). Subtitle on the post: ''Cheesy Angel Chicken and Rice Casserole''. Two screenshots: one with ingredients and the start of the instructions, the other with the end. The middle of the instructions is missing (after ''combine the cooked chicken, rice, butter and cream cheese'' - presumably mixing in the soup, garlic, dressing mix, stock, half the cheese, salt and pepper, and spreading in the dish). Total time 35 minutes; 548 kcal per serving. Hashtags: #angelchickenrice #cheesycasserole #chickenandrice #comfortfood #easydinner #familymeal #cheesygoodness #casserole #bakeddinner #weeknightmeal.

Couldn''t read for sure: middle of instructions missing between the two screenshots

A page of this recipe was missing from the photos.', NULL),
('Applebees Chicken Wonton Tacos (Copy-cat)', 'This is a copy-cat recipe for Applebees Chicken Wonton Tacos -- a fusion dish with elements from both Mexican and Asian Cuisine.', 8, NULL, 40, '["1/2 cup stir fry sauce (like Kikkoman)", "1 cup asian dressing (Toasted Sesame, like Kraft brand)", "1/4 cup soy sauce", "1/4 cup teriyaki sauce", "2 pounds boneless skinless chicken breast (diced)", "1/4 cup asian dressing (Toasted Sesame)", "2 cups coleslaw (chopped cabbage Mix)", "1/2 cup green onion (finely diced)", "1/2 cup cilantro (finely diced)", "1/2 cup red onion", "20 wonton wrappers", "1/4 cup olive oil", "lime slices (Fresh)"]'::jsonb, '["Combine first 5 ingredients & marinate in refrigerator for one hour.", "Toss cabbage with remaining 1/4 c. Of Toasted Sesame Asian Dressing & set aside."]'::jsonb, '["Yummly", "chicken", "tacos", "Asian", "Mexican", "copycat", "Applebee''s"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'From Yummly (web printout pages 1/4 and 2/4, printed 6/1/2021). By ANNEWITHHELD. 13 ingredients, 40 minutes, 330 calories, 8 servings. The steps stop after the ''STEP 3'' heading at the bottom of page 2/4; Step 3 onward is on pages 3/4-4/4, which are not in the photos.

Couldn''t read for sure: ''2 pounds boneless skinless chicken breast'': ''skinless'' mostly hidden by glare; ''1/4 cup asian dressing (Toasted Sesame)'': middle hidden by glare; ''lime slices (Fresh...'': the rest of the parenthetical is hidden by glare; ''like Kraft brand'': cut off at the page edge as ''Kraft brar''

A page of this recipe was missing from the photos.', 'https://www.yummly.com/recipe/Applebees-Chicken-Wonton-Tacos-_Copy-cat_-1427035?columns=3&position=2%2F2'),
('Bacon Cheeseburger Casserole', NULL, 8, 15, 35, '["1 lb. ground beef", "1 onion, chopped", "1/3 cup ketchup", "2 Tbsp. yellow mustard", "1 cup KRAFT Shredded Sharp Cheddar Cheese", "8 slices OSCAR MAYER Bacon, cooked, crumbled", "4 cups (1/2 of 32-oz. pkg.) frozen bite-size seasoned potato nuggets", "cooking spray"]'::jsonb, '["Heat: Heat oven to 400°F.", "Brown: Brown meat with onions in skillet; drain. Stir in ketchup and mustard.", "Spoon: Spoon into 9-inch square baking dish sprayed with cooking spray; top with remaining ingredients.", "Bake: Bake 30 to 35 min. or until casserole is heated through and potato nuggets are golden brown."]'::jsonb, '["Kraft", "beef", "bacon", "casserole", "tater tots"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Kraft Recipes printout (page 1 of 2, printed 2/10/2014). Total time 50 min; 8 servings, 1 cup each. Kraft Kitchens tips: Healthy Living: Save 50 calories and 6g of fat per serving by preparing with extra-lean ground beef, KRAFT 2% Milk Shredded Cheddar Cheese and OSCAR MAYER Turkey Bacon. Special Extra: Add 1 chopped tomato to cooked meat with the ketchup and mustard. Nutrition per serving: 310 calories, 19g total fat, 7g saturated fat, 55mg cholesterol, 690mg sodium, 18g carbohydrate, 1g dietary fiber, 4g sugars, 17g protein. Page 2 of 2 not in the photos (the recipe is complete on page 1).

Couldn''t read for sure: ''Shredded'' and ''OSCAR MAYER'' partly obscured by glare; ''32-oz. pkg.'' partly obscured', NULL),
('Baked French Toast', NULL, 8, NULL, 60, '["1 c. brown sugar", "1/2 c. melted butter", "1 teas cinnamon", "bread", "1 1/2 c. milk", "6 eggs"]'::jsonb, '["Mix & pour into pan: 1 c. brown sugar, 1/2 c. melted butter, 1 teas cinnamon.", "Layer bread and mix 1 1/2 c. milk, 6 eggs; pour over bread & let sit overnight.", "Bake 350° for 45-60 min. Flip bread 1/2 thru baking to carmalize both sides of bread."]'::jsonb, '["breakfast", "french toast", "make-ahead", "casserole"]'::jsonb, '["breakfast"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe card taped in a spiral recipe notebook. Amount of bread not given.

Couldn''t read for sure: servings ''8'' (single scrawled digit); ''Flip bread 1/2 thru baking'' - ''1/2 thru'' faded', NULL),
('Baked Potato Soup', NULL, NULL, NULL, 75, '["4 large potatoes", "2/3 cup butter", "2/3 cup flour", "3/4 tsp salt", "1/4 tsp white pepper", "6 cups milk", "1 cup sour cream", "1/4 cup green onions", "10 slices of bacon", "1 cup cheese", "1/2 cup half & half"]'::jsonb, '["Bake potatoes at 350 for 65-75 min.", "In large saucepan, melt butter, stir in flour, salt & pepper until smooth. Gradually add milk. Bring to boil. Remove from heat and put in sour cream, potatoes and onions, bacon & cheese."]'::jsonb, '["soup", "potato", "bacon"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe (Evernote printout of a spiral notebook page, page 2/3, 2/4/2021). Written to the side of the ingredient list, handwritten: "can vegetable broth" / "bacon grease". The half & half is listed but not mentioned in the directions. cookMinutes is the potato baking time only.

Couldn''t read for sure: side note read as "can vegetable broth" (written "canvegtible broth"); side note "bacon grease"', NULL),
('Baked Sweet and Sour Chicken, Pineapple and Peppers', 'The BEST Sweet and Sour Chicken - takeout OR homemade - I have ever had in my entire life! This Sweet and Sour Chicken Recipe is also baked with pineapple, carrots, onions and bell peppers so its a complete meal-in-one with no need to stir fry extra veggies!', 4, 30, 50, '["3-4 boneless skinless chicken breasts (1 1/2 pounds), cut in bite-size pieces", "3 eggs", "1/2 cup flour", "1 1/3 cup cornstarch", "1/2 teaspoon garlic powder", "1/2 teaspoon salt", "1/4 teaspoon pepper", "1/4 teaspoon ginger powder", "1/4 teaspoon onion powder", "1/2 cup pineapple juice from 20 oz. pineapple tidbits can listed below", "1 cup red wine vinegar", "1 1/2 cups sugar", "1/4 cup + 2 tablespoons ketchup", "1 small onion, diced", "2 tablespoons soy sauce", "4 garlic cloves, minced", "1 teaspoon salt", "1/2 teaspoon red pepper flakes", "1/2 teaspoon ginger powder", "1 20 oz. can pineapple tidbits in juice", "1 green bell pepper, chopped", "1 red bell pepper, chopped", "1 cup carrots sliced as THINLY as possible (2-3 carrots)", "oil (enough to cover the bottom of a large skillet)", "non-stick cooking spray"]'::jsonb, '["Add \"Sweet and Sour Sauce\" ingredients to a medium/large saucepan, stir and bring to a boil then reduce to a gentle simmer. Allow to simmer while you prepare the chicken and dice the vegetables, stirring occasionally (turn off if longer than 20 minutes). Note, the sauce will not thicken, simmering is to soften the onions and blend flavors.", "Preheat oven to 350 degrees and lightly grease a 9x13 baking dish with non-stick cooking spray.", "Whisk eggs together in a large bowl; set aside. Add 1/2 cup flour to a large freezer bag; set aside next to eggs. Whisk cornstarch, garlic powder, salt, pepper, ginger powder and onion powder in medium bowl; set aside next to flour.", "Add chicken to eggs and coat, then remove, allowing excess to drip off, then add to freezer bag with flour. Toss until evenly coated then discard any extra flour. Add cornstarch/spices to the chicken in the freezer bag and shake until evenly coated.", "Over high heat, heat enough oil (any kind) to generously cover the bottom of a large skillet until hot and rippling. Add chicken and cook 1-2 minutes per side, or until browned but not cooked through. (You may need to cook in 2 batches depending on size of your skillet). Transfer chicken to prepared 9x13 baking dish.", "Add carrots pineapple and peppers to the sweet and sauce and mix until well combined. Pour sauce over chicken and stir until sauce/chicken/vegetables are evenly combined. Cook, uncovered for 50 minutes or until sauce thickens, stirring occasionally.", "Serve over rice."]'::jsonb, '["Carlsbad Cravings", "chicken", "pineapple", "Chinese", "sweet and sour", "baked"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from Carlsbad Cravings, 2 pages (printed 12/15/21). Servings printed as ''4-6''. Course: Main Course. Total time 1 hour 20 minutes. Recipe note: "**If your chicken breasts are extra thick (like the ones from Costco), I recommend tenderizing/flattening with a meat mallet (or the side of a large can beforehand)". Serve over rice.

Couldn''t read for sure: ''meal-in-one'' in blurb partly washed out; Course value washed out (probably ''Main Course''); ''1/4 teaspoon pepper'' and ''1/4 teaspoon ginger powder'': ''teaspoon'' partly washed out; step 3 ''bowl; set aside'', ''cornstarch, garlic powder'', ''set aside next to flour'' partly washed out; step 4 ''then remove'' partly washed out; notes ''meat mallet'' partly washed out', 'https://carlsbadcravings.com/baked-sweet-and-sour-chicken-pineapple-carrots-and-bell-peppers/'),
('Banana Nut Bread', NULL, NULL, NULL, 35, '["3 bananas", "2 eggs", "1/4 cup oil", "1 cup oatmeal", "1/2 cup of almond flour (you can use oatmeal as well)", "1 tsp cinnamon", "1 tsp baking powder", "1/4 cup monk fruit sweetener", "1 tsp baking soda", "pinch of salt"]'::jsonb, '["Mix everything and turn on the oven at 350F. Let it cook above 30 or 35 minutes."]'::jsonb, '["Daystar", "bread", "banana", "quick bread", "baking"]'::jsonb, '["breakfast"]'::jsonb, 'Printout of Daystar "Joni''s Recipes" (same printout as Magic Cookies). No nuts are listed despite the title.

Couldn''t read for sure: fractions for oil and monk fruit sweetener: best reading 1/4 (small print); almond flour amount: best reading 1/2', NULL),
('BBQ Ranch Pork Chops Crock Pot Recipe', 'Tonight, dinner will be a showstopper with these easy 4 ingredient Crock Pot BBQ Ranch Pork Chops on the menu!', 4, 5, 240, '["1.5 lbs boneless center cut pork loin chops (approx. 4 chops)", "18 oz. Sweet Baby Ray''s barbecue sauce (1 bottle)", "1 oz. Hidden Valley Ranch seasoning mix (1 packet) or 3 Tbsp buttermilk ranch dressing mix", "14.5 oz. Swanson chicken broth (1 can)"]'::jsonb, '["Pour can of Chicken Broth into bottom of Crock Pot", "Place Pork Chops in Crock Pot, and cook on LOW for 3 1/2 hours, covered.", "After 3 1/2 hours on LOW, drain juices from Crock Pot", "Mix together Barbecue Sauce and Ranch Packet in medium bowl.", "Pour mixture of Pork Chops, and cook on LOW for 30 more minutes, or until done. Enjoy!!"]'::jsonb, '["The Frugal Girls", "pork", "pork chops", "slow cooker", "BBQ", "American"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from The Frugal Girls (printed 2/3/2021). Course: Entree. Cuisine: American. Author: The Frugal Girls. Total time 4 hrs 5 mins. Step 5 is printed ''Pour mixture of Pork Chops'' (probably meant ''over'').

Couldn''t read for sure: step 4 ''Barbecue'' partly washed out; step 5 ''Pork'' washed out; step 3 ''LOW'' partly washed out', 'https://thefrugalgirls.com/2017/07/bbq-ranch-pork-chops.html'),
('BBQ Sauce', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 c. yellow mustard", "1/2 c. sugar", "1/4 c. brown sugar", "3/4 c. cider vinegar", "1/4 c. water", "2 tbls chili powder", "1 teas. black pepper", "1 teas. white pepper", "1/4 teas. cayenne", "1/2 teas. soy sauce", "2 tbls. butter", "1 tbls. liquid smoke"]'::jsonb, '["Cook mustard, sugar, brown sugar, cidar, water, chillie, pepper + cayenne in sauce pan for 30 min.", "The soy sauce, butter + smoke for 10 min."]'::jsonb, '["sauce", "BBQ", "mustard"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten notebook page (same page as the Alfredo Sauce). The second step reads "The soy sauce, butter + smoke for 10 min" (probably "Then add the soy sauce...").

Couldn''t read for sure: ''The'' in step 2 (probably ''Then'')', NULL),
('Beef Stroganoff', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 lb. beef", "1 medium onion", "1 cup sour cream", "1 can beef broth", "1/2 cup water", "3 cups noodles, uncooked", "1 can cream of mushroom"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '["beef", "pasta", "stroganoff"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten in a spiral notebook (Evernote printout); ingredients only, no directions. ''1 can cream of mushroom'' is written in a different hand/pen off to the side. The printed Bisquick Deluxe Cheeseburger Melt card is taped on the same page.

