('Bell Pepper Sandwich', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 small green bell pepper", "1.5 oz cream cheese, softened", "2 tsp stone-ground mustard", "1 1/2 tsp Salt-Free Everything Bagel Seasoning", "4 slices deli turkey", "2 slices bacon, cooked, broken in half", "1 slice Provolone cheese, cut in half", "2 tbsp mashed avocado", "3 slices thinly-sliced cucumber"]'::jsonb, '["Slice bell pepper in half, de-seed, then de-vein", "To both sides of pepper, spread on cream cheese and mustard before sprinkling on Everything Bagel Seasoning. Add 2 slices of deli turkey to each side of pepper, one slice of bacon to one side and one slice of bacon to the other side. Provolone to one side, mashed avocado atop Provolone, then cucumber slices atop avocado.", "Assemble sandwich by placing the side with fewer ingredients atop the other side, cut in half with a serrated knife, and serve."]'::jsonb, '["plantbasedandveganism.com", "turkey", "sandwich", "keto", "low carb", "bell pepper"]'::jsonb, '["lunch"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout, page 4 of 11 only (pages with the title, description, servings and times not in the photos). Title taken from the footer URL (''bell-pepper-sandwich''). Page header: ''Free Keto Meal Plan: KETO DIET PLAN FOR BEGINNERS STEP BY STEP GUIDE''. Recipe Notes (partly covered by a photo on the printout; cut-off text marked ...): Green Bell Pepper Substitution: Some people prefer to not ea[t] ... fan, try red, yellow, or orange. If you don''t like raw bell peppers ... sandwich or you can make it into a sandwich and then grill it o... You could also make a lettuce wrap. Cream Cheese Substitution: Mayonnaise would work great he[re] ... egg-free. You can also omit the cream cheese. How To Make This Recipe Dairy-Free: Use mayonnaise instead ... omitting the Provolone.

Couldn''t read for sure: title inferred from the footer URL, not printed on this page; ''1 1/2 tsp'' everything bagel seasoning: fraction is blurry, could be 1 1/4; footer URL partly blurry: https://plantbasedandveganism.com/bell-pepper-sandwich-100... (not used as sourceUrl)

A page of this recipe was missing from the photos.', NULL),
('Best Ever Deviled Eggs', NULL, 12, 5, 12, '["6 eggs hardboiled & sliced in half", "2 tablespoons mayonnaise", "1 scant tablespoon mustard", "1 teaspoon worcestershire sauce", "a splash of hot sauce Frank''s Red Hot is my favorite", "salt & pepper to taste", "paprika to garnish"]'::jsonb, '["Place your cooked egg yolks in a small bowl & mash them up with a fork. Stir in the mayo, mustard, worcestershire sauce, hot sauce, salt, & pepper. Scoop the filling into the egg whites. Sprinkle with paprika."]'::jsonb, '["Mrs Happy Homemaker", "eggs", "appetizer", "side", "deviled eggs"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from Mrs Happy Homemaker, printed 12/15/21. Servings: 1 dozen deviled eggs. Total time 17 mins. Rated 5 from 16 votes. The footer URL is partly obscured (…happyhomemaker.com/best-ever-deviled-eggs/).', NULL),
('Better Than Takeout Fried Rice', 'Skip the delivery! Our 20-minute Better Than Takeout Fried Rice brings the sizzle of restaurant-style flavors right to your kitchen table.', 6, 8, 12, '["3 Tbsp butter, divided", "3 eggs, lightly beaten", "1 large carrot, peeled and cubed", "1 small white onion, chopped", "3 cloves garlic, minced", "4-5 cups rice, preferably long-grain rice (jasmine or basmati), cooked and chilled", "1 cup frozen peas", "4 green onions, thinly sliced", "1/4 cup soy sauce*, plus more to taste", "2 tsp sesame oil", "3 tsp oyster sauce", "salt and pepper"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat a large skillet or wok to medium heat. I''ve used both nonstick and regular skillets; I kind of prefer nonstick for this rice.", "Add 1 tbsp. of butter to the pan.", "Once the butter has melted, pour the lightly beaten eggs. Let them cook for about 30-40 seconds or until set, then scramble.", "Once the eggs are fully cooked, remove them and set them aside.", "Add the remaining butter to the pan. When it''s hot, add the carrot and onion, and cook until tender.", "Next, add the garlic and cook until fragrant, taking care not to brown. Turn the heat up slightly and add the cold rice and peas.", "Then, cook the mixture for about 3-4 minutes (it will sizzle and should brown a bit).", "Add the eggs, green onions, soy sauce, sesame oil, and oyster sauce.", "Cook for a few more minutes or until the mixture is hot.", "Season with salt and pepper, and serve immediately."]'::jsonb, '["Life Made Simple", "rice", "fried rice", "Chinese", "side", "eggs"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from Life Made Simple (lifemadesimplebakes.com). Two printouts of the same recipe are in the photos: one dated 8/11/24 (pages 1-2 of 4; pages 3-4 not in the photos) and one dated 6/14/25 (pages 13-14 of 18), which together give the full ingredient list and all 10 steps. Author: Andrea. Course: Side Dish. Cuisine: Chinese. Calories: 585 kcal. Rated 4.79 from 144 votes. The asterisk note for the soy sauce is not on these pages.', 'https://lifemadesimplebakes.com/better-than-takeout-fried-rice/'),
('Biscuits and Gravy Casserole', 'For a delicious breakfast that is so easy to make, this Biscuits and Gravy Breakfast Casserole is perfect! Biscuit dough topped with browned breakfast sausage, cheddar cheese, eggs beaten with milk, and peppered gravy, then baked until puffed up and bubbly. This is a great a way to start the day!', 8, 15, 45, '["8 count package refrigerated biscuit dough use large biscuits, such as Grands", "1 pound bulk sausage", "1 cup shredded cheddar cheese", "6 large eggs", "1/2 cup milk", "salt and pepper to taste", "1 2 3/4 ounce package peppered gravy mix (makes 2 cups)"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat oven to 350F. Grease a 13x9 baking dish with non-stick cooking spray.", "In a large skillet, cook the sausage over medium heat until completely browned. Drain off the fat and set the sausage aside.", "Cut each biscuit into 4 pieces and spread over the bottom of the prepared pan in an even layer.", "Add the cooked sausage over the biscuit dough, then sprinkle the cheese over the sausage.", "In a large bowl, whisk together the eggs and milk; add salt and pepper to taste, then pour the mixture all over the casserole.", "Make the gravy according to the package instructions. Pour the prepared gravy over the whole casserole.", "Bake the casserole for 40-45 minutes until puffed up and golden brown on top."]'::jsonb, '["Kitchen Fun With My 3 Sons", "sausage", "casserole", "biscuits", "breakfast", "American"]'::jsonb, '["breakfast"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout (footer URL is blurry, appears to be kitchenfunwithmy3sons.com). Author: Jill. Course: Breakfast. Cuisine: American.', NULL),
('Broccoli-Rice Casserole', NULL, NULL, NULL, 45, '["butter", "1/2 cup chopped onion", "1 cup rice", "1 cup water", "20 oz frozen broccoli", "8 oz Cheez Whiz", "1 can mushroom soup"]'::jsonb, '["Saute onion in butter. Add 1 cup rice to pan; cook on low.", "Add water and frozen broccoli to the onions; bring to boil.", "Empty into 3 qt. baking dish. [Top] with 8 oz Cheez Whiz with can mushroom soup. Bake 350° 45 min."]'::jsonb, '["broccoli", "rice", "side", "casserole"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten in a spiral notebook (Evernote printout dated 2/3/2021), below Twice Baked Potato Casserole. Directions are written as bracketed notes next to the ingredients (''Butter / 1/2 cup chopped onion } saute''; ''1 cup rice } add to pan, cook on low''; ''1 cup water / 20 oz frozen broccoli } add to onions, bring to boil''), then ''Empty into 3 qt. baking dish. 8 oz cheez whiz with can mushroom soup. Bake 350° 45 min.'' The steps above are arranged from those notes.

Couldn''t read for sure: bake time ''45 min'' (could be ''15 min''); ''cook on low'' (handwriting); ''Casserole'' in title partly under glare', NULL),
('Brown Sugar Balsamic-Glazed Pork Chop with Garlicky Carrots and Green Beans', NULL, 2, NULL, 30, '["3 thyme sprigs", "6 oz carrot", "8 oz green beans", "1/2 oz balsamic vinegar", "1/2 tsp garlic salt", ".46 oz brown sugar", "1 fl oz garlic aioli", ".3 oz butter", "12 oz boneless pork chops", "olive oil", "salt", "pepper"]'::jsonb, '["Prepare the Ingredients: All cook times are approximate based on testing. If using any fresh produce, thoroughly rinse and pat dry. Peel, trim, and cut carrot into 1/2\" slices on an angle. Trim ends off green beans, if necessary. Stem and mince thyme. Pat pork chops dry and season both sides with 1/4 tsp. salt, a pinch of pepper, and thyme.", "Cook the Vegetables: Place a large non-stick pan over medium-high heat and add 1 tsp. olive oil. Add carrots to hot pan and stir occasionally, 2 minutes. Add green beans and stir occasionally, 1 minute. Add 1/4 cup water and a pinch of pepper. Cover and cook until tender, 6-8 minutes. If vegetables need more time, add 2 Tbsp. water, cover, and stir occasionally, 1-3 minutes. Uncover and season with garlic salt. Remove from burner. While vegetables cook, continue recipe.", "Cook the Pork Chops: Place a medium non-stick pan over medium-high heat and add 2 tsp. olive oil. Add pork chops to hot pan and cook until golden brown and chops reach a minimum internal temperature of 145 degrees, 3-5 minutes per side. Pork thickness can vary; if you receive a thinner chop, we recommend checking for doneness sooner. Remove from burner. Transfer chops to a plate. Rest, 3 minutes. Reserve pan; no need to wipe clean.", "Make the Glaze: Return pan used to cook pork chops to medium heat and add 2 Tbsp. water. Add vinegar and brown sugar to hot pan. Bring to a simmer. Once simmering, stir occasionally until thickened, 2-3 minutes. Remove from burner. Stir in butter until melted and combined.", "Make Aioli and Finish Dish: In a mixing bowl, combine garlic aioli and 2 tsp. water. Plate dish as pictured on front of card, topping pork chop with glaze and garnishing vegetables with aioli. Bon appétit!"]'::jsonb, '["Home Chef", "pork", "pork chops", "meal kit"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Home Chef meal kit card. Prep & Cook Time 20-30 min; cook within 6 days; difficulty intermediate; not spicy. Customize It Options (default 12 oz boneless pork chops used above): 16 oz USDA Choice New York strip steak; 12 oz antibiotic-free boneless skinless chicken breasts; 12 oz sirloin steaks; 12 oz filets mignon. Customize It Instructions: If using chicken breasts, follow same instructions as pork chops in Steps 1 and 3, cooking until chicken reaches minimum internal temperature, 5-7 minutes per side. If using filets mignon, sirloin steaks, or NY strip steak, follow same instructions as pork chops in Steps 1 and 3, cooking until steaks reach desired doneness, or 4-6 minutes per side for medium/medium-well. Rest, 3 minutes. Steak thickness can vary; if you receive a thinner steak, we recommend checking for doneness sooner. Minimum internal temperatures: 145° steak, pork, lamb, seafood; 160° ground beef, ground pork; 165° chicken, ground turkey. Rest steak or pork after cooking, 3 minutes. Step 3 text is partly washed out by glare in the photo; the missing words were reconstructed from the card''s pattern.

Couldn''t read for sure: Step 3 heading ''Cook the Pork Chops'' (partly washed out); Step 3 ''Place a medium non-stick pan ... add 2 tsp. olive oil'' (''Place a medium'' and ''tsp. olive oil'' washed out); Step 3 ''Add pork chops to hot pan ... and chops reach a minimum internal temperature ... per side'' (several words washed out); Step 1 carrot ''1/2" slices'' (fraction small)', 'https://www.homechef.com/19024'),
('Cabbage Pockets', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["2 lbs hamburger", "1 1/2 onions, diced", "2 teas caraway seeds", "salt", "pepper", "cabbage"]'::jsonb, '["Brown hamburger with 1 1/2 onions, diced. Season with 2 teas caraway seeds, salt & pepper and add cabbage."]'::jsonb, '["beef", "cabbage", "German", "hand pies", "family recipe"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten in a spiral recipe notebook. Ingredient list only; the single step is inferred from ''onions diced, brown'' on the page. Written directly below ''Mom''s bread'', so the pockets are probably made with that bread dough (bierock/runza style). Amount of cabbage not given.', NULL),
('Cabbage Pockets (enchilada page)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 head of cabbage", "1 lb. hamburger", "1 onion", "1 teaspoon caraway seed", "salt & pepper to taste", "1 egg", "4 T water", "1 teas. oil"]'::jsonb, '["Brush dough with 1 egg beaten & 4 T water, 1 teas. oil before baking."]'::jsonb, '["beef", "cabbage", "German", "hand pies"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe card taped in a notebook (Evernote printout dated 2/3/2021), below Gourmet Enchiladas. Short version: the dough and filling directions are not written here (a fuller Cabbage Pockets recipe exists elsewhere). Only the egg-wash instruction is written.

Couldn''t read for sure: title ''Cabbage'' partly under glare; ''cabbage'' and ''hamburger'' line ends under glare', NULL),
('Cajun Dirty Rice Casserole', 'Cajun Dirty Rice Casserole - dirty rice loaded with chicken, smoked sausage, and parmesan cheese. SO good and SUPER easy to make! Zatarain''s Dirty Rice, sour cream, cream of chicken soup, parmesan cheese, cooked chicken, smoked sausage, and french fried onions. Can make in advance and refrigerate or freeze for later. A great dish for your Mardi Gras parties! #cajun #mardigras #casserole #rice #freezermeal #chicken #smokedsausage', 6, 25, 30, '["1 (8-oz) box Zatarain''s Dirty Rice", "1 lb smoked sausage, chopped", "2 cups chopped cooked chicken", "1 (10.5-oz) can cream of chicken soup, undiluted", "1 cup sour cream", "1 cup shredded parmesan cheese", "1 (2.8-oz) can French fried onions", "cooking spray"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat oven to 350°F. Lightly spray a 9x13-inch baking dish with cooking spray.", "In a large skillet, cook smoked sausage until starting to brown. Add dirty rice mix and water called for on the package. Prepare dirty rice according to package directions.", "Remove dirty rice and sausage from heat. Stir in cooked chicken, cream of chicken soup, sour cream, and parmesan cheese.", "Spread rice mixture into prepared baking dish. Top casserole with onions.", "Bake uncovered for 30 minutes, until bubbly."]'::jsonb, '["Plain Chicken", "chicken", "sausage", "Cajun", "casserole", "rice", "freezer meal"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from Plain Chicken (Author: Plain Chicken), page 1 of 2; page 2 not in the photos, but the recipe appears complete on page 1. Total time 55 mins. Notes: Can make in advance and refrigerate or freeze for later. To bake after freezing, thaw completely and bake as directed above. Can use turkey smoked sausage. Footer URL blurry (plainchicken.com wprm_print).', NULL),
('Cajun-Spiced Chicken & Maple Mustard with Creamy Vegetable Farro', 'To temper the piquant Cajun-style spices on our seared chicken, we''re creating a sweet and savory topping of maple syrup and creamy mustard sauce. A toothsome bed of farro and veggies mixed with sour cream provides welcome heartiness to the dish.', 4, NULL, 40, '["4 boneless, skinless chicken breasts", "1 cup semi-pearled farro", "2 zucchini", "1 Tbsp apple cider vinegar", "1 Tbsp hot sauce", "2 Tbsps maple syrup", "2 Tbsps ghee", "1/2 lb sweet peppers", "2 cloves garlic", "2 scallions", "1 Tbsp creamy mustard sauce", "1/4 cup sour cream", "1 Tbsp Cajun spice blend (smoked paprika, ground yellow mustard, onion powder, garlic powder, whole dried oregano, whole dried thyme & cayenne pepper)"]'::jsonb, '["Cook the farro: Remove the ghee from the refrigerator to bring to room temperature. Fill a medium pot 3/4 of the way up with salted water; cover and heat to boiling on high. Once boiling, add the farro. Cook, uncovered, 18 to 20 minutes, or until tender. Turn off the heat. Drain thoroughly and return to the pot.", "Cook the chicken: Meanwhile, pat the chicken dry with paper towels. Season on both sides with salt, pepper, and enough of the spice blend to coat (you may have extra). In a large pan (nonstick, if you have one), heat the ghee on medium-high until melted. Add the seasoned chicken. Cook 6 to 7 minutes per side, or until browned and cooked through. Leaving any browned bits (or fond) in the pan, transfer to a cutting board.", "Prepare the remaining ingredients & make the sauce: Meanwhile, wash and dry the fresh produce. Cut off and discard the stems of the peppers; remove the cores. Halve lengthwise, then thinly slice crosswise. Thinly slice the scallions, separating the white bottoms and hollow green tops. Halve the zucchini lengthwise, then cut crosswise into 1/2-inch pieces. Peel and roughly chop 2 cloves of garlic. Combine in a bowl; add the sliced white bottoms of the scallions. In a separate bowl, whisk together the maple syrup and creamy mustard sauce.", "Cook the vegetables: In the pan of reserved fond, heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil on medium-high until hot. Add the sliced peppers; season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, 2 to 3 minutes, or until slightly softened. Add the prepared zucchini mixture (if the pan seems dry, add a drizzle of olive oil); season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, 3 to 4 minutes, or until lightly browned. Turn off the heat. Taste, then season with salt and pepper if desired.", "Finish & serve your dish: To the pot of cooked farro, add the cooked vegetables, vinegar, sour cream, 2 tablespoons of olive oil, and as much of the hot sauce as you''d like, depending on how spicy you''d like the dish to be. Stir to thoroughly combine. Taste, then season with salt and pepper if desired. Slice the cooked chicken crosswise. Serve the sliced chicken over the finished farro. Top the chicken with the sauce. Garnish with the sliced green tops of the scallions. Enjoy!"]'::jsonb, '["Blue Apron", "chicken", "Cajun", "farro", "grain bowl"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Blue Apron recipe card. Steps also use about 3 tablespoons olive oil, salt and pepper. Wine pairing: Plush & Fruity.', NULL),
('Calico Beans', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 lb beef", "1/4 bacon", "1/2 c onion", "1 c pork beans", "1 c. kidney beans", "1 c. butter & northern beans", "1/2 c ketchup", "1/2 c. brown sugar", "1 tsp. mustard", "1 tbls. vinegar", "4 dashes garlic powder"]'::jsonb, '["Brown beef, bacon and onion together.", "Put in crock pot."]'::jsonb, '["beans", "ground beef", "slow cooker", "side"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten notebook page, faded. Beef, bacon and onion are bracketed with "brown together". The title is also visible upside-down at the top of photo d8cf8801.

Couldn''t read for sure: title is faded; reads like ''Caian/Calico Beans''; 1/4 bacon (probably 1/4 lb); 1 c pork beans (pork & beans)', NULL),
('Camp Fire Bundle', NULL, NULL, NULL, 90, '["2 cups Olive Garden dressing", "1 can corn", "1 can green beans", "half onion, chopped", "2 spoonfuls minced garlic", "1 stick of butter", "3 TBSP Kicken Chicken seasoning", "1 bag of small potatoes, diced in half", "2 chicken breasts, diced", "2 links of smoked sausage", "salt & pepper", "1 green pepper", "1 sweet potato, diced"]'::jsonb, '["Put in a pan. Put in oven or grill at 375° for 1 hr & 30 min. Stir and check potatoes to see if it is done."]'::jsonb, '["chicken", "sausage", "potatoes", "grill", "camping", "one pan"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe on lined paper. Written as ''3 tbls. Kicken Chicken'' (probably Kick''n Chicken seasoning), ''2 spoon full minced garlic'', ''2 links of smoked sausage links''.

Couldn''t read for sure: ''Kicken Chicken'' (written; likely Kick''n Chicken seasoning); oven/grill temperature: best reading ''375°''', NULL),
('Central Freight Soup', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 lb. hamburger meat - browned", "3 cans minestrone soup", "2 cans Ranch Style beans", "1 can Rotel", "1 can drained corn - I use frozen", "1 can stewed tomatoes"]'::jsonb, '["Combine the browned hamburger meat with the soups, beans, Rotel, corn and stewed tomatoes and cook. The longer it cooks - the better. Can be put in crock-pot."]'::jsonb, '["soup", "beef", "ground beef", "slow cooker"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe card ("Recipe for" card). Written directions only say: "The longer it cooks - the better. Can be put in crock-pot." Handwritten next to the title: "Great!" (underlined).

Couldn''t read for sure: "Ranch Style" beans ("Style" partly under glare); "drained corn" ("corn" under glare); title word "Freight"', NULL),
('Cheesy Angel Chicken and Rice Casserole', NULL, 8, 10, 25, '["3 cups cooked chicken, diced or shredded", "3 cups cooked rice", "1/2 cup butter, room temperature and cubed", "8 ounces cream cheese, room temperature and cubed", "10.5 ounces cream of chicken soup", "3 cloves garlic, minced", "0.7 ounce Italian dressing mix (I used Good Seasons)", "1 cup chicken stock", "2 cups shredded Colby Jack cheese, divided use", "salt and pepper to taste", "fresh parsley for garnish", "cooking spray"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat oven to 350 degrees F, and generously spray a 9x13\" casserole dish with cooking spray.", "In a microwave-safe bowl, soften the cream cheese and butter in the microwave for 20-30 seconds. Whisk until [text hidden by a comment box on the printout] rice, butter and cream cheese mixture, cream of chicken soup, garlic, Italian dressing mix, chicken stock, half of the shredded cheese, and salt and pepper. Mix well until evenly combined.", "Transfer the chicken and rice mixture into the prepared casserole dish.", "Top with the remaining shredded cheese.", "Cover the dish with foil, and bake in the preheated oven for 20-25 minutes, until the cheese is melted and the casserole is bubbling.", "Remove from oven, and allow the casserole to cool for 5 minutes. Remove foil.", "Garnish with fresh parsley, and enjoy."]'::jsonb, '["Homemade Cooking", "Facebook", "chicken", "rice", "casserole", "cheesy"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Facebook post by Homemade Cooking, posted under the heading "Angel Chicken Rice" (pages 1 and 2 of 4 printed). Prep Time: 10 minutes | Cooking Time: 25 minutes | Total Time: 35 minutes | Kcal: 548 kcal | Servings: 8. A Facebook comment box covers part of step 2 on the printout: after "Whisk until" some text is hidden, picking up again with "rice, butter and cream cheese mixture..." (it presumably combines the chicken and rice with the other ingredients). Pages 3-4 (comments) not in the photos.

Couldn''t read for sure: step 2: text after ''Whisk until'' is hidden by a comment box; only the visible text is transcribed; step 1: ''generously'' is washed out (best reading)', NULL),
('Cheesy Cream Cheese Hamburger Pasta Casserole', 'Cheesy Cream Cheese Hamburger Pasta Casserole is a delicious comfort food casserole. My family has been making this ooey gooey cheesy casserole for years.', NULL, 20, 30, '["1 lb ground beef", "1/2 small green pepper, diced", "1/2 small red pepper, diced", "1/2 medium onion, chopped", "2 medium garlic cloves, minced", "8 oz cream cheese, at room temp or microwave for a minute to soften", "1 cup sour cream", "1 cup Parmesan cheese", "1 cup cheddar cheese or mozzarella", "12 oz pasta of your choice cooked al dente", "3 cups pasta sauce of your choice", "salt and pepper to taste"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat your oven to 350°.", "In a large skillet over medium-high heat, saute the hamburger and cook until almost cooked through.", "Add the onion, peppers, garlic salt and pepper ad cook until the veggies are cooked through.", "In a medium saucepan boil water for pasta . Add pasta and cook until pasta is just al dente. Do not over cook as the pasta will continue to cook in the oven. Drain.", "Add the cream cheese. If you didn''t leave it out at room temperature you can microwave it for a minute in the microwave. Add sour cream and Parmesan cheese.", "In a sprayed 9\"x 13\" casserole dish, add the pasta mixture. Then add the hamburger mixture and sauce on top and stir until everything is loosely combined.,", "Top with the shredded cheddar or mozzarella.", "Bake at 350° for 25-30 minutes, or until the casserole is heated through. Serve immediately."]'::jsonb, '["Maria''s Mixing Bowl", "beef", "pasta", "casserole", "Italian", "ground beef"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from Maria''s Mixing Bowl (footer URL looks like mariasmixingbowl.com/wprm_print/28792 but is blurry). Author: Rob. Course: Dinner. Cuisine printed as "Italain". Total time 50 minutes. No servings printed.', NULL),
('Cheesy Potato Casserole', 'Casserole may be prepared and baked as directed on the same day.', 8, NULL, NULL, '["3 pounds baking potatoes, peeled and quartered", "1/2 cup butter or margarine", "2 (3-ounce) packages cream cheese, softened", "1 cup (4 ounces) shredded Cheddar cheese, divided", "3/4 cup finely chopped green bell pepper", "3/4 cup finely chopped green onions", "1 (2-ounce) jar diced pimiento, drained", "1/2 cup grated Parmesan cheese", "1/2 cup milk", "1 teaspoon salt"]'::jsonb, '["Cook: Cook baking potato in boiling water to cover 15 minutes or until tender; drain and mash.", "Add: Add butter and cream cheese to mashed potatoes; beat at medium speed with an electric mixer until smooth. Stir in 1/2 cup Cheddar cheese, chopped bell pepper, and next 5 ingredients. Spoon into a lightly greased 11- x 7-inch baking dish.", "Cover: Cover casserole, and chill overnight. Let stand at room temperature 30 minutes before baking.", "Bake: Bake, uncovered, at 325° for 35 to 40 minutes or until thoroughly heated. Sprinkle with remaining 1/2 cup Cheddar cheese, and bake 5 more minutes."]'::jsonb, '["potatoes", "casserole", "side", "make-ahead"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Magazine clipping taped in a recipe notebook (Evernote printout, 2/4/2021). Kitchen Express: Substitute 1 (22-ounce) package frozen mashed potatoes for baking potatoes. Prepare according to package directions. (The Kitchen Express tip is circled.)

Couldn''t read for sure: ''1/2 cup milk'' amount smudged; ''1 teaspoon salt'' amount smudged; bake temperature ''325°'' slightly smudged', NULL),
('Cheesy Potato Kielbasa Soup', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 pound kielbasa, cut into 1/2 inch pieces", "2 garlic cloves, minced", "1/2 cup finely diced yellow onion", "1/2 cup peeled and finely diced (2 large carrots)", "1/2 cup finely sliced celery (2-3 stalks)", "4 cups chicken stock", "1 1/2 pounds potato, cut into cubes", "2 cups milk", "2 cups shredded cheddar cheese", "1/2 cup shredded parmesan cheese", "1/2 teaspoon kosher salt", "1/4 teaspoon black pepper", "1/4 cup chopped parsley"]'::jsonb, '["Add olive oil to a Dutch oven or soup pot and heat over medium-high heat. Add the sausage and cook for 5-6 minutes, stirring frequently. Remove the sausage using a slotted spoon.", "Add garlic, onions, carrots, and celery and sauté for 2 minutes.", "Add the chicken stock and potatoes. Bring to boil and then reduce heat. Cover and cook for 15 minutes, or until the potatoes are tender.", "Add the cooked sausage, milk, cheddar cheese, parmesan cheese, salt, and pepper. Stir and cook on low heat 5-10 minutes longer, until the cheese has melted.", "Stir in parsley before serving."]'::jsonb, '["Honey and Birch", "soup", "sausage", "kielbasa", "potato", "cheese"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Printout page 11/18 only (header: Cheesy Potato Kielbasa Soup » The Thirsty Feast, 9/16/21). The first page (title, description, servings, times, and the start of the ingredient list, which likely includes the olive oil used in step 1) is not in the photos.

A page of this recipe was missing from the photos.', 'https://www.honeyandbirch.com/potato-kielbasa-soup/'),
('Cheesy Smoked Sausage Skillet', 'Cheesy Smoked Sausage Skillet - smoked sausage, tomato sauce, chicken broth, heavy cream, refrigerated cheese tortellini, and parmesan. Everything cooks in the same pan! Even the pasta!! SO easy and super delicious! We ate this 2 nights in a row.', 4, 5, 15, '["1 lb smoked sausage, sliced into 1/4-inch slices", "1 Tbsp olive oil", "3 cloves garlic, minced", "1 (8-oz) can tomato sauce", "1 Tbsp tomato paste", "1 Tbsp Italian seasoning", "1 cup chicken broth", "1/2 cup heavy cream", "1 (9-oz) package refrigerated cheese tortellini", "1/4 cup parmesan cheese"]'::jsonb, '["In a 12-inch skillet, brown sausage in olive oil.", "Add garlic and cook for 30 seconds. Stir in remaining ingredients.", "Bring to a boil then cover and simmer on low for 12-15 minutes.", "Serve with additional parmesan cheese, if desired."]'::jsonb, '["Plain Chicken", "sausage", "pasta", "tortellini", "skillet", "one pan"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'From Plain Chicken (web printout, page 1 of 2, printed 10/27/23). Author: Plain Chicken. Yield: 4 people. Total time 20 mins. Recipe notes: Can use turkey smoked sausage if you prefer. Page 2 not in the photos (the recipe is complete on page 1). The footer URL (plainchicken.com/cheesy-smoked-sausage-skillet/) is too blurry to use as sourceUrl.

Couldn''t read for sure: description ''tomato sauce'' and ''cheese tortellini, and parmesan'': partly faded/glare; ''1 (9-oz) package refrigerated cheese tortellini'' and ''1/4 cup parmesan cheese'': faded but readable', NULL),
('Chicken & Poblano Burrito Bowls with Marinated Tomatoes & Ancho Sour Cream', 'Our Mexican spice blend stars two ways in these burrito bowls: it''s cooked into our hearty base of rice and black beans, then used to spice a mix of tender chicken, poblano pepper, and onion served on top. A smoky sour cream topper lends even more bold flavor to the bowls.', 4, NULL, 30, '["1 1/8 lbs chopped chicken breast", "1 poblano pepper", "1/2 lb grape tomatoes", "1 clove garlic", "1 oz sliced pickled jalapeño pepper", "1 Tbsp ancho chile paste", "1 Tbsp Mexican spice blend (ancho chile powder, smoked paprika, garlic powder, ground cumin & dried Mexican oregano)", "1 15.5-oz can black beans", "1 cup jasmine rice", "1 red onion", "1 lime", "1/4 cup sour cream", "2 Tbsps grated cotija cheese", "olive oil", "salt", "pepper"]'::jsonb, '["Cook the rice & beans: Drain and rinse the beans. In a medium pot, combine the rice, drained beans, half the spice blend, a big pinch of salt, and 2 cups of water; stir to combine. Heat to boiling on high. Once boiling, reduce the heat to low. Cover and cook, without stirring, 16 to 18 minutes, or until the water has been absorbed and the rice is tender. Turn off the heat and fluff with a fork. Add a drizzle of olive oil and stir to combine.", "Prepare the remaining ingredients & make the salsa: Meanwhile, wash and dry the fresh produce. Halve the tomatoes. Halve the lime crosswise. Peel 1 clove of garlic; using a zester, finely grate into a paste (or use the small side of a box grater). Halve, peel, and thinly slice the onion. Cut off and discard the stem of the poblano pepper. Halve the pepper lengthwise; remove the ribs and seeds, then thinly slice crosswise. Combine in a large bowl. Roughly chop the jalapeño pepper. Thoroughly wash your hands immediately after handling the peppers. In a bowl, combine the halved tomatoes, the juice of 1 lime half, as much of the garlic paste as you''d like, a drizzle of olive oil, and as much of the chopped jalapeño pepper as you''d like, depending on how spicy you''d like the dish to be. Season with salt and pepper; stir to combine.", "Cook the chicken & vegetables: Pat the chicken dry with paper towels. Transfer to the bowl of prepared onion and poblano pepper. Season with salt, pepper, and the remaining spice blend; toss to coat. In a large pan (nonstick, if you have one), heat a drizzle of olive oil on medium-high until hot. Add the seasoned chicken and vegetables in an even layer. Cook, without stirring, 3 to 4 minutes, or until lightly browned. Continue to cook, stirring occasionally, 4 to 5 minutes, or until browned and the chicken is cooked through. Turn off the heat.", "Make the ancho sour cream & serve your dish: Meanwhile, in a bowl, whisk together the chile paste, sour cream, and the juice of the remaining lime half. Taste, then season with salt and pepper if desired. Serve the cooked rice and beans topped with the cooked chicken and vegetables, salsa (including any liquid), ancho sour cream, and cheese. Enjoy!"]'::jsonb, '["Blue Apron", "chicken", "Mexican", "burrito bowl", "rice", "WW"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Blue Apron recipe card, WW Approved. Time: 20-30 mins. 12 green SmartPoints, 8 blue SmartPoints, 8 purple SmartPoints. Wine pairing: Crisp & Minerally.

Couldn''t read for sure: chicken breast ''1 1/8 lbs'' (fraction small; could be 1 1/4)', NULL),
('Chicken & Spinach Lumaca Rigata Pasta with Ricotta & Garlic Bread', 'In this vibrant pasta, we''re bringing together seared chicken and spinach with a bold sauce, which gets deliciously varied flavors and textures from worcestershire sauce, Niçoise olives, and briny capers. Two finishing touches—a dollop of creamy ricotta and a side of garlic bread—tie all the rich flavors together.', 4, NULL, 35, '["1 3/8 lbs chopped chicken breast", "1 small baguette", "5 oz baby spinach", "1 Tbsp capers", "1 oz pitted Niçoise olives", "4 Tbsps crème fraîche", "1 tsp whole dried oregano", "3/4 lb lumaca rigata pasta", "1 14-oz can whole peeled tomatoes", "2 cloves garlic", "2 Tbsps vegetarian worcestershire sauce", "1/2 cup part-skim ricotta cheese", "1/4 cup grated parmesan cheese", "1/4 tsp crushed red pepper flakes"]'::jsonb, '["Prepare the ingredients & season the ricotta: Place an oven rack in the center of the oven, then preheat to 450°F. Fill a large pot 3/4 of the way up with salted water; cover and heat to boiling on high. Wash and dry the fresh produce. Peel 2 cloves of garlic; keeping one clove whole, roughly chop the remaining clove. Roughly chop the olives and capers. Combine the chopped garlic, chopped olives, and chopped capers in a bowl. Place the tomatoes in a bowl; gently break apart with your hands. Halve the baguette. In a separate bowl, combine the ricotta, half the parmesan, and a drizzle of olive oil. Season with salt and pepper; stir to combine.", "Cook the chicken: Pat the chicken dry with paper towels; season with salt, pepper, and the oregano. In a large pan (nonstick, if you have one), heat a drizzle of olive oil on medium-high until hot. Add the seasoned chicken in an even layer. Cook, without stirring, 3 to 4 minutes, or until lightly browned. Continue to cook, stirring occasionally, 3 to 4 minutes, or until browned and cooked through. Leaving any browned bits (or fond) in the pan, transfer to a plate. Cover with foil to keep warm.", "Make the garlic bread: Meanwhile, place the halved baguette on a sheet pan, cut side up. Drizzle with olive oil; season with salt and pepper. Bake 6 to 8 minutes, or until lightly browned. Transfer to a cutting board. Carefully rub the cut sides with the whole garlic clove, then discard the clove. Halve crosswise.", "Make the sauce: Heat the pan of reserved fond on medium-high until hot (if the pan seems dry, add a drizzle of olive oil). Add the chopped olive mixture; season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, 1 to 2 minutes, or until slightly softened. Add the crushed tomatoes (carefully, as the liquid may splatter) and as much of the red pepper flakes as you''d like, depending on how spicy you''d like the dish to be; season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, 3 to 4 minutes, or until slightly thickened. Add the worcestershire sauce. Cook, stirring frequently, 30 seconds to 1 minute, or until combined. Turn off the heat. Taste, then season with salt and pepper if desired.", "Cook the pasta: Meanwhile, add the pasta to the pot of boiling water. Cook, stirring occasionally, 5 to 7 minutes, or until al dente (still slightly firm to the bite). Turn off the heat. Reserving 1 cup of the pasta cooking water, drain thoroughly and return to the pot.", "Finish the pasta & serve your dish: To the pot of cooked pasta, add the spinach, cooked chicken, sauce, and half the reserved pasta cooking water. Cook on medium-high, stirring constantly, 1 to 2 minutes, or until the pasta is coated (if necessary, gradually add the remaining cooking water to ensure the pasta is thoroughly coated). Turn off the heat. Stir in the crème fraîche. Taste, then season with salt and pepper if desired. Serve the finished pasta topped with the seasoned ricotta and remaining parmesan. Serve the garlic bread on the side. Enjoy!"]'::jsonb, '["Blue Apron", "chicken", "pasta", "Italian"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Blue Apron recipe card. Wine match: Light & Bright. Steps also use olive oil, salt and pepper (not in the printed ingredient list).

Couldn''t read for sure: chicken amount: small fraction read as ''1 3/8 lbs'' (could be 1 1/8 lbs)', NULL),
('Chicken Alfredo Pizza', 'A super easy, make at home Chicken Alfredo Pizza', 8, 15, 15, '["1 can pizza dough", "1/2 cup Alfredo sauce", "2 cups mozzarella cheese (divided)", "1/3 cup green onions (chopped)", "3/4 cup bacon (cooked and crumbled)", "1 1/2 cup chicken (cooked and shredded)", "1 teas. garlic salt", "1 teas. Italian seasoning", "1/2 c. parmesan cheese"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat oven to 400 degrees F. (Time can vary depending on your crust. For best result bake according to the pizza dough instructions). Prepare a baking sheet with non-stick cooking spray. Roll our pizza dough and place on a prepared baking sheet.", "Spoon and spread Alfredo sauce onto your pizza dough and sprinkle with 1 1/2 cup mozzarella cheese. Top with green onions, bacon, and chicken. Finish the pizza off with the remaining cheese.", "Place pizza in preheated oven on a pizza pan and cook for 12-15 minutes or until crust is fully cooked and cheese is melted."]'::jsonb, '["The Diary of a Real Housewife", "chicken", "pizza", "bacon", "American"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Printout from The Diary of a Real Housewife (Jennie Duncan), page 1 of 2. Servings: 8 slices, 266 kcal per slice. Handwritten next to the ingredients: "sprinkle on alfredo: 1 teas. garlic salt, 1 teas. Italian seasoning, 1/2 c. parmesan cheese" (added to ingredients).', 'https://www.thediaryofarealhousewife.com/wprm_print/recipe/20330'),
('Chicken and Dumplings', 'This is comfort food like no one''s business.', 8, 15, 30, '["2 tbsp. butter", "2 tbsp. olive oil", "1/2 c. all-purpose flour", "1 whole chicken, cut into pieces", "salt and pepper", "1/2 c. finely diced carrots", "1/2 c. finely diced celery", "1 whole medium onion, finely diced", "1/2 tsp. ground thyme", "1/4 tsp. turmeric", "6 c. low-sodium chicken broth", "1/2 c. apple cider", "1/2 c. heavy cream", "For the dumplings: 1 1/2 c. all-purpose flour", "1/2 c. yellow cornmeal", "1 tbsp. (heaping) baking powder", "1 tsp. kosher salt", "1 1/2 c. half-and-half", "2 tbsp. minced fresh parsley (optional)", "salt as needed"]'::jsonb, '["Sprinkle chicken pieces with salt and pepper, then dredge both sides in flour.", "Melt butter in a pot over medium-high heat. In two batches, brown chicken on both sides and remove to a clean plate.", "In the same pot, add diced onion, carrots, and celery. Stir and cook for 3 to 4 minutes over medium-low heat. Stir in ground thyme and turmeric, then pour in chicken broth and apple cider. Stir to combine, then add browned chicken. Cover pot and simmer for 20 minutes.", "While chicken is simmering, make the dough for the dumplings: sift together all dry ingredients, then add half-and-half, stirring gently to combine. Set aside.", "Remove chicken from pot and set aside on a plate. Use two forks to remove chicken from the bone. Shred, then add chicken to the pot. Pour heavy cream into the pot and stir to combine.", "Drop tablespoons of dumpling dough into the simmering pot. Add minced parsley if using. Cover pot halfway and continue to simmer for 15 minutes. Check seasonings; add salt if needed. Allow to sit for 10 minutes before serving. *Adapted from Gourmet Magazine"]'::jsonb, '["The Pioneer Woman", "chicken", "dumplings", "soup", "comfort food", "Southern"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from The Pioneer Woman (2 pages), by Ree Drummond, published Dec 14, 2010. Total time 45 mins. Adapted from Gourmet Magazine.', 'https://www.thepioneerwoman.com/food-cooking/recipes/a9790/chicken-and-dumplings/'),
('Chicken and Dumplings (biscuit version)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["32 oz chicken broth", "1 can of cream of chicken soup", "1 traditional rotisserie chicken", "1 can of 8 biscuits (the fluffy kind work best)", "pepper", "flour"]'::jsonb, '["Pour chicken broth and cream of chicken into a large pot, stir well, and bring to a simmer/boil.", "While that is warming up, cut biscuits into fours and roll in flour. Shred the chicken before hand.", "Once it comes to a boil put chicken and the biscuits into the pot, stir well, and put a layer on pepper over the pot and stir again.", "Cook for 10-13 minutes at a simmer. (Whatever the biscuits say to cook for is what I go by). Then reduce heat and let cool for at least 5-7 minutes."]'::jsonb, '["chicken", "dumplings", "soup", "comfort food", "biscuits"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Screenshot of a phone note titled "Chicken and Dumplings Recipe" (version made with canned biscuits). Glare covers parts of the ingredient list and step 1; obscured words were filled in from context.

Couldn''t read for sure: "32oz chicken broth" - "chicken" under glare; "1 can of cream of chicken soup" - "of cream" under glare; "1 traditional rotisserie chicken" - "rotisserie" under glare; step 1 "cream of chicken into a large pot" and "bring to a simmer/boil" partly under glare; step 2 "While that is warming up" and "into fours and roll in flour" partly under glare; step 3 "comes to a boil" partly under glare', NULL),
('Chicken Bacon Gnocchi Soup', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["6 strips bacon, cut into small pieces", "1/2 medium onion, chopped", "2 cloves garlic, minced", "4 cups chicken broth", "1 cup heavy whipping cream", "Italian seasoning, to taste", "1 pound potato gnocchi, uncooked", "2 cups rotisserie chicken, cooked and shredded", "2 cups fresh baby spinach, packed", "salt, to taste", "pepper, to taste"]'::jsonb, '["In a soup pot over medium-high heat, cook the bacon until crispy, about 10 minutes.", "Transfer the cooked bacon to a paper-towel-lined plate and leave about 2 tablespoons of the bacon fat in the pot.", "Add the onion to the pot and saute until softened and lightly browned, about 4-5 minutes.", "Stir the garlic into the onions and cook until fragrant, about 1 minute.", "Add the chicken broth, the cream, the Italian seasoning, the gnocchi, and most of the bacon (reserving the rest for garnish) to the pot and stir and scrape up any browned bits from the bottom of the pot.", "Increase the heat to high and bring the soup to a boil."]'::jsonb, '["chicken", "bacon", "gnocchi", "soup", "Italian"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout, page 3 of 11 (printed 8/17/24), which has no title; the title "Chicken Bacon Gnocchi Soup" comes from the page URL (https://belaya.info/chicken-bacon-gnocchi-soup.html/..., rest of URL too small to read). Instructions are printed before the ingredients. The printed instructions end at bringing the soup to a boil and never mention adding the chicken or spinach (presumably stir them in and simmer until the gnocchi are cooked and the spinach wilts).', NULL),
('Chicken Bacon Ranch Casserole', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1/2 lb. bacon, cooked and chopped", "1 lb. boneless, skinless chicken breasts, diced", "1 tbsp. olive oil", "1 packet dry Ranch dressing mix", "8 oz. pasta (I used Shells)", "1 cup Mozzarella cheese, shredded", "1/2 cup Cheddar cheese, shredded", "Salt/Pepper to taste", "1 jar Alfredo sauce (14.5 oz)"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat oven to 375 and grease a 9 x 9 baking dish.", "Heat a large skillet over medium heat. Cook bacon until brown and crispy, about 7 minutes.", "Drain fat and place bacon on a paper towel to absorb the grease.", "In a gallon size Ziploc bag, add in the olive oil, diced chicken (raw at this point), and Ranch mix.", "Shake around in bag until chicken is evenly coated.", "Add chicken to skillet and cook until no longer pink. Set aside.", "In a pot of boiling water, cook pasta until al dente.", "Drain water and add pasta to greased baking dish.", "Add cooked chicken and Alfredo sauce to the pasta.", "Sprinkle both cheeses, bacon, and salt/pepper to the top of the Alfredo and place pan in oven.", "Bake until bubbly and cheese is melted, about 15 minutes.", "Remove from oven and serve!! Enjoy!!"]'::jsonb, '["chicken", "bacon", "ranch", "casserole", "pasta"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'PrintFriendly web printout, pages 2 and 3 of 5 (pages 1, 4 and 5 not in the photos; ingredients start on page 2 and directions end on page 3). The title "Chicken Bacon Ranch Casserole" is handwritten at the top of page 2.

Couldn''t read for sure: step 2 "Cook bacon until" partly under glare; step 3 "to absorb the grease" partly under glare; step 4 "diced chicken" partly under glare', NULL),
('Chicken Con Queso', 'This Chicken Con Queso is loaded with taco-spiced chicken, white rice, queso, pico de gallo, salsa and so much more. It''s a Mexican food lover''s dream! Even better, our Chicken Con Queso recipe is virtually foolproof and ultra delicious—meaning you''ll be crowned queen or king of the kitchen in no time.', 4, 30, NULL, '["1 tablespoon olive oil", "3 large boneless skinless chicken breasts, cut into cubes", "1 packet Old El Paso Taco seasoning mix", "1 1/2 tablespoons water", "1 cup half and half or heavy cream", "2 cups instant white rice", "1 cup premade queso blanco (white queso from the store) (I really like Gordo''s brand), melted", "1 cup restaurant style salsa (thin salsa)", "1/4 cup chopped fresh cilantro, plus more for garnish", "1 small can Old El Paso Green Chiles", "1/2 cup pico de gallo or chopped tomatoes", "1 cup Mexican blend cheese"]'::jsonb, '["Heat the chicken cubes and olive oil in a large skillet over medium/high heat.", "Sprinkle chicken with the taco seasoning, turning to make sure both sides are coated. Add in the 1 1/2 tablespoons water to assist with coating all the chicken.", "Turn the chicken as you cook, about 6-8 minutes until the chicken is just cooked through.", "Place chicken on a plate and cover in foil to retain heat. Set aside.", "In the same skillet, add the heavy cream and white rice. Stir to combine. Add in the melted queso and salsa. Stir to fully combine. Bring to a boil, then cover and reduce heat to simmer for 5 minutes or until the rice is fully cooked and fluffy.", "Stir in cilantro, green chiles, and pico de gallo into the rice mixture. Add the chicken back to skillet and nestle into the rice.", "Cover with the 1 cup cheese. Place skillet under the broiler for approximately 3-5 minutes or until the cheese is fully melted on top.", "Garnish with more cilantro if desired."]'::jsonb, '["Old El Paso", "chicken", "Mexican", "rice", "skillet", "cheese"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Old El Paso web printout (oldelpaso.com/recipes/chicken-con-queso, printed 11/8/22; full URL in footer too blurry to copy). Prep 30 minutes, total 30 minutes. Expert tips: Pico de gallo is a fresh salsa typically made with chopped tomatoes, red onion, jalapeños, cilantro and lime juice. Look for it premade in the produce section of most grocery stores. Looking for a Mexican-blend cheese for this pollo con queso recipe? Consider using Old El Paso Shredded Mexican Style 4 Cheese Blend. Instant rice is rice that has been precooked and dried, allowing it to cook completely in less than half the time of regular rice (this tip is partly covered by cactus and star stickers on the page).

Couldn''t read for sure: instant rice tip words hidden under stickers: ''Instant'', ''that has'', ''precooked'', ''allowing'', ''completely'', ''than half'', ''regular rice'' (reconstructed)', NULL),
('Chicken Divan (Reynolds Wrap)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 60, '["4 chicken breasts", "2 cups rice", "2 can cream of chicken", "1 c. milk", "2 c. broccoli", "8 ice cubes", "cheddar cheese"]'::jsonb, '["Bake at 400° for 1 hr. Add cheddar cheese after meal is cooked."]'::jsonb, '["chicken", "broccoli", "rice", "foil pack", "Reynolds"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten in a spiral notebook below Crock Pot Chicken Teriyaki (Evernote printout page 2/3). As written: "cheddar cheese after meal cooked", "400° 1 hr." Presumably cooked in a Reynolds Wrap foil packet/oven bag.

Couldn''t read for sure: ''4 chicken breasts'' (''breasts'' hidden by glare); ''2 can cream of chicken'' (could be 1 can); ''2 cups rice'' (may mean instant rice)', NULL),
('Chicken Enchiladas (handwritten card)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 40, '["chicken breast", "chopped onion", "1 cup picante sauce", "1 can cream of chicken", "8 oz sour cream", "2 tbs chili powder", "Mexican shredded cheese", "tortillas"]'::jsonb, '["Boil chicken breast & chopped onion. Slice it.", "Sauce mix: 1 cup picante sauce, can of cream of chicken, 8 oz sour cream, 2 tbs chili powder. (Oven 350°.)", "Mix chicken, 3/4 of the sauce mix & Mexican shredded cheese - fill tortillas. Put seam down in dish.", "Spread remaining mix over tortillas. Sprinkle w/ cheese. Cover with foil, bake at 350° for 30-40 min."]'::jsonb, '["chicken", "Mexican", "enchiladas", "casserole", "handwritten"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe card with no title; the title "Chicken Enchiladas" was supplied, not written on the card. The top of the card may be cut off. The first line is partly covered by a white smudge/stain: it reads "boil ... chicken breast & chopped on..." (likely "onion"); a word between "boil" and "chicken" is obscured. No amounts given for chicken, onion, cheese or tortillas. "350°" is written beside the sauce mix heading.

Couldn''t read for sure: first line obscured: "boil [?] chicken breast & chopped on[ion]" - a word after "boil" and the end of "onion" are covered; "8 oz sour cream" (written "8oz", partly smudged); "2 tbs chili powder" (the 2 is smudged); "mexi. shredded cheese" read as Mexican shredded cheese; "Sprinkle w/cheese" (end of word smudged)', NULL),
('Chicken Taco Mexican Pinwheels', 'A creamy filling made with chicken taco flavors is spread over a soft flour tortilla and rolled up to make the most delicious Mexican pinwheels ever!', 80, 15, NULL, '["12 oz cream cheese, softened to room temp (my packages are 8oz, so I used a package and a half)", "1/2 cup sour cream", "2 cups shredded chicken **see recipe notes below", "1.5 Tbsp taco seasoning (choose your favorite)", "1 1/2 cups shredded Mexican cheese", "10 oz can of diced tomatoes with green chiles, very well drained", "1 1/2 tsp garlic, finely minced", "5 green onions, sliced thinly", "3/4 - 1 cup cilantro, chopped finely (adjust to your tastes)", "8 burrito sized flour tortillas", "fresh minced cilantro, for garnish optional"]'::jsonb, '["Combine all ingredients in a large mixing bowl, stirring until well combined.", "Lay flour tortilla down on work surface and spread about 1/4 cup (amount will vary from person to person) evenly over the tortilla, leaving a 1/2 - 1 inch border all around.", "Start at the bottom of the tortilla (closest to you), and roll up tightly towards the top, like a cigar. Place roll seam side down on prepared pan.", "Repeat with remaining tortillas and place in refrigerator for 30 minutes to several hours to chill and firm up.", "Use a sharp, serrated knife to slice roll into 1 inch pinwheels and serve."]'::jsonb, '["The Chunky Chef", "chicken", "Mexican", "appetizer", "snack"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'The Chunky Chef printout, page 1 of 2 (page 2 not in the photos). Servings: 80 pinwheels (approximately 8 per person). Total time 15 mins; 40 kcal. Recipe notes: 1. Recipe preparation time does not count chilling time, as that will vary from person to person. 2. If you have leftover filling, it can be frozen (in a sealed bag or airtight container) for up to 2 months. 3. SHREDDED CHICKEN RECOMMENDATIONS: Tequila Lime Chicken - cook as directed, then shred (this gives the best flavor); Leftover cooked chicken from another recipe; (list continues on page 2 not in the photos).', 'https://www.thechunkychef.com/chicken-taco-mexican-pinwheels/'),
('Chicken Tot Pie', 'Chicken Tot Pie is an easy fun twist on classic pot pie. Tender chicken, corn, peas, green beans and carrots in a creamy sauce with crispy tater tot crust.', 8, 5, 45, '["1 can cream of chicken soup", "1/2 cup sour cream", "2/3 cup whole milk", "16 ounces frozen mixed vegetables", "1 teaspoon dried thyme", "1 teaspoon kosher salt", "1/2 teaspoon coarse ground black pepper", "4 cups chicken breast, cooked and chopped", "1 cup cheddar cheese, shredded", "32 ounces frozen tater tots"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat oven to 375 degrees.", "Mix the cream of chicken soup, sour cream, milk, mixed vegetables, thyme, salt, pepper, chicken and cheese in a large bowl.", "Pour into baking dish then top with tater tots, lined up neatly in rows.", "Bake for 45-50 minutes until top is browned and crispy."]'::jsonb, '["Dinner then Dessert", "chicken", "casserole", "American", "tater tots", "pot pie"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Dinner then Dessert web printout (page 1 of 2), author Sabrina Snyder. Course: Dinner; Cuisine: American; 433 kcal per serving. Page 2 of the printout is not in the photos; ingredients and all 4 instructions are on page 1.', 'https://dinnerthendessert.com/chicken-tot-pie-tater-tot-pot-pie/'),
('Chilli Clam Chowder', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["3 medium diced onions", "2 lbs. beef", "2 cans 28 oz tomatoes", "2 cans red kidney beans", "1 can baked beans", "1 can black beans", "1 can tomato sauce", "4 c. frozen corn", "1/4 c. chilli powder", "salt", "pepper", "1/3 jar salsa", "1 garlic clove", "1/2 tsp. dried basil", "2 TBS Creole seasoning", "2 TBS Italian seasoning", "1 TBS oregano", "2 TBS chili powder (extra)", "2 TBS Lawry''s salt"]'::jsonb, '["20 min."]'::jsonb, '["chili", "beef", "beans", "soup"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe (Evernote printout, page 2/3, 2/4/2021). Title as written is "Chilli Clam Chowder", but there are no clams: it is a beef, bean and tomato chili. The only cooking direction written is "20 min." A separate handwritten box labeled "Add" lists extra seasonings, included at the end of the ingredients: 2 TBS Creole, 2 TBS Italian season, 1 TBS oregano, 2 TBS chili powder (boxed, marked "extra"), 2 TBS Lowry''s salt.

Couldn''t read for sure: title: written clearly as "Chilli Clam Chowder" (could be a family joke name; the dish is a chili); "Creole" read as Creole seasoning; "Lowrys Salt" taken as Lawry''s seasoned salt', NULL),
('Chinese Chicken Salad', 'Chinese Chicken Salad is crispy, crunchy, and colorful. This fresh salad is a refreshing choice for a side salad at dinner or to bring to a get-together.', 6, 20, 20, '["1/2 cup rice wine vinegar", "1/4 cup light soy sauce", "3 tablespoons granulated sugar", "1/2 teaspoon roasted garlic paste", "1 teaspoon ginger paste", "1/2 cup vegetable oil", "1/2 head green cabbage thinly sliced", "1/2 head red cabbage thinly sliced", "1 small red bell pepper seeds and stem removed, thinly sliced", "1 small carrot sliced thinly", "2 green onions chopped (you can use the green parts only or the whites too, for added onion flavor)", "1 cup loosely packed cilantro chopped", "2 cups cooked chicken cubed or shredded", "1 cup chow mein noodles crispy fried", "1 cup wonton strips crispy fried", "1 tablespoon toasted sesame seeds"]'::jsonb, '["Whisk together vinegar, soy sauce, sugar, garlic paste, and ginger paste. Slowly drizzle the oil into the other dressing ingredients while whisking vigorously to emulsify the ingredients. Set aside.", "In a large salad bowl toss together cabbage, bell pepper, carrots, green onions, cilantro, and chicken.", "Chill, covered, in the refrigerator until ready to serve.", "Just before serving, add chow mein noodles and wonton strips to the salad ingredients.", "Whisk sesame seeds into the dressing. Drizzle desired amount of dressing over the salad and toss to combine.", "Serve immediately."]'::jsonb, '["The Best Blog Recipes", "chicken", "salad", "Chinese", "Asian"]'::jsonb, '["lunch", "dinner"]'::jsonb, 'The Best Blog Recipes web printout, 2 pages (Recipe Creation: Shauna Smart). The first 6 ingredients are the Soy Ginger Dressing; the rest are the Salad. 349 kcal per serving. Nutrition per serving: Carbohydrates 69g, Protein 13g, Fat 2g, Sodium 1055mg, Sugar 13g.

Couldn''t read for sure: "1/2 cup rice wine vinegar" (end of "vinegar" under glare); "for added onion flavor" printed as "addedonion flavor"', NULL),
('Chocolate Scotcheroos (short version)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 c. sugar", "1 c corn syrup", "1 c. peanut butter", "6 c. rice crispies", "1 c. choc.", "1 c. butterscotch"]'::jsonb, '["Sugar and corn syrup: cook over heat until boils, then add peanut butter.", "Chocolate and butterscotch: melt, put on top."]'::jsonb, '["dessert", "bars", "peanut butter", "chocolate", "butterscotch"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten as "Choc. Scotcheroos" below Outrageous Chocolate Chip Cookies on an Evernote printout. Instructions are brackets beside the ingredients: sugar + corn syrup "cook over heat until boils then add peanut butter"; choc. + butterscotch "melt put on top". Mixing in the rice crispies is not written. A fuller copy of this recipe exists elsewhere.

Couldn''t read for sure: "6 c. rice crispies" (6 is faint)', NULL),
('Chocolate Scotcherous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 cup sugar", "1 cup light corn syrup", "1 cup peanut butter", "6 cups Rice Krispies", "1 cup milk chocolate chips", "1 cup butterscotch morsels", "butter (for the pan)"]'::jsonb, '["Combine sugar & syrup in 3 qt. sauce pan. Cook over moderate heat, stirring frequently until mixture boils. Remove from heat. Stir in peanut butter, mix well. Add Rice Krispies, stir until well blended. Press into buttered 13x9 pan. Melt chocolate chips & butterscotch morsels together over hot water (double boiler), stir until well blended."]'::jsonb, '["dessert", "bars", "no bake", "peanut butter", "chocolate", "butterscotch"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe (Scotcheroos; title spelled "Scotcherous" on the card). The card ends after melting the chips; presumably the melted chocolate/butterscotch is spread over the bars.', NULL),
('Churrasco Steak Strip Farfalle with Fontina Cream Sauce', NULL, 2, NULL, 40, '["10 oz steak strips", "5 oz farfalle pasta", "1/4 oz cilantro", "1 1/2 oz fontina cheese slices", "1/2 tsp garlic salt", ".14 oz lemon juice", "4 fl oz cream sauce base", "1 tsp chile and cumin rub", "1 zucchini", "1 roma tomato", "olive oil", "salt", "pepper"]'::jsonb, '["Boil the Pasta: All cook times are approximate based on testing. If using any fresh produce, thoroughly rinse and pat dry. Bring 8 cups water to a boil in a medium pot. Once water is boiling, add pasta and cook until al dente, 10-12 minutes. Reserve 1 cup pasta cooking water. Drain pasta in a colander and set aside. While pasta boils, continue recipe.", "Prepare the Ingredients: Trim ends off zucchini, halve lengthwise, and cut into 1/4\" half-moons. Core tomato and cut into 1/2\" dice. Mince cilantro (no need to stem). Cut cheese into bite-sized pieces. Pat steak strips dry. Coarsely chop, then separate pieces.", "Cook the Steak Strips: Place a large non-stick pan over medium-high heat and add 1 tsp. olive oil. Add steak strips and chile and cumin rub to hot pan. Stir occasionally until no pink remains and steak strips reach a minimum internal temperature of 145 degrees, 4-6 minutes. Remove from burner. Transfer steak strips to a plate. Rest, 3 minutes. Reserve pan; no need to wipe clean.", "Cook the Vegetables: Return pan used to cook steak strips to medium heat. Add zucchini and 1 tsp. olive oil to hot pan. Stir occasionally until starting to brown, 2-4 minutes. Add tomatoes, garlic salt, and a pinch of pepper. Stir occasionally until tomatoes begin to release juices, 1-2 minutes.", "Make Sauce, Add Pasta, and Finish Dish: Add cream base, 1/4 tsp. salt, and half the reserved pasta cooking water to hot pan. Bring to a simmer. Once simmering, add cheese pieces, one piece at a time, stirring after each addition, until melted and combined. Add pasta and steak strips. Stir until combined and heated through, 1-2 minutes. If sauce is too thick, add additional pasta cooking water, 1 Tbsp. at a time, until desired consistency is reached. Add lemon juice and stir to combine. Remove from burner. Plate dish as pictured on front of card, garnishing with cilantro. Bon appétit!"]'::jsonb, '["Home Chef", "beef", "steak", "pasta", "Latin"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Home Chef meal kit card (homechef.com/22074). Difficulty: Easy. Spice level: Not spicy. Cook within 6 days. Customize It options: 10 oz. steak strips (default), 10 oz. diced boneless skinless chicken breasts, 8 oz. shrimp, 12 oz. filets mignon, 20 oz. double portion steak strips. Customize It instructions: If using 20 oz. steak strips, follow same instructions as 10 oz. steak strips, working in batches if necessary. If using diced chicken breasts, pat dry. Follow same instructions as steak strips in Step 3, stirring occasionally until chicken reaches minimum internal temperature, 5-7 minutes. If using filets mignon, pat dry. Follow same instructions as steak strips in Step 3, cooking until steak reaches desired doneness, or 4-6 minutes per side for medium/medium-well. Rest, 3 minutes. Serve alongside pasta. If using shrimp, pat dry. Follow same instructions as steak strips in Step 3, cooking until shrimp reach minimum internal temperature, 2-3 minutes per side. Minimum internal temperatures: 145° steak, pork, lamb, seafood; 160° ground beef, ground pork; 165° chicken, ground turkey. Rest steak or pork after cooking, 3 minutes. Step 3 on the steps page is partly washed out by glare; its first line and a few words were reconstructed from the legible fragments.

Couldn''t read for sure: lemon juice amount printed as ''.14 oz'' (possibly a stray mark before ''14''); step 3 first line mostly washed out by glare: best reading ''Place a large non-stick pan over medium-high heat and add 1 tsp. olive oil.''; step 3 words ''Add steak strips'', ''hot pan'', ''steak strips reach a'', ''plate'', ''Reserve pan'' partly washed out; step 3 cook time ''4-6 minutes'' (faint)', NULL),
('Cinnamon Apple Breakfast Porridge', NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, '["1/2 cup whole raw almonds", "1/2 cup whole raw cashews", "1/4 cup raw walnuts", "1/3 cup unsweetened coconut flakes", "1 large ripe banana", "1 egg yolk (optional)", "1 tbsp ghee (or coconut oil)", "1 14 oz. can pure coconut milk", "2 tsp pure vanilla extract", "2 tsp ground cinnamon", "1/8 tsp ground nutmeg", "1 medium apple, chopped into bite-sized pieces"]'::jsonb, '["In a medium bowl, add the nuts and coconut flakes. Add enough filtered water to the bowl to completely cover the nuts and coconut. Add a pinch of salt and cover the bowl with a kitchen"]'::jsonb, '["Whole30", "porridge", "apple", "nuts", "breakfast", "paleo"]'::jsonb, '["breakfast"]'::jsonb, 'From a "Winter Whole30 Recipes" handout (Breakfast section). Step 1 is cut off at the bottom of the page mid-sentence; the rest of the steps (next page of the handout) are not in the photos.

A page of this recipe was missing from the photos.', NULL),
('Classic White Bread', NULL, NULL, NULL, 20, '["1 1/8 cup water", "3 cups bread flour", "1 1/2 tbsp dry milk", "2 tbls. sugar", "1 1/2 tsp. salt", "2 tbls. butter", "2 tsp. yeast"]'::jsonb, '["Bake at 375° for 20 min."]'::jsonb, '["bread", "white bread", "bread machine", "side", "handwritten"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten in a spiral recipe notebook, heading "Classic White" with "375° 20 min" beside it (looks like bread-machine amounts).', NULL),
('Colorful Kielbasa', '"This stick-to-your-ribs dish is sure to satisfy the heartiest appetite," writes Schelby Thompson of Dover, Delaware. "You can take it from stovetop to table in about half an hour."', 4, NULL, 30, '["1 can (10-3/4 ounces) condensed cream of celery soup, undiluted", "3/4 cup water", "1 tablespoon butter or margarine", "1 pound smoked kielbasa, cut into 1/2-inch pieces", "3/4 cup uncooked long grain rice", "1 package (10 ounces) frozen peas", "1 jar (4-1/2 ounces) sliced mushrooms, drained", "1 cup (4 ounces) shredded cheddar cheese"]'::jsonb, '["In a skillet, combine soup, water and butter; bring to a boil. Add kielbasa and rice. Reduce heat; cover and simmer for 15-18 minutes or until rice is almost tender.", "Stir in peas and mushrooms. Cover and simmer 15 minutes or until rice is tender and peas are heated through.", "Sprinkle with cheese; cover and let stand until melted."]'::jsonb, '["kielbasa", "sausage", "rice", "skillet", "one-pan"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Yield: 4-6 servings. Newspaper/magazine clipping taped in a notebook (Evernote printout page 2/3, 2/2/2021). Below it is the start of another clipping, "Pork Chop Skillet Meal", cut off after the first two ingredients.

Couldn''t read for sure: ''ribs'', ''the'', ''writes'', ''of Dover'' in the blurb hidden by glare; ''bring to a boil'' and ''Reduce heat;'' partly hidden by glare; ''or until'' after 15-18 minutes (glare)', NULL),
('Colorful Kielbasa (handwritten)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 can cream of celery", "3/4 c. water", "1 tbls. butter", "1 pound of cheddarwurst", "3/4 c. uncooked rice", "1 package frozen peas", "1 cup cheese"]'::jsonb, '["In a skillet, combine soup, water & butter, bring to boil.", "Add cheddarwurst and rice. Cover & simmer for 15 min.", "Stir in peas, cover until rice is done.", "Add cheese last."]'::jsonb, '["sausage", "kielbasa", "rice", "skillet"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten notebook page (Evernote printout dated 2/3/2021), below Green Beans. Margin notes beside the ingredients: ''Bring to boil'' (soup, water, butter), ''then add these'' (cheddarwurst, rice, peas), ''Last'' (cheese). The last step comes from the ''Last'' margin note. Uses cheddarwurst (cheddar-filled smoked sausage) rather than plain kielbasa.

Couldn''t read for sure: ''cheddarwurst'' written ''cheddar worst''; ''rice'' in last line partly under glare', NULL),
('Copycat Cracker Barrel Grilled Chicken Tenderloins', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 lb chicken tenders or cut chicken breasts", "1/2 cup Italian dressing", "2 tablespoons honey", "2 teaspoons lime juice"]'::jsonb, '["Place chicken tenderloins into a large plastic bag with wet ingredients. Marinate in refrigerator for at least one hour.", "Add chicken and liquid to a large skillet. Cook over medium heat until liquid is reduced and chicken is golden in color, but not dry. Be sure to turn chicken throughout the cooking process."]'::jsonb, '["Dear Crissy", "chicken", "copycat", "Cracker Barrel", "skillet"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'From Dear Crissy (web printout, printed 3/24/22). By Crissy Page. Category: Dinner.', 'https://dearcrissy.com/copycat-cracker-barrel-grilled-chicken-tenderloins-recipe/'),
('Copycat Panera Broccoli Cheese Soup', 'Copycat Panera Broccoli Cheese Soup is ready in less than 30 minutes! The perfect bowl of comfort food without leaving your house!', 4, 10, 20, '["1/4 cup unsalted butter", "1/2 cup diced onions yellow or white", "1 cup shredded carrots I used matchsticks that I cut into half inch pieces", "2 1/2-3 cups broccoli florets chopped small", "1 1/2 cups chicken broth", "1 cup milk I use skim/fat free", "1 cup heavy whipping cream", "1/4 cup all-purpose flour", "1 1/2 teaspoons kosher salt", "1/2 teaspoon black pepper", "pinch of crushed red pepper flakes or more as desired", "2 cups shredded cheddar cheese"]'::jsonb, '["In a large pot over medium high heat, melt butter. Add in onions, carrots and broccoli. Cook to soften about 5 minutes (may be more or less depending on the size vegetables you cut).", "Slowly add in broth, milk, and cream. Sprinkle with flour and add salt, pepper and red pepper flakes. Continue stirring and heating over medium heat until thickened. This will take about 10-15 minutes.", "Once thick, add cheese and stir until melted and smooth. Serve soup and enjoy!"]'::jsonb, '["Shugary Sweets", "soup", "broccoli", "cheese", "copycat", "vegetarian", "American"]'::jsonb, '["lunch", "dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Printed from Shugary Sweets. Author: Aimee. Course: Soups and Stews. Cuisine: American. Equipment: Cuisinart CSB-79 Smart Stick 2 Speed Hand Blender. Notes: Easily double the ingredients to make more of this delicious soup! Use a good quality cheddar cheese for best results. And shred the cheese yourself for the creamiest results. Footer URL too blurry to copy (shugarysweets.com/copycat-panera-broccoli-cheese-soup/).', NULL),
('Cowboy Caviar', 'A deliciously addictive appetizer with beans, corn, avocado with a burst of lime!', NULL, NULL, 10, '["1 (15 oz) can black beans (preferably no salt)", "2 ears of corn (grilled outside with a little butter, salt and pepper adds TONS of flavor)", "1 bell pepper (I used red, yellow and green)", "2 cloves garlic, minced", "1 tablespoon shallot", "2 tablespoons red onion", "1 large avocado", "5-6 grape tomatoes sliced in quarters", "4 tablespoons olive oil", "1 tablespoon white vinegar", "1 teaspoon lime zest", "4 tablespoons lime juice", "1 tablespoon sugar", "1/4 cup cilantro, chopped fine (or parsley)", "1 teaspoon sea salt", "1/4 teaspoon freshly ground black pepper", "1/4 teaspoon cayenne pepper", "1/4 teaspoon cumin"]'::jsonb, '["Combine the corn, peppers, garlic, shallots, red onion and avocado in a bowl."]'::jsonb, '["appetizer", "dip", "beans", "salad", "Mexican", "vegetarian"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Web printout (PrintFriendly, https://www.printfriendly.com/p/g/6iZRLL), printed 12/15/21, page 3 of 4. Rated 5 from 4 reviews. Ingredients from "Black Beans" through "Grape Tomatoes" are the salad; olive oil through cumin are "For the Viniagrette". Only step 1 is on this page; the remaining steps (page 4 of 4) are not in the photos. Pages 1-2 (title area) also not in the photos; the title comes from the page header.

