('Cowboy Stew', 'Dinner''s on! My Cowboy Stew recipe combines three types of tender meat with beans & veggies in a one-pot wonder delicious enough to feed everyone!', 8, 15, 90, '["4 slices bacon, chopped", "2 (12-ounce) packages smoked kielbasa sausage, cut into 1/2 inch slices", "1 1/2 pounds ground beef, 80/20", "1 medium onion, diced", "3 cloves garlic, minced", "3 tablespoons all-purpose flour", "1 1/2 teaspoons salt", "1/2 teaspoon black pepper", "1 teaspoon chili powder", "1 (14.5-ounce) can petite diced tomatoes, with liquid", "2 (16-ounce) cans baked beans, with liquid", "1 (7-ounce) can chopped green chilies, with liquid", "1 (15-ounce) can sweet corn, with liquid", "2 medium russet potatoes, peeled and cut into 1/2 inch cubes", "1 cup water", "2 tablespoons parsley, chopped"]'::jsonb, '["Cook bacon until brown and crispy in a large pot. Using a slotted spoon, transfer bacon to a plate lined with a paper towel to drain."]'::jsonb, '["Gonna Want Seconds", "beef", "sausage", "bacon", "stew", "soup", "American"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'From gonnawantseconds.com (web printout, page 1 of 2, printed 5/1/22). Author: Kathleen. Course: Main Course, Soup. Cuisine: American. Calories: 745 kcal. Total time 1 hour 45 minutes. Only step 1 is on this page; the remaining steps are on page 2, which is not in the photos.

