('Crockpot Ham, Green Beans and Potatoes', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 pound boneless ham, cut into bite-sized pieces", "1 pound fresh green beans, trimmed", "1 pound baby potatoes, halved or quartered", "1 onion, diced", "3 cloves garlic, minced", "1 tsp dried thyme", "1 tsp dried rosemary", "1 tsp paprika", "1/2 tsp salt", "1/4 tsp black pepper", "1 cup chicken or vegetable broth"]'::jsonb, '["Place the ham, green beans, potatoes, onion, and garlic in the crockpot.", "In a small bowl, mix together the thyme, rosemary, paprika, salt, and black pepper.", "Sprinkle the seasoning mix over the ingredients in the crockpot.", "Pour the broth over everything in the crockpot.", "Cover the crockpot and cook on low for 6-8 hours, or on high for 3-4 hours, or until the potatoes are tender and the green beans are cooked to your liking.", "Serve hot and enjoy!"]'::jsonb, '["ham", "slow cooker", "crockpot", "green beans", "potatoes"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Printed recipe card (white text on a black box with a photo of the dish). The printed steps are unnumbered; each line was taken as one step. Ingredients were printed as ''1 pound of ...'', ''1 teaspoon of ...''.

Couldn''t read for sure: green beans line: glare after ''trimm'', read as ''trimmed''; there may be more words after it; ''halved or quartered'' and ''minced'': partly under glare, best reading; step 3 ''seasoning'' and ''in the crockpot'': partly under glare, best reading', NULL),
('Crockpot Ravioli Casserole', 'This crockpot ravioli casserole is a four ingredient dinner recipe that is both easy and delicious. Also, incredibly filling as well. If you''re a fan of casserole crockpot recipes, you''ll want to whip it up for dinner tonight!', NULL, 10, 120, '["20 oz. frozen four cheese ravioli {1 pkg.}", "24 oz. pasta sauce {1 jar}", "4 cups shredded mozzarella cheese", "1 pound cooked and drained Italian sausage", "non stick cooking spray"]'::jsonb, '["Spray the inside of a 6 quart crock pot with non stick cooking spray", "Pour 1/2 jar of pasta sauce in the crockpot", "Spread 1/2 of the ravioli in an even layer on top of the sauce", "Spread 1/2 of the cooked Italian sausage over the cheese", "Spread out 2 cups of mozzarella over the ravioli", "Repeat that one more time making two layers", "Cook on HIGH for 1 hour 45 minutes, or LOW for 3 hours 30 minutes, or until done. ENJOY"]'::jsonb, '["Coupon Cravings", "sausage", "pasta", "Italian", "casserole", "slow cooker"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout, page 1 of 1. Course: Dinner. Cuisine: American. Total time 2 hours 10 minutes. Recipe Notes: If you want the casserole browned on top you can put the crock in the oven on broil for a few minutes. Footer URL somewhat blurry (couponcravings.com/crockpot-ravioli-casserole-recipe/).', NULL),
('Crunchy Baked Chicken Tacos', 'Crispy and Crunchy Baked Chicken Tacos are a quickly thrown-together and satisfying meal, complete with baked chicken, taco seasoning, black beans, hard taco shells, and plenty of shredded cheddar cheese.', 12, 10, 15, '["2 cups cooked chicken", "1 cup black beans", "1 cup diced tomatoes", "2 tablespoons taco seasoning", "12 hard taco shells", "6 ounces sharp cheddar cheese, shredded (about 1.5 cups)", "cilantro, lettuce, salsa, olives, sour cream, hot sauce, etc. for serving, optional"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F., line a baking dish with foil or parchment paper, and spray the foil or parchment with a bit of cooking spray.", "In a medium bowl, combine the chicken, black beans, tomatoes, and taco seasoning, and stir to combine well.", "Place the taco shells in the prepared pan.", "Fill each taco shell with the chicken mixture, distributing it evenly between the shells.", "Top the filled taco shells with the grated cheese.", "Bake the tacos for 12 to 15 minutes, or until the cheese is melted and the filling is hot.", "Serve hot with optional cilantro, lettuce, olives, sour cream, hot sauce, etc."]'::jsonb, '["Bless This Mess", "chicken", "tacos", "Mexican", "baked"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'From Bless This Mess (blessthismessplease.com; web printout 1/2, printed 6/1/2021). Author: Melissa Griffiths - Bless this Mess. Yield: 12 tacos. Total time 25 minutes. The taco seasoning links to a homemade taco seasoning mix recipe (https://www.blessthismessplease.com/homemade-taco-seasoning-mix/). Recipe notes: Don''t forget to spray the pan with cooking spray, or the taco shells stick badly (the cheese kind of glues them into place). I like to remove as much of the tomato guts/seeds as I can so that they don''t make my taco shells soggy while cooking. Page 2/2 not in the photos (recipe complete on page 1). Footer URL ends in a glare spot, so sourceUrl left out.

Couldn''t read for sure: Cook Time is hidden by glare; 15 minutes assumed from prep 10 + total 25; servings 12 = ''Yield: 12 tacos''', NULL),
('Crunchy Southwestern Chicken Wrap', 'Crunchy Southwestern Chicken Wrap - easy lunch ideas are hard to come by. These chicken wraps come together in minutes, you can make them ahead, and the creamy spicy sauce makes them extra tasty!', 4, 15, NULL, '["3/4 cup sour cream", "3/4 cup salsa", "1 1/2 Tbls taco seasoning", "4 large tortillas, (wrap size)", "1 1/3 cup shredded lettuce", "1/2 cup tomato, diced", "1 whole avocado, diced", "1/2 cup cheddar cheese, shredded", "2 cup cooked chicken, shredded", "1 cup Fritos, crushed"]'::jsonb, '["In a bowl mix together sour cream, salsa, and taco seasoning until well blended.", "Lay a tortilla flat on a cutting board. Spread 1 heaping tablespoon of sauce over the bottom half of the tortilla, leaving a 1 inch border on each side.", "Sprinkle 1/3 cup of lettuce, 2 Tbls tomato, 1/4 of the avocado, 2 Tbls of cheese, and 1/2 cup of chicken over the sauce. Crush 1/4 cup of Fritos over the chicken. Drizzle 1 Tbls of sauce over the top.", "Fold in the sides and roll tightly. Repeat with the remaining wraps. Cut in half to serve."]'::jsonb, '["Dinners, Dishes, and Desserts", "chicken", "wraps", "Southwestern", "American", "sandwich"]'::jsonb, '["lunch", "dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from dinnersdishesanddesserts.com (pages 1-2 of 3; page 3 is only the site''s newsletter signup). Sauce: sour cream, salsa, taco seasoning; Wraps: the rest. Prep time 15 minutes, total time 15 minutes. Cuisine: American / Category: Dinner Recipes. (c) Erin S. Nutrition per wrap (serving size 1): 491 calories, saturated fat 11g, cholesterol 90mg, sodium 1091mg, carbohydrates 22g, fiber 3g, sugar 5g, protein 23g.', 'https://dinnersdishesanddesserts.com/crunchy-southwestern-chicken-wrap/'),
('Cubed Steak Stew', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["3 tbls flour", "1 1/2 tsp salt", "1/4 tsp pepper", "4 beef cubed steaks, cut", "3 tbls bacon grease", "1 large onion, thinly sliced", "1 clove of minced garlic", "4 medium potatoes", "1 can tomatoes", "1 can tomato sauce", "1 tsp salt", "1 package peas", "1/2 medium green pepper"]'::jsonb, '["Mix flour, 1 1/2 tsp salt & pepper. Coat meat with flour mixture. Melt bacon grease, brown meat. Add onion, garlic, potatoes, tomatoes, tomato sauce & 1 tsp salt. Boil. Cook on low for 30 min until meat & potatoes are done. Add green pepper & peas."]'::jsonb, '["beef", "stew", "cubed steak", "handwritten"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe on a lined card, printed from an Evernote shared note ("Untitled note", page 2/3, dated 2/3/2021). Card footer: "Let the countryside and everything in it rejoice!" 1 Chronicles 16:32 TLB.

Couldn''t read for sure: ''3 tbls bacon grease'': written like ''baking grease'', read as bacon grease because the directions say ''melt bacon grease''; ''1 tsp salt'' (3rd-to-last ingredient line): the word after ''1 teas'' is hidden by glare; read as salt because the directions say ''& 1 teas salt''; ''1 clove of minced garlic'': written ''or'' or ''of''; ''4 beef cubed steaks cut'': ''beef'' is a best reading', NULL),
('Deluxe Cheeseburger Melt', NULL, 8, 15, 28, '["1 1/3 cups Original Bisquick mix", "1/4 cup water", "2 eggs", "1 1/2 cups shredded Cheddar cheese", "1 lb ground beef", "1 can (10 3/4 oz) condensed cream of mushroom soup", "1 cup frozen mixed vegetables", "cooking spray"]'::jsonb, '["Heat oven to 400°F. Spray 13\"x9\" pan. Stir Bisquick mix, water, eggs and 1 cup of the cheese. Spread in pan.", "Brown beef; drain. Stir in soup and vegetables; heat until hot. Spread over batter in pan.", "Bake 23-25 min or until edges are light golden brown. Sprinkle with remaining cheese. Bake 1-3 min or until cheese melts."]'::jsonb, '["Bisquick", "beef", "casserole", "cheeseburger"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Printed Bisquick box/card clipping taped into a notebook beside handwritten Beef Stroganoff. High Altitude (3500-6500 ft): No changes. © 2004 General Mills.

Couldn''t read for sure: prep time ''15 min'' (blurry); ''Bisquick'' in step 1 and ''vegetables; heat'' in step 2 partly under glare; ''golden'' partly under glare', NULL),
('Down Home Steak ''n'' Potatoes with Garlic Herb Butter, Mixed Greens & Creamy Mustard Sauce', NULL, 2, NULL, 15, '["12 oz potatoes", "1 tomato", "2 TBSP garlic herb butter", "10 oz ranch steak", "4 oz cream sauce base", "2 tsp Dijon mustard", "2 oz mixed greens", "4 oz shredded carrots", "5 tsp balsamic vinegar", "kosher salt", "black pepper", "1 tsp cooking oil", "1 tsp olive oil"]'::jsonb, '["Prep: Wash and dry produce. Quarter potatoes. Cut tomato into wedges. Place potatoes and half the garlic herb butter in a microwave-safe bowl; season with salt and pepper. Cover with plastic wrap; microwave until tender, 6-7 minutes. Keep covered.", "Sizzle: Pat steak* dry and season with salt and pepper. Drizzle oil in a hot pan. Cook steak to desired doneness, 3-6 minutes per side. To finish steak, add remaining garlic herb butter and spoon over. Transfer to a cutting board; reserve butter in pan.", "Mix: In a second microwave-safe bowl, mix half the cream sauce (all for 4), half the mustard (all for 4), and a big pinch of pepper. Cover with plastic wrap; microwave 40 seconds. In a third bowl, toss mixed greens, tomato, carrots, half the vinegar (all for 4), and a drizzle of olive oil (large drizzle for 4); season with salt and pepper.", "Serve: Thinly slice steak against the grain. Spoon melted butter over steak. Serve with salad and potatoes. Drizzle with creamy mustard sauce."]'::jsonb, '["HelloFresh", "beef", "steak", "potatoes", "Fast & Fresh", "American"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'HelloFresh ''Fast & Fresh'' recipe card, WK 9-14. Box to plate: 15 minutes. Calories: 570. *Steak is fully cooked when internal temperature reaches 145°. Ingredient amounts are for 2 people (4-person: 24 oz potatoes, 2 tomatoes, 4 TBSP garlic herb butter, 20 oz ranch steak, 4 oz cream sauce base, 2 tsp Dijon mustard, 4 oz mixed greens, 8 oz shredded carrots, 5 tsp balsamic vinegar; cooking oil 1 tsp, olive oil 2 tsp).', NULL),
('Easy Cheesy Mexican Rice Chicken', NULL, 4, 10, 45, '["4 boneless, skinless chicken breasts", "1 cup long-grain white rice", "1 can (10 oz) diced tomatoes with green chilies, undrained", "1 can (14.5 oz) chicken broth", "1 teaspoon chili powder", "1 teaspoon cumin", "1/2 teaspoon garlic powder", "1 cup shredded Mexican blend cheese", "salt and pepper, to taste", "chopped cilantro (optional topping)", "diced avocado (optional topping)", "sour cream (optional topping)", "non-stick cooking spray"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat your oven to 375°F (190°C). Grease a 9x13-inch baking dish with non-stick cooking spray.", "Season the chicken breasts with salt, pepper, chili powder, cumin, and garlic powder on both sides.", "In a large mixing bowl, combine the rice, diced [... rest of this step is hidden by the comment box in the printout ...]", "Pour the rice mixture into the prepared baking dish and spread it out evenly.", "Arrange the seasoned chicken breasts on top of the rice mixture.", "Cover the baking dish with aluminum foil and bake in the preheated oven for 35-40 minutes, or until the chicken is cooked through and the rice is tender.", "Remove the foil and sprinkle the shredded cheese over the chicken and rice.", "Return the baking dish to the oven and bake for an additional 5-10 minutes, or until the cheese is melted and bubbly.", "Remove from the oven and let it cool for a few minutes before serving.", "Serve the Cheesy Fiesta Chicken with Mexican Rice hot, garnished with chopped cilantro, diced avocado, and a dollop of sour cream, if desired."]'::jsonb, '["Recipeasy", "Facebook", "chicken", "rice", "Mexican", "casserole"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Facebook post by Recipeasy (May 26), printed 8/17/24, pages 1 and 2 of 4 (pages 3-4 not in the photos; they appear to be comments). The "Write a comment..." box covers the rest of step 3; it presumably combines the rice, diced tomatoes with green chilies, and chicken broth. Prep Time: 10 minutes | Cooking Time: 45 minutes | Total Time: 55 minutes | Servings: 4.

Couldn''t read for sure: Step 3 hidden by comment box after ''In a large mixing bowl, combine the rice, diced''; ''Total Time: 55 minutes | Servings: 4'' line is half covered by the image (best reading)', NULL),
('Easy Crockpot Potato Soup', NULL, NULL, NULL, 480, '["1 30 oz. frozen bag of cubed potatoes", "3 14 oz. cans of chicken broth", "1 can of cream of chicken soup", "1/2 c. onion", "1/4 tsp. ground pepper", "1 pkg. cream cheese", "cheese, for sprinkling", "some Velveeta cheese"]'::jsonb, '["Cook 6 to 8 hrs. Put the cream cheese in at the end; soften it so it will melt easier.", "Sprinkle with cheese. Add some Velveeta cheese."]'::jsonb, '["soup", "potato", "slow cooker", "crockpot"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe (Evernote printout, page 2/3, 2/4/2021). As written: "1 pkg. cream cheese (put in at the end) soften it so it will melt easier. 6 to 8 hrs. sprinkle with cheese. add some Velveta cheese." The amounts at the start of the first three ingredient lines are partly washed out by glare.

Couldn''t read for sure: "1 30 oz." frozen bag of potatoes (size partly washed out; could be 32 oz); "cubed" potatoes (written like "culed"); "3 14 oz." cans of chicken broth (only the 3 is clear); "1 can" of cream of chicken soup (amount washed out)', NULL),
('Easy Hamburger Soup', 'Hamburger Soup is a quick and easy meal loaded with vegetables, lean beef, diced tomatoes and potatoes. It''s great made ahead of time, reheats well and freezes perfectly.', 8, 10, 25, '["1 pound lean ground beef", "1 onion diced", "2 cloves garlic minced", "2 medium potatoes peeled and diced", "3 1/2 cups beef broth", "28 ounces diced tomatoes with juice", "1 can condensed tomato soup", "2 teaspoons Worcestershire sauce", "1 teaspoon Italian seasoning", "1 bay leaf", "salt and pepper to taste", "3 cups mixed vegetables fresh or frozen"]'::jsonb, '["Brown onion, ground beef and garlic until no pink remains. Drain any fat.", "Add potatoes, broth, tomatoes, tomato soup, Worcestershire sauce, seasoning and bay leaves. Simmer covered 10 minutes.", "Stir in vegetables. Simmer 15-20 minutes or until potatoes are tender."]'::jsonb, '["Spend With Pennies", "beef", "soup", "ground beef", "American"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Web page printout, author Holly Nilsson (no URL printed on these pages; site tag is a guess from the author). Course: Soup. Cuisine: American. Total time 35 minutes. Nutrition per 1.5 cup serving: 245 calories, carbohydrates 25g, protein 16g, fat 9g, saturated fat 3g, cholesterol 38mg, sodium 692mg, potassium 923mg, fiber 5g, sugar 4g, vitamin A 3670IU, vitamin C 24.2mg, calcium 79mg, iron 4.6mg.', NULL),
('Farmer''s Casserole', 'This casserole is handy—you can put it together the night before, let the flavors blend, then bake it in the morning. It''s also versatile...elegant enough to serve for a ladies'' brunch but hearty enough to satisfy a man-sized appetite.', NULL, NULL, 60, '["3 cups frozen shredded hash browns", "3/4 cup shredded Monterey Jack cheese", "1 cup diced fully cooked ham", "1/4 cup chopped green onions", "4 eggs", "1 can (12 ounces) evaporated milk", "1/4 teaspoon pepper", "1/8 teaspoon salt"]'::jsonb, '["Place potatoes in an 8-in. square baking dish. Sprinkle with cheese, ham and onions. Beat eggs, milk, pepper and salt; pour over all. Cover and refrigerate for several hours or overnight.", "Remove from refrigerator 30 minutes before baking. Bake, uncovered, at 350° for 55-60 minutes or until a knife inserted near the center comes out clean."]'::jsonb, '["ham", "eggs", "potatoes", "casserole", "breakfast", "make-ahead"]'::jsonb, '["breakfast"]'::jsonb, 'From Nancy Schmidt, Center, Colorado (printed magazine clipping taped in a notebook; Evernote printout dated 2/4/2021). Yield is printed but washed out. Glare covers part of the blurb and ingredient names; those words were filled in from context. Shares the page with Sun-dried Tomato Pesto with Bowtie Pasta.

Couldn''t read for sure: ''frozen shredded hash browns'': ''shredded hash'' covered by glare; ''Monterey Jack'': mostly covered by glare; ''fully cooked ham'': ''cooked ham'' covered by glare; ''green onions'': partly covered; blurb words ''you can'', ''blend, then'', ''elegant enough'', ''enough to satisfy'' covered by glare; ''a knife inserted'': partly covered; Yield number unreadable (probably 6 servings); author name ''Schmidt'' (blurry)', NULL),
('Fiesta Chicken Casserole', 'Fiesta chicken casserole is filled with chunks of chicken, tender pasta, corn, black beans, all in a one dish cheesy chicken casserole. Simple to make and a great way to use up leftover chicken or a Rotisserie chicken.', 8, 15, 25, '["2 cups uncooked spiral pasta", "1 cup sour cream", "1 cup salsa", "1 teaspoon cumin", "1 teaspoon garlic powder", "1 teaspoon onion powder", "1 can (15 oz) corn (drained)", "1 can (15 oz) black beans (drained & rinsed)", "2 cups cooked shredded/chunked chicken", "2 cups shredded cheese", "cooking spray"]'::jsonb, '["Heat oven to 350 degrees. Prepare a 9x13 baking dish and spray with cooking spray. Set aside.", "Cook pasta according to package directions. Don''t forget to salt the pasta water. I use about 1 teaspoon salt.", "While pasta is cooking, combine sour cream, salsa, cumin, garlic powder, and onion powder in a large mixing bowl.", "Drain the pasta when it''s done cooking and add into the sour cream mixture. Stir to combine. Add in the corn, black beans, chicken, and 1 cup of the shredded cheese. Stir together to combine.", "Pour into the baking dish and sprinkle the remaining cheese on top. Cover with tin foil and cook for 20 minutes.", "Take the tin foil off and let cook an additional 5 minutes. Garnish with green onions, tomato, and avocado slices if wanted."]'::jsonb, '["Together as Family", "chicken", "pasta", "casserole", "Mexican"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Together as Family printout (12/3/2019). Author: Jessica - Together as Family. 350 kcal. Recipe Notes: I have found that it works best to use some of the fresh salsa that you can find in the produce area of the grocery store, instead of the jarred salsa on the shelves. You of course can use the jarred salsa, I just think the fresh salsa tastes better and does not seem to have as much liquid in the salsa.

Couldn''t read for sure: ''1 cup of the shredded cheese'' and ''let cook an additional'' partly washed out (reconstructed)', 'https://togetherasfamily.com/fiesta-chicken-casserole/'),
('Fiesta Ranch Chicken Pasta Salad', 'Fiesta Ranch Chicken Pasta Salad is full of fresh southwestern flavors with black beans, corn, cheese and tomatoes. Hearty chicken salad recipe topped with Fritos!', 15, 15, 10, '["16 oz pasta rotini, bowtie, tri-colored, etc", "3 boneless chicken breasts cooked and diced (I usually use a rotisserie chicken)", "1 packet taco seasoning mix", "15 oz can black beans drained and rinsed", "15 oz can kidney beans drained and rinsed", "10 oz corn frozen or canned", "1 cup onion chopped", "1 green pepper chopped", "3 oz olives sliced", "2 cups grated cheddar cheese", "2 tomatoes chopped", "1 pkg Frito Corn Chips (for topping)", "2 cups mayonnaise (dressing)", "1 cup buttermilk (dressing)", "1 pkg Hidden Valley Fiesta Ranch Dressing Mix (dressing)"]'::jsonb, '["Cook pasta, drain and cool. Combine with all of the other ingredients in a large mixing bowl, and then mix up the dressing.", "Whisk all of the dressing ingredients together in a small bowl until smooth.", "Add dressing to the salad and keep refrigerated until ready to serve. Right before serving, add"]'::jsonb, '["Butter with a Side of Bread", "chicken", "pasta salad", "salad", "Tex-Mex", "American"]'::jsonb, '["lunch", "dinner"]'::jsonb, 'From Butter with a Side of Bread (web printout, page 1 of 2, printed 4/30/22). Author: Jessica & Nellie. Rated 4.94 from 16 votes. Course: Salad. Cuisine: American. Calories: 577 kcal. Total time 25 mins. Salad dressing: 2 cups mayonnaise, 1 cup buttermilk, 1 pkg Hidden Valley Fiesta Ranch Dressing Mix. Step 3 is cut off at the bottom of page 1 (''Right before serving, add ...'', probably the Fritos); page 2 not in the photos. Footer URL too blurry for sourceUrl.

Couldn''t read for sure: ''bowtie, tri-colored'': partly hidden by a stain; ''breasts cooked'': partly hidden; ''taco seasoning mix'': ''mix'' partly hidden; description ''is full of'' and ''tomatoes'' partly hidden

A page of this recipe was missing from the photos.', NULL),
('Firecracker Meatballs with Roasted Green Beans & Jasmine Rice', NULL, 2, 10, 40, '["2 scallions", "1 thumb ginger", "2 TBSP mayonnaise", "1 1/2 TBSP sour cream", "2 tsp honey", "2 TBSP soy sauce", "1 tsp sriracha", "1/2 cup jasmine rice", "10 oz ground beef", "1/4 cup panko breadcrumbs", "6 oz green beans", "kosher salt", "black pepper", "2 tsp cooking oil"]'::jsonb, '["Prep: Adjust rack to top position (top and middle positions for 4 servings) and preheat oven to 425 degrees. Wash and dry produce. Trim and thinly slice scallions, separating whites from greens; mince whites. Peel and mince ginger.", "Make firecracker sauce: In a large bowl, combine mayonnaise, sour cream, honey, 2 tsp soy sauce (4 tsp for 4 servings), and Sriracha to taste. (You''ll use the rest of the soy sauce later.) Set aside.", "Cook rice: In a small pot, combine rice, 3/4 cup water (1 1/2 cups for 4 servings), and a big pinch of salt. Bring to a boil, then cover and reduce to a low simmer. Cook until rice is tender, 15-18 minutes. Keep covered off heat until ready to serve.", "Form meatballs: While rice cooks, in a second large bowl, combine beef*, panko, scallion whites, ginger, remaining soy sauce, salt (we used 3/4 tsp; 1 1/2 tsp for 4 servings), and pepper. Form into 10-12 1 1/2-inch meatballs (20-24 for 4).", "Roast: Place meatballs on one side of a lightly oiled baking sheet. Trim green beans if necessary. Toss on empty side with a drizzle of oil, salt, and pepper. (For 4 servings, divide between 2 sheets; roast meatballs on middle rack and green beans on top rack.) Roast on top rack until meatballs are cooked through and green beans are browned and tender, 14-16 minutes.", "Finish & serve: Fluff rice with a fork; season with salt and pepper. Carefully add meatballs to bowl with sauce; toss to coat. Divide rice between bowls or plates. Top with meatballs and drizzle with any remaining sauce. Serve green beans on the side. Garnish with scallion greens."]'::jsonb, '["HelloFresh", "beef", "meatballs", "Asian", "rice"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'HelloFresh recipe card (WK 6-2). Calories: 770 per serving. Firecracker sauce: "Sweet, savory, and spicy—this sauce is a flavor explosion!" Splish splash tip: Splash cold water on your hands before shaping the meatballs in Step 4. This will make the beef hold on to itself rather than to you. *Ground beef is fully cooked when internal temperature reaches 160°. HelloCustom option: swap the jasmine rice for 12 oz cauliflower rice (24 oz for 4 servings; 660 calories) and use an extra 1 tsp cooking oil. HelloCustom step 3: Heat a drizzle of oil in a small pot over medium-high heat. Add cauliflower rice (no need to drain), a big pinch of salt, and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, until tender and any excess liquid has absorbed, 6-8 minutes. (Save jasmine rice for another use.) 4-person amounts: 2 scallions, 1 thumb ginger, 4 TBSP mayonnaise, 3 TBSP sour cream, 4 tsp honey, 4 TBSP soy sauce, 2 tsp sriracha, 1 cup jasmine rice, 20 oz ground beef, 1/2 cup panko, 12 oz green beans. Both pages of this card were photographed twice (identical photos).

Couldn''t read for sure: step 4 salt amount for 2 servings is faint: read as ''we used 3/4 tsp'' (could be 1/4 tsp); footnote temperature: ''160°'' (small blurry print)', NULL),
('Fluffy Sourdough Pancakes', 'These sourdough pancakes are easy to make with any sourdough starter for a delicious flavor that my two daughters love!', 6, 10, 10, '["1 cup sourdough starter", "1 cup milk", "1 large egg, beaten", "1 tablespoon vegetable oil", "1 1/4 cups all-purpose flour", "2 tablespoons white sugar", "1 teaspoon baking powder", "1/2 teaspoon baking soda", "1/2 teaspoon salt", "cooking spray"]'::jsonb, '["Gather all ingredients.", "Combine sourdough starter, milk, egg, and oil in a bowl,", "Whisk flour, sugar, baking powder, baking soda, and salt together in a separate bowl.", "Stir in sourdough starter mixture until just combined; some lumps are okay.", "Lightly coat a griddle with cooking spray; heat over medium-high heat. Drop batter by 1/4 cupfuls, in batches, onto hot griddle. Cook until bubbles form and edges are dry, about 2 minutes.", "Flip and cook until golden brown, another 2 to 3 minutes. Repeat with remaining batter."]'::jsonb, '["allrecipes", "pancakes", "sourdough", "breakfast"]'::jsonb, '["breakfast"]'::jsonb, 'allrecipes printout, submitted by e_prusia. Yield: 12 pancakes. Total time 20 mins. Handwritten next to the sourdough starter: "240 grams". Nutrition per serving: 223 calories.', NULL),
('Foil Pack: Salsa Verde Chicken & Rice', NULL, 2, 10, 40, '["1 cup instant white rice", "1 1/2 cups water", "2 (7 ounces each) large boneless skinless chicken breasts", "1/2 teaspoon each: cumin, garlic powder, salt and pepper", "1 teaspoon chili powder", "1/8 teaspoon paprika, optional", "1 ounce full fat cream cheese", "6 tablespoons salsa verde", "1/2 cup roasted corn", "1/2 cup black beans", "1/2 cup pepperjack cheese", "Optional: roasted green chiles, lime, cilantro, sour cream, red bell pepper", "cooking spray"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F.", "Generously grease with cooking spray 2 large sheets of heavy duty tin foil.", "Weigh your chicken to get (2) 7-ounce pieces. Pound or slice the pieces to 1/2 inch thickness.", "Toss together the instant rice and water and let stand for 5 minutes.", "In a bowl, toss together all of the seasonings: cumin, garlic powder, salt, pepper, chili powder, and paprika. Dredge each chicken breast evenly in the seasonings (both sides).", "Divide the rice and water mixture evenly among the 2 foil packets.", "Place the seasoned chicken on top.", "Slice the cream cheese into 4 equal pieces and place 2 pieces on top of each chicken breast.", "Pour 3 tablespoons of salsa verde on top of each chicken breast.", "Put 1/4 cup corn and 1/4 cup black beans next to each chicken breast. If desired add a few pieces of thinly sliced red pepper to each packet.", "Seal the packet allowing for expansion and make sure it is 100% sealed.", "Bake for 30-50 minutes** or until the chicken is completely cooked through (registers 165 degrees F)", "Mix everything around in your foil pack and top each with pepperjack cheese.", "Add other optional toppings as desired."]'::jsonb, '["Chelsea''s Messy Apron", "chicken", "rice", "foil pack", "Mexican"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Chelsea''s Messy Apron printout (page 1/2, printed 6/15/2021). Servings: 2 large foil packs; this recipe easily doubles or triples. 626 kcal. Author: Chelsea. Cost $7.72. Total time 50 minutes. Page 2/2 (which probably holds the ** note on bake time) is not in the photos.

Couldn''t read for sure: ''sour cream'' in optional toppings (glare)', 'https://www.chelseasmessyapron.com/foil-pack-creamy-salsa-verde-chicken-rice-veggies/'),
('Fried Sesame Shrimp with Snow Pea Stir-Fry and Rice', NULL, 2, NULL, 35, '["8 oz shrimp", "4 oz snow peas", "1 tsp sriracha", "1/4 cup tempura mix", "1/2 cup panko breadcrumbs", "1 tsp multicolor sesame seeds", "2 garlic cloves", "3/4 cup jasmine rice", "2 fl. oz. garlic sesame sauce", "olive oil", "salt"]'::jsonb, '["Cook the Rice: If using any fresh produce, thoroughly rinse and pat dry. Bring a small pot with rice, a pinch of salt, and 1 1/2 cups water to a boil. Once boiling, reduce to a simmer, cover, and cook until rice is tender, 15-18 minutes. Remove from burner and set aside. While rice cooks, continue recipe.", "Prepare Ingredients and Make Sauce: Trim ends off snow peas and cut into 1\" pieces. Mince garlic. In a mixing bowl, combine garlic sesame sauce and Sriracha (to taste). Set aside. Pat shrimp dry.", "Coat the Shrimp: In another mixing bowl, add tempura mix, 1/4 cup water, and sesame seeds. Stir until a thick batter forms, like pancake batter. Add shrimp to bowl with batter and gently stir to coat. Place panko on a plate. Transfer shrimp to plate with panko and flip until coated, pressing gently to adhere.", "Cook the Shrimp: Line a plate with a paper towel. Heat 3 Tbsp. olive oil in a medium non-stick pan over high heat. Let oil heat, 5 minutes. After 5 minutes, test oil temperature by adding a pinch of batter to it. It should sizzle gently. If it browns immediately, let oil cool. If it doesn''t brown, increase heat. Carefully place shrimp in hot oil and cook until shrimp are golden brown and reach a minimum internal temperature of 145 degrees, 2-4 minutes per side. Remove from burner. Transfer shrimp to towel-lined plate.", "Cook Stir-Fry and Finish Dish: Place a large non-stick pan over medium-high heat and add 2 tsp. olive oil. Add snow peas and garlic to hot pan. Stir occasionally until snow peas are tender, 3-4 minutes. Remove from burner. Plate dish as pictured on front of card, topping rice with snow peas, shrimp, and sauce (to taste). Bon appétit!"]'::jsonb, '["Home Chef", "shrimp", "seafood", "Asian", "stir-fry", "rice"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Home Chef recipe card (Meal Kit), www.homechef.com/24891. Difficulty: Expert. Spice level: Medium. Cook within 3 days. Customize It Options (default is 8 oz Shrimp): 12 oz Boneless Skinless Chicken Breasts. Customize It Instructions: If using chicken breasts, pat dry, and, on a separate cutting board, cut into 1" dice. Follow same instructions as shrimp in Steps 3 and 4, cooking until chicken reaches minimum internal temperature, 5-7 minutes.

Couldn''t read for sure: step 1 heading obscured by glare; ''Cook the Rice'' is a best guess; rice water: best reading ''1 1/2 cups''; step 3: ''flip until coated, pressing gently to adhere'' partly obscured (best reading); step 4: ''by adding a pinch of batter'' partly obscured (best reading)', NULL),
('Garlic Bread', NULL, NULL, NULL, 20, '["1 cup + 2 tbls. water", "3 cups + 2 tbls. flour", "1 1/2 tbls. sugar", "3/4 tsp. salt", "3/4 tbls. butter", "3 tbls Parmesan", "3/4 tsp. sweet basil", "3/4 tsp. garlic powder", "3/4 tsp. garlic paste", "1 tsp yeast"]'::jsonb, '["Bake at 375° for 20 min."]'::jsonb, '["bread", "garlic", "bread machine", "side", "handwritten"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten in a spiral recipe notebook (looks like bread-machine amounts). Heading reads "Garlic..." with "375° 20 min" beside it; the word after "Garlic" is faded. On the sweet basil and garlic powder lines, "tbls" was crossed out and "tsp" written above. A stray "375" is written between this recipe and Classic White. Faint bleed-through from another page (potato bread?) is visible on the right but not readable.

Couldn''t read for sure: title: heading reads "Garlic" followed by a faded word (best reading "Garlic Bread")', NULL),
('Garlic Butter Chicken with Zucchini, Corn, and Ravioli', 'Let me introduce you to my family''s new favorite chicken dinner - Garlic Butter Chicken with Zucchini, Corn, and Ravioli. This recipe has everything: protein, veggies, and carbs! It''s a super easy and delicious meal that is worthy of consideration for your monthly dinner rotation! Perfect for frozen or refrigerated (store-bought) ravioli!', 4, 15, 15, '["8 oz ravioli store-bought (frozen or refrigerated)", "2 tablespoons olive oil", "2 zucchini medium, sliced", "salt and pepper to taste", "1.5 cups corn kernels cooked (about 3 corn ears - corn on the cob)", "1 lb chicken breasts skinless, boneless, sliced", "1/2 teaspoon smoked paprika or more", "1/2 teaspoon chili powder or more", "1/4 teaspoon salt or to taste", "black pepper freshly ground, to taste", "2 tablespoons olive oil", "5 cloves garlic minced", "2 tablespoons freshly squeezed lime juice or more", "4 tablespoons butter divided", "fresh cilantro chopped"]'::jsonb, '["Cook ravioli: Bring a large pot of water to boil. Cook ravioli according to package instructions (usually 7 to 10 minutes). Drain.", "Cook ravioli: While you wait for the water to start boiling and while the ravioli is cooking, proceed with the rest of the recipe.", "Prepare the vegetables: Heat olive oil in a large, high-sided cast-iron skillet over medium heat until hot. Add sliced zucchini. Sprinkle with a pinch of salt and freshly ground black pepper. Cook for about 3 minutes on medium heat. Flip the veggies once. Remove cooked zucchini to a plate.", "Make Garlic Butter Chicken: Slice the chicken breasts into strips. Season the chicken with smoked paprika, chili powder, salt, and freshly ground black pepper.", "Make Garlic Butter Chicken: Heat 2 tablespoons of olive oil on medium heat in the same, now empty, cast-iron skillet. Add the chicken in one layer and cook, undisturbed, for about 4 minutes.", "Make Garlic Butter Chicken: Flip the chicken strips over, add minced garlic, and cook for 2 more minutes. Lower the heat to low and add freshly squeezed lime juice and 2 tablespoons of butter. Cook for another 2 minutes or more, frequently stirring, until the chicken is cooked through but not overcooked and the garlic has softened.", "Assembly: Add cooked sliced zucchini, and cooked corn kernels to the same skillet with cooked chicken.", "Assembly: Add 2 remaining tablespoons of butter and melt it on low heat, stirring it together with the veggies. Do it rather quickly, for a couple of minutes, just until the butter melts and the garlic butter sauce coats both the chicken and the zucchini and corn evenly. Remove from heat.", "Assembly: Add cooked and drained ravioli, and coat them with the butter sauce and veggies. Remove from heat.", "Assembly: Season with more salt, smoked paprika, and chili powder, if desired. Add more freshly squeezed lime juice, if desired.", "Assembly: When serving, top with the chopped fresh cilantro. Sprinkle a small amount of chili powder over chicken and ravioli, for presentation purposes, if desired."]'::jsonb, '["Julia''s Album", "chicken", "pasta", "ravioli", "American", "skillet"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Julia''s Album web printout, 2 pages (author Julia). Course: Main Course; Cuisine: American; 609 kcal per serving. Ingredient groups: Pasta (ravioli), Veggies (olive oil, zucchini, salt and pepper, corn), Garlic Butter Chicken (chicken through butter), Garnish (cilantro).

Couldn''t read for sure: description "Garlic Butter Chicken", "protein, veggies, and carbs" and "your monthly dinner rotation" partly under glare ("monthly" could be another word); "8 oz ravioli store-bought (frozen or refrigerated)" - "frozen" under glare; Prepare the vegetables: "cast-iron skillet", "freshly ground", "once. Remove" partly under glare; Assembly 1: "cooked corn kernels" partly under glare; Assembly 2: "and melt it", "for a couple of minutes", "the chicken and the zucchini" under glare; Assembly 3: "coat them with" partly under glare', 'https://juliasalbum.com/chicken-zucchini-corn-ravioli/'),
('General Tso''s Chicken with Bok Choy & Jasmine Rice', 'In this quick-cooking spin on a takeout favorite, hoisin sauce, honey, sambal oelek, and sesame oil lend our chicken the sweet, spicy, and nutty flavors for which General Tso''s is known. A light dusting of cornstarch on the chicken just before it hits the pan creates a delicately crispy exterior (and helps it soak up the irresistible sauce later).', 4, NULL, 25, '["1 1/8 lbs chopped chicken breast", "1 cup jasmine rice", "2 Tbsps apple cider vinegar", "1 Tbsp honey", "1/2 cup Asian-style sautéed aromatics", "15 oz baby bok choy", "1/4 cup hoisin sauce", "1/4 cup cornstarch", "1 Tbsp sambal oelek", "1 Tbsp sesame oil"]'::jsonb, '["Cook the rice: Remove the honey from the refrigerator to bring to room temperature. In a medium pot, combine the rice, a big pinch of salt, and 2 cups of water. Heat to boiling on high. Once boiling, reduce the heat to low. Cover and cook, without stirring, 12 to 14 minutes, or until the water has been absorbed and the rice is tender. Turn off the heat and fluff with a fork.", "Prepare the bok choy & make the sauce: While the rice cooks, wash and dry the bok choy; cut off and discard the root end, then roughly chop the leaves and stems. In a bowl, whisk together the hoisin sauce, vinegar, honey (kneading the packet before opening), sesame oil, and as much of the sambal oelek as you''d like, depending on how spicy you''d like the dish to be.", "Coat & cook the chicken: While the rice continues to cook, pat the chicken dry with paper towels. Place in a large bowl and season with salt and pepper. Add the cornstarch and toss to thoroughly coat. In a large pan (nonstick, if you have one), heat the sautéed aromatics on medium-high until hot. Add the coated chicken in an even layer. Cook, without stirring, 3 to 4 minutes, or until lightly browned. Continue to cook, stirring occasionally, 3 to 4 minutes, or until browned and cooked through.", "Finish & serve your dish: Add the chopped bok choy to the pan; season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, 1 to 2 minutes, or until slightly softened. Add the sauce. Cook, stirring frequently, 1 to 2 minutes, or until thoroughly combined and the sauce is slightly thickened. Turn off the heat. Serve the finished chicken, bok choy, and sauce over the cooked rice. Enjoy!"]'::jsonb, '["Blue Apron", "chicken", "Chinese", "rice", "stir-fry"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Blue Apron recipe card. Wine match: Crisp & Minerally. Did You Know? (sautéed aromatics): A mix of scallions, ginger, and garlic help to quickly build layers of flavor in this dish. Steps also use salt and pepper.

Couldn''t read for sure: step 4 heading is faded: read as ''Finish & serve your dish''', NULL),
('General Tso''s Chicken with Gai Lan & Jasmine Rice', 'In this quick-cooking spin on a takeout favorite, hoisin sauce, honey, sambal oelek, and sesame oil lend our chicken the sweet, spicy, and nutty flavors for which General Tso''s is known. It''s all served over a simple bed of jasmine rice, which is perfect for catching any extra bites of sauce.', 4, NULL, 30, '["1 1/2 lbs chicken tenders", "1 cup jasmine rice", "1 Tbsp rice vinegar", "1 Tbsp honey", "1/2 cup Asian-style sautéed aromatics", "3/4 lb gai lan", "1/4 cup hoisin sauce", "3/4 cup cornstarch", "1 Tbsp sambal oelek", "1 Tbsp sesame oil", "oil", "salt", "pepper"]'::jsonb, '["Cook the rice: Remove the honey from the refrigerator to bring to room temperature. In a medium pot, combine the rice, a big pinch of salt, and 2 cups of water. Heat to boiling on high. Once boiling, reduce the heat to low. Cover and cook, without stirring, 12 to 14 minutes, or until the water has been absorbed and the rice is tender. Turn off the heat and fluff with a fork.", "Prepare the gai lan & start the sauce: Meanwhile, wash and dry the gai lan; cut off and discard the bottom 1/2 inch of the stems. Thinly slice the stems and roughly chop the leaves, keeping them separate. In a bowl, whisk together the hoisin sauce, vinegar, honey (kneading the packet before opening), sesame oil, 2 tablespoons of warm water, and as much of the sambal oelek as you''d like, depending on how spicy you''d like the dish to be.", "Coat & cook the chicken: Pat the chicken dry with paper towels. Place in a large bowl and season with salt and pepper. Add the cornstarch; toss to thoroughly coat. In a large pan (nonstick, if you have one), heat a thin layer of oil on medium-high. Once the oil is hot enough that a pinch of cornstarch sizzles immediately when added, add the coated chicken (shaking off any excess cornstarch before adding). Cook 3 to 5 minutes per side, or until browned and cooked through. Leaving any browned bits (or fond) in the pan, transfer to a paper towel-lined plate.", "Finish & serve your dish: To the pan of reserved fond, add the sliced gai lan stems and sautéed aromatics; season with salt and pepper. Cook on medium-high, stirring occasionally, 1 to 2 minutes, or until slightly softened. Add the chopped gai lan leaves and sauce (carefully, as the liquid may splatter). Cook, stirring frequently, 1 to 2 minutes, or until combined and the sauce is slightly thickened. Add the cooked chicken. Cook, stirring constantly, 1 to 2 minutes, or until coated and combined. Turn off the heat. Taste, then season with salt and pepper if desired. Serve the finished chicken and sauce over the cooked rice. Enjoy!"]'::jsonb, '["Blue Apron", "chicken", "Chinese", "Asian", "rice", "stir-fry"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Blue Apron recipe card. Time: 20-30 minutes. Did You Know? The Asian-style sautéed aromatics mix includes garlic, ginger, onions, and scallions. Wine pairing: Zesty & Tropical.

Couldn''t read for sure: cornstarch ''3/4 cup'' (fraction blurry; could be 1/4); hoisin sauce ''1/4 cup'' (fraction blurry); gai lan ''3/4 lb'' (fraction blurry); wine pairing ''Zesty & Tropical'' (faded)', NULL),
