('Graham Cracker Crust I', '"Remember this recipe when you want to whip up your favorite chocolate, coconut custard or banana cream pie. Butter, graham cracker crumbs and sugar are perfectly balanced in this recipe. And the mixture presses nicely into a pie pan, and can be pre-baked or just chilled."', 8, 10, 7, '["1 1/2 cups finely ground graham cracker crumbs", "1/3 cup white sugar", "6 tablespoons butter, melted", "1/2 teaspoon ground cinnamon (optional)"]'::jsonb, '["Mix graham cracker crumbs, sugar, melted butter or margarine, and cinnamon until well blended. Press mixture into an 8 or 9 inch pie plate.", "Bake at 375 degrees F (190 degrees C) for 7 minutes. Cool. If recipe calls for unbaked pie shell, just chill for about 1 hour."]'::jsonb, '["allrecipes.com", "pie crust", "dessert", "baking"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Allrecipes.com printout. Submitted by Carol. Ready in 17 minutes.', NULL),
('Green Beans', NULL, NULL, NULL, 20, '["1 1/2 cups of green beans (2 cans)", "2 tbls. butter", "2 tablespoon flour", "1 teaspoon sugar", "1 1/4 teaspoon pepper", "1 teaspoon onion", "1 cup sour cream", "1/2 lb. Swiss cheese", "2 cups of corn flakes", "2 tbls. melted butter"]'::jsonb, '["Drain beans, melt butter, [add] flour, sugar, pepper and onion. Add to [sour cream and beans]. Sprinkle cheese then corn flakes. Bake 400° for 20 min."]'::jsonb, '["green beans", "side", "casserole", "vegetable"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten notebook page (Evernote printout dated 2/3/2021), above Colorful Kielbasa. Glare covers the middle of the directions; bracketed words are guesses from context. The corn flakes are presumably tossed with the 2 tbls. melted butter.

