('Green Chile', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["2 pkg. of lean pork steak cubed & fat removed", "1/4 cup of flour", "1 can split pea soup", "1 can of Ortega tomato & green chiles", "1 or 2 cans of green chiles chopped", "garlic salt", "salt & pepper to taste", "oregano", "1 can of water", "1 small can of tomato sauce or V-8 juice"]'::jsonb, '["Brown pork in fat. Mix 1/4 cup of flour near the end of browning, stir in 1 can split pea soup, 1 can of Ortega tomato & green chiles, 1 or 2 cans of green chiles chopped. Sprinkle garlic salt & salt & pepper to taste. Sprinkle with oregano. 1 can of water, 1 small can of tomato sauce or V-8 juice."]'::jsonb, '["pork", "green chile", "stew", "Mexican"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten card taped in the notebook. Handwritten in different ink with an arrow pointing at the garlic salt: "real garlic".', NULL),
('Green Chile Con Queso', NULL, NULL, NULL, 30, '["1 medium size onion chopped", "1 clove garlic, minced or 1/4 teas garlic powder", "2 tablespoons fat", "big can of taco sauce", "1/2 c. evaporated milk", "1 lb. of jalepano Kraft cheese"]'::jsonb, '["Combine garlic, onion & fat in top portion of double boiler. Cook at medium heat until onion is transparent.", "Add taco sauce & bring to a boil.", "Remove from heat & add milk & cheese. Reduce heat, simmer 1/2 hr.", "Cool to room temp. & serve."]'::jsonb, '["appetizer", "dip", "queso", "cheese", "Tex-Mex", "handwritten"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe card ("From the kitchen of:" left blank).', NULL),
('Grilled Fish Tacos with Chipotle-Lime Dressing', 'I came up with this recipe when I couldn''t find good directions for grilled fish tacos. I liked the chipotle-lime combination in a dip I once tried so I imitated it here. Choose toppings to suit your taste, or include typical accompaniments such as salsa fresca, cabbage, a squeeze of lime juice, and chopped cilantro.', NULL, 35, 9, '["1/4 cup extra virgin olive oil", "2 tablespoons distilled white vinegar", "2 tablespoons fresh lime juice", "2 teaspoons lime zest", "1 1/2 teaspoons honey", "2 cloves garlic, minced", "1/2 teaspoon cumin", "1/2 teaspoon chili powder", "1 teaspoon seafood seasoning, such as Old Bay(TM)", "1/2 teaspoon ground black pepper", "1 teaspoon hot pepper sauce, or to taste", "1 pound tilapia fillets, cut into chunks", "1 (8 ounce) container light sour cream", "1/2 cup adobo sauce from chipotle peppers", "2 tablespoons fresh lime juice", "2 teaspoons lime zest", "1/4 teaspoon cumin", "1/4 teaspoon chili powder", "1/2 teaspoon seafood seasoning, such as Old Bay(TM)", "salt and pepper to taste", "1 (10 ounce) package tortillas", "3 ripe tomatoes, seeded and diced", "1 bunch cilantro, chopped", "1 small head cabbage, cored and shredded", "2 limes, cut in wedges"]'::jsonb, '["To make the marinade, whisk together the olive oil, vinegar, lime juice, lime zest, honey, garlic, cumin, chili powder, seafood seasoning, black pepper, and hot sauce in a bowl until blended. Place the tilapia in a shallow dish, and pour the marinade over the fish. Cover, and refrigerate 6 to 8 hours.", "To make the dressing, combine the sour cream and adobo sauce in a bowl. Stir in the lime juice, lime zest, cumin, chili powder, seafood seasoning. Add salt, and pepper in desired amounts. Cover, and refrigerate until needed.", "Preheat an outdoor grill for high heat and lightly oil grate. Set grate 4 inches from the heat.", "Remove fish from marinade, drain off any excess and discard marinade. Grill fish pieces until easily flaked with a fork, turning once, about 9 minutes.", "Assemble tacos by placing fish pieces in the center of tortillas with desired amounts of tomatoes, cilantro, and cabbage; drizzle with dressing. To serve, roll up tortillas around fillings, and garnish with lime wedges."]'::jsonb, '["Allrecipes", "fish", "tilapia", "tacos", "Mexican", "grilled"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Allrecipes printout (page 1 of 2), recipe by Mary Dohrmann. Ingredients are grouped: first 12 = Marinade, next 8 = Dressing, last 5 = Toppings. Ready in 6 h 44 m (includes 6-8 hours marinating). The print URL says servings=6, but no yield is printed on the page. Page 2 of the printout is not in the photos; all 5 directions are on page 1.

Couldn''t read for sure: prep time label obscured; read as Prep 35 m; marinade "such as Old Bay(TM)" partly obscured by glare; step 1 "Place the tilapia in" partly obscured; step 2 "lime zest" partly obscured', 'http://allrecipes.com/recipe/142614/grilled-fish-tacos-with-chipotle-lime-dressing/print/?recipeType=Recipe&servings=6'),
