('Mexican Chicken Salad Sandwiches', 'Make lunch spectacular with MEXICAN CHICKEN SALAD SANDWICHES! This easy twist on a classic is sure to please everyone at the table. Chicken salad loaded with taco seasoning, green chiles, corn, peppers, enchilada sauce, and more. SO GOOD!', 4, 10, NULL, '["1 1/2 lb cooked shredded chicken breast", "3/4 cup low fat mayonnaise", "1/4 cup enchilada sauce", "1/2 ounce taco seasoning", "1 3.5 ounce can green chiles", "1 cup cooked corn", "1 orange pepper diced", "1/2 red onion diced", "1/4 cup fresh cilantro chopped", "1 tablespoon fresh lime juice"]'::jsonb, '["Place cooked shredded chicken in a large bowl and add in all other ingredients. Stir to fully combine. Add a bit more mayo if needed for texture.", "Eat in a wrap, on a croissant, on toasted bread, or by itself; the sky is the limit!", "Enjoy"]'::jsonb, '["The Cookie Rookie", "chicken", "sandwich", "chicken salad", "Mexican", "no cook"]'::jsonb, '["lunch"]'::jsonb, 'From The Cookie Rookie (web printout, printed 6/1/2021). Author: Becky Hardin - The Cookie Rookie. Course: Main Course. Cuisine: Mexican. Total time 10 minutes. The taco seasoning line says ''Click for Homemade Recipe!''. Nutrition: Calories 475kcal | Carbohydrates 18g | Protein 48g | Fat 23g | Saturated Fat 5g | Cholesterol 170mg | Sodium 1322mg | Potassium 660mg | Fiber 2g | Sugar 6g | Vitamin A 810IU | Vitamin C 30.4mg | Calcium 34mg | Iron 1.6mg.

Couldn''t read for sure: ''1 orange pepper diced'': middle hidden by a stain (only ''1 ora... ...er diced'' shows); could be ''orange bell pepper''; ''1/2 red onion diced'': the amount and ''red'' are hidden by a stain; ''1/4 cup fresh cilantro'': the fraction is partly hidden; description ''everyone at the table'' and ''enchilada sauce'' partly hidden', 'https://www.thecookierookie.com/mexican-chicken-salad-sandwiches/'),
('Mexican Chicken with Cheese Sauce', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["4 boneless, skinless chicken breasts", "1 tablespoon olive oil", "1 teaspoon chili powder", "1 teaspoon ground cumin", "1 teaspoon garlic powder", "1 teaspoon onion powder", "salt and pepper to taste", "1 cup shredded Mexican cheese blend", "1/2 cup diced tomatoes", "1/4 cup chopped fresh cilantro", "lime wedges for garnish"]'::jsonb, '["Prepare the Chicken: Season the chicken breasts with chili powder, cumin, garlic powder, onion powder, salt, and pepper.", "Cook the Chicken: In a skillet, heat olive oil over medium heat. Add the seasoned chicken breasts and cook until golden brown and cooked through, about 6-8 minutes per side. Remove from skillet and set aside.", "Make the Cheese Sauce: In the same skillet, reduce the heat to low and add the shredded Mexican cheese blend. Stir until melted and smooth."]'::jsonb, '["cookiespedia", "chicken", "Mexican", "cheese sauce", "skillet"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from cookiespedia.com (pages 2 and 3 of 10). Handwritten on page 2 above the photo: "Mexican chicken with cheese sauce" (the title). Photo caption, partly washed out: "This recipe combines juicy, flavorful chicken with a creamy, decadent cheese sauce, creating a delicious and satisfying [Mexican-]inspired dish." Only directions 1-3 are on these pages; the remaining steps (pages 4+) are not in the photos.

Couldn''t read for sure: photo caption is partly washed out; ''juicy'', ''cheese sauce'', ''satisfying Mexican-inspired'' are best readings; ingredient ''1 cup shredded Mexican cheese blend'': ''cheese'' partly washed out

