('Mexican Corn Salad', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 red onion (chopped)", "1 green pepper (chopped)", "2 can whole kernel corn (drained)", "3/4 c mayo", "2 t sugar", "1 1/2 t. creole seasoning", "1 10 oz. bag chili cheese Fritos", "2 cups shredded cheese"]'::jsonb, '["Mix well.", "Just before serving add a 10 oz. bag of chili cheese Fritos and 2 cups of shredded cheese. Yummy."]'::jsonb, '["salad", "corn", "side", "Mexican"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten card on an Evernote printout (page 2 of 3).', NULL),
('Mexican Pizza', NULL, 3, 30, NULL, '["1 pound lean ground beef", "1 packet (1 ounce) taco seasoning", "1/2 cup water", "6 medium-size flour tortillas", "1 can (16 ounces) refried beans", "1 can (10 ounces) red enchilada sauce", "1 cup shredded cheddar cheese", "1 cup shredded pepper-jack cheese", "1 Roma tomato diced", "1 green onion diced", "1 small can sliced black olives", "non-stick spray"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat oven to 375 degrees F. Take 2 baking sheets and spray them with non-stick spray. Place 3 tortillas on each baking sheet. Place in the oven and bake for 3 to 5 minutes, then carefully flip tortillas over while they''re still in the oven (*don''t burn yourself please*) and bake another 2 to 5 minutes to crisp on the other side. You want tortillas a slight golden color. Remove from oven and set aside.", "Meanwhile, cook and crumble ground beef in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Drain grease. Add taco seasoning and water. Bring mixture to a boil, then reduce heat to medium-low. Stir and simmer for 10 minutes. Remove from heat.", "In a microwave-safe bowl, heat the refried beans until warmed through. Spread a thin layer of beans on one tortilla. Top with 1/3 of the meat mixture. Place another tortilla on top of the meat. Spread 3 Tablespoons of enchilada sauce on top of the top tortilla. Sprinkle with some cheddar cheese and pepper-jack cheese. Add a few dices of tomato, green onion and olives.", "Repeat process with the remaining tortillas. You will have 3 Mexican pizzas total.", "Place pizzas on the baking sheet and bake for 5 minutes, or until cheese is melted and bubbly. Remove from oven and let stand to cool slightly before slicing and serving. Enjoy ♥"]'::jsonb, '["Life In The Lofthouse", "beef", "Mexican", "pizza", "tortillas"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from Life In The Lofthouse (1 page). Prep Time 30 minutes, Total Time 30 minutes. Author: Holly. Rated 5 from 4 votes. Some words in steps 1-3 are washed out on the printout (see uncertain list).

Couldn''t read for sure: step 1: ''spray them'' (''them'' washed out); step 2: ''over medium-high heat'' and ''boil, then reduce heat'' partly washed out; step 3: ''warmed through. Spread a thin layer'', ''Place another tortilla on top of the meat'', ''top tortilla. Sprinkle with some'', ''tomato'' partly washed out (best readings)', 'https://life-in-the-lofthouse.com/mexican-pizza/'),
('Mexican-Spiced Pork Roast with Caramelized Onion, Spinach & Black Beans', 'To contrast the bold spices that coat our rich pork roast, we''re serving it alongside a duo of black beans and caramelized onion—or onion cooked slowly to brown its natural sugars, which adds incredible depth of flavor. A side of tender sweet peppers and onion (roasted with the pork) gives the dish an extra vibrant boost.', 4, NULL, 55, '["1 pork roast", "1/2 lb sweet peppers", "5 oz baby spinach", "2 scallions", "2 tsps honey", "2 Tbsps rice vinegar", "1 15.5-oz can black beans", "1 red onion", "2 cloves garlic", "2 Tbsps butter", "1 Tbsp Mexican spice blend (ancho chile powder, smoked paprika, garlic powder, ground cumin & dried Mexican oregano)"]'::jsonb, '["Prepare & start the pork: Remove the honey from the refrigerator to bring to room temperature. Place an oven rack in the center of the oven, then preheat to 450°F. Line a sheet pan with foil. Pat the pork dry with paper towels. Season on all sides with salt, pepper, and enough of the spice blend to coat (you may have extra). Place on one side of the sheet pan. Roast 25 minutes. Leaving the oven on, remove from the oven.", "Prepare the remaining ingredients: Meanwhile, wash and dry the fresh produce. Halve and peel the onion; small dice one half, then cut the other half into 1-inch-wide wedges, separating the layers. Cut off and discard the stems of the peppers; remove the cores, then quarter lengthwise. Combine the onion wedges and quartered peppers in a medium bowl. Drain and rinse the beans. Peel and roughly chop 2 cloves of garlic. Thinly slice the scallions, separating the white bottoms and green tops. Combine the chopped garlic and sliced white bottoms of the scallions in a bowl.", "Caramelize the onion: In a large pan (nonstick, if you have one), heat the butter on medium-high until melted. Add the diced onion; season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, 3 to 4 minutes, or until lightly browned. Add half the honey (kneading before opening) and 1/2 cup of water (carefully, as it may splatter). Cook, stirring occasionally, 5 to 7 minutes, or until thickened. Transfer to a bowl. Wipe out the pan.", "Roast the vegetables & pork: To the bowl of prepared onion and peppers, add a drizzle of olive oil; season with salt and pepper. Stir to coat. Carefully transfer to the other side of the sheet pan of partially roasted pork. Roast 11 to 13 minutes, or until the vegetables are tender and the pork is cooked through.* Remove from the oven. Transfer the pork to a cutting board and let rest at least 5 minutes.", "Cook the beans: Meanwhile, in the same pan, heat 1 teaspoon of olive oil on medium-high until hot. Add the prepared garlic and white bottoms of the scallions; season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring frequently, 30 seconds to 1 minute, or until slightly softened. Add the drained beans. Cook, stirring frequently, 1 to 2 minutes, or until heated through. Add the vinegar (carefully, as it may splatter), remaining honey, and 1/4 cup of water; season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, 3 to 4 minutes, or until the water has cooked off.", "Finish & serve your dish: To the pan of cooked beans, add the spinach and caramelized onion. Cook on medium-high, stirring constantly, 30 seconds to 1 minute, or until the spinach is slightly wilted. Turn off the heat. Taste, then season with salt and pepper if desired. Find the lines of muscle (or grain) on the rested pork; thinly slice crosswise against the grain. Serve the sliced pork with the finished beans and roasted vegetables. Garnish with the sliced green tops of the scallions. Enjoy!"]'::jsonb, '["Blue Apron", "pork", "Mexican", "roast", "carb conscious", "WW approved"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Blue Apron recipe card. Marked WW Approved and Carb Conscious. Wine match: Fruity & Savory. *An instant-read thermometer should register 145°F. Steps also use olive oil, salt and pepper (not in the printed ingredient list).', NULL),
('Million Dollar Ravioli Casserole', 'Million Dollar Ravioli Casserole - seriously delicious! Meat sauce, frozen ravioli, and 4 cheeses! The BEST pasta casserole EVER!!! Can make ahead and refrigerate or freeze for later. Frozen cheese ravioli, cream cheese, sour cream, cottage cheese, Italian sausage, spaghetti sauce, parmesan cheese and mozzarella cheese. Serve with a simple salad and garlic bread. Great for dinner parties and potlucks! Everyone loves this easy casserole! I never have any leftovers!! #casserole #pasta #freezermeal', 8, 15, 45, '["1 lb Italian sausage", "1 (28-oz) jar spaghetti sauce", "1 cup cottage cheese", "1 (8-oz) package cream cheese softened", "1/4 cup sour cream", "2 Tbsp parsley", "1/2 tsp garlic powder", "1/3 cup grated parmesan cheese", "1 (25-oz) package frozen cheese ravioli", "2 cups mozzarella cheese", "cooking spray"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat oven to 350°F. Spray a 9x13x2-inch pan with cooking spray. Set aside.", "In a large skillet brown Italian sausage. Drain fat from skillet. Stir in spaghetti sauce and set aside.", "In a large bowl, combine cottage cheese, softened cream cheese, sour cream, parmesan cheese, parsley and garlic powder. Add ravioli. Toss to coast.", "Spread ravioli in the bottom of the prepared baking pan.", "Pour meat sauce over ravioli and top with mozzarella cheese.", "Bake uncovered for 45 minutes. Allow to cool for 10-15 minutes before serving."]'::jsonb, '["Plain Chicken", "sausage", "pasta", "casserole", "Italian", "freezer meal"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from Plain Chicken (2 pages). Equipment: 9x13-inch baking dish. Recipe notes: Can make the casserole in advance and refrigerate or freeze for later. If baking straight from the refrigerator, you may need to add a few minutes to the cooking time. To bake after freezing, thaw completely and bake as directed above.

Couldn''t read for sure: sourceUrl read from slightly blurry page-2 text: https://www.plainchicken.com/million-dollar-ravioli-casserole/', 'https://www.plainchicken.com/million-dollar-ravioli-casserole/'),
('Mini Pineapple Upside Down Cakes', 'This is such an easy dessert recipe that is simple enough to make at the last minute on a weeknight but beautiful (and DELICIOUS!) enough to serve to guests!', 18, 15, 25, '["2 cans pineapple slices (20 ounce cans)", "1/3 cup butter, melted", "2/3 cup brown sugar", "maraschino cherries, cut in half", "1 box yellow cake mix", "non-stick cooking spray"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat the oven to 350F. Spray the muffin tins with non-stick cooking spray. Open the cans of pineapple and save the juice.", "Mix together the melted butter and brown sugar until combined. Add a spoonful of the mixture to the bottom of each muffin cup, distributing it evenly.", "Prepare the cake mix according to the package directions except instead of water, use the juice from the canned pineapple.", "Add a well drained pineapple slice to the bottom of each muffin cup. Place half a maraschino cherry in the middle of each pineapple slice with the cut side facing up.", "Add about 1/4 cup to 1/3 cup of cake batter into each muffin cup.", "Bake at 350F for 20 to 25 minutes or until the tops have turned golden and a toothpick comes out clean.", "Pull them out of the oven and let them cool for 5 minutes. Loosen the edges if needed, then place a cookie sheet on top of the muffin pan and carefully flip them over so the mini cakes come out onto the cookie sheet."]'::jsonb, '["One Little Project", "dessert", "cake", "pineapple", "cake mix"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from One Little Project (printed 2/8/2021). Recipe notes: You NEED to use a jumbo muffin pan for this recipe - a regular muffin pan is not big enough. This recipe makes enough for 18 mini cakes. Alternatively, if you don''t have enough jumbo muffin pans to make 18, you can also make 6 mini upside down cakes and one 9 inch round upside down cake.', 'https://onelittleproject.com/mini-pineapple-upside-down-cakes/'),
('Mint Oreo Brownies', 'Mint Oreo Brownies are stuffed with mint Oreos, topped with mint frosting, and sprinkled with more crushed Oreo''s and a gooey fudge drizzle.', 24, 30, 30, '["1/2 cup butter", "1/2 cup oil", "2 cups granulated sugar", "4 eggs", "2 teaspoons vanilla", "1/4 teaspoon mint extract", "2/3 cup cocoa powder", "1 cup all purpose flour", "1/2 teaspoon salt", "1/2 teaspoon baking powder", "1 15.5 ounce package Mint Oreos", "1/2 cup butter, softened (mint buttercream)", "1 3/4 cups powdered sugar (mint buttercream)", "1-2 tablespoons heavy cream or milk (mint buttercream)", "1/4 to 1/2 teaspoon mint extract (mint buttercream)", "a few drops green food coloring (mint buttercream)", "3 tablespoons butter (fudge drizzle)", "3 tablespoons cocoa powder (fudge drizzle)", "1 tablespoon corn syrup or honey (fudge drizzle)", "1/2 cup powder sugar (fudge drizzle)", "1-2 tablespoons milk or heavy cream (fudge drizzle)"]'::jsonb, '["To make the brownies, preheat oven to 350 F. Grease and flour a 9 x 13 inch pan. Melt the butter in a large microwave safe bowl. Whisk in the oil, sugar, eggs, vanilla and mint extracts. Beat in the cocoa, flour, salt and baking powder. Spread half the batter into the prepared pan, layer on 24 whole mint oreos and spread the second half of the batter on half. Bake for 25-30 minutes or until an inserted toothpick comes out with a few crumbs. Let cool completely.", "To make the mint buttercream layer, beat the butter in a stand mixer for 1-2 minutes, beat in the powdered sugar. Add enough of the milk or cream to be a spreadable consistency and the mint extract to your tastes. Spread on top of cooled brownies.", "Gently crush the remaining oreos in the package and sprinkle on top of the frosted brownies.", "to make the fudge drizzle, melt the butter in a medium microwave safe bowl. Stir in the cocoa powder, corn syrup, powdered sugar, and enough milk or heavy cream to make a smooth consistency. Microwave to 20 seconds and stir. Drizzle on top of cooled brownies. I put mine into a ziploc bag and cut the corner off for a more controlled drizzle. Let cool and cut into bars."]'::jsonb, '["Chocolate with Grace", "dessert", "brownies", "mint", "Oreo", "chocolate", "American"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from Chocolate with Grace (printed 11/8/21), 2 pages. Additional time 40 mins; total time 1 hr 40 mins. Nutrition per brownie: 238 kcal, carbohydrates 26g, protein 2g, fat 15g, saturated fat 7g, polyunsaturated fat 2g, monounsaturated fat 6g, trans fat 1g, cholesterol 51mg, sodium 149mg, potassium 69mg, fiber 1g, sugar 19g, vitamin A 321IU, calcium 18mg, iron 1mg.', 'https://chocolatewithgrace.com/mint-oreo-brownies/'),
('Mom''s Bread', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1/2 cup sugar", "1 cube butter (1/2 c.)", "3 eggs", "3 cups milk", "2 pkgs. yeast", "about 3 cups flour, plus more to work dough", "3 teas. salt"]'::jsonb, '["Cream 1/2 cup sugar and 1 cube butter (1/2 c.). Add 3 eggs.", "Warm 3 cups milk, add 2 pkgs. of yeast and dissolve. Add to creamed sugar & eggs, mix.", "Add just enough dough about 3 cups. Cover, let rice to the top of the mixer bowl.", "Add 3 teas. of salt & flour to work dough."]'::jsonb, '["bread", "yeast bread", "family recipe"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten in a spiral recipe notebook. From Mom. ''Add just enough dough about 3 cups'' presumably means flour; ''let rice'' = let rise. Written further down the same page: ''2 pkgs of yeast = to 4 1/2 tsp of yeast of the loose pkg.'' No baking time/temperature given.', NULL),
('Mom''s Cinnamon Rolls', NULL, NULL, NULL, 20, '["1/2 cup butter", "1/2 cup sugar", "3 eggs", "3 cups milk", "2 pkgs. yeast (or 2 tblsp. of yeast from a jar)", "4-5 cups flour, plus enough flour to start kneading", "3 teas. salt"]'::jsonb, '["Cream 1/2 cup butter and 1/2 cup sugar. Add 3 eggs & beat.", "Heat 3 cups milk to (105-115°), add 2 pkgs. yeast or 2 tblsp. of yeast from a jar. Mix until totally dissolved. Add enough flour while mixer is running 4-5 cups just enough to make a creamy mixture, cover, let rise to top of bowl. Turn mixer on and add 3 teas. of salt and enough flour to start kneading. Let rise until doubles in size.", "Bake 375° for 20 min."]'::jsonb, '["bread", "cinnamon rolls", "baking", "breakfast", "family recipe"]'::jsonb, '["breakfast"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe from a spiral recipe notebook ("Mom''s" recipe). The page ends with "over" - the back of the page (probably shaping, filling and/or icing instructions) is not in the photos.

A page of this recipe was missing from the photos.', NULL),
('Mrs. Lantz''s Blackberry Cobbler', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["4 cups blackberries", "1 cup sugar", "1 cup AP flour", "1/4 tsp salt", "1 egg", "1/4 tsp almond extract", "1 Tbsp lemon juice", "6 Tbsp butter"]'::jsonb, '["Prepare a 9x6 baking dish and preheat oven to 425°.", "Rinse blackberries and plop them in the dish. Mom doesn''t care if you dry them.", "Drizzle lemon juice and almond extract over top of the blackberries.", "Mix together sugar, flour, salt and egg. It will be chunky.", "Spread the mixture evenly over the blackberries.", "Melt butter and drizzle over top of everything.", "Bake for 25 minutes—until golden and bubbling.", "Serve with vanilla ice cream for the dreamiest outcome.", "Yum."]'::jsonb, '["allrecipes", "dessert", "cobbler", "blackberry", "baking"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Phone screenshot of a recipe posted in the comments on allrecipes.com (no servings or times given).', NULL),
('Nana''s Frosting', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["8 oz. cream cheese (room temp)", "1/2 unsalted butter (room temp)", "3 cups powdered sugar", "1/2 tsp vanilla"]'::jsonb, '["High speed mixer."]'::jsonb, '["dessert", "frosting", "cream cheese"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten card. From Nana. Butter amount is written as just "1/2" with no unit (probably 1/2 cup). Vanilla is spelled "vinalla" on the card. The only instruction is "- High speed mixer".

Couldn''t read for sure: butter amount "1/2", no unit written', NULL),
('No-Bake Mini Banana Cream Pies', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 1/2 cups graham cracker crumbs", "1/2 cup melted butter", "1/4 cup sugar", "1 package (3.4 oz) instant banana cream pudding mix", "2 cups cold milk", "1 cup heavy cream", "2 tablespoons powdered sugar", "1 teaspoon vanilla extract", "2 ripe bananas, sliced", "whipped cream, for topping", "honey, for drizzling"]'::jsonb, '["In a medium bowl, mix the graham cracker crumbs, melted butter, and sugar until well combined.", "Press the mixture into the bottom and up the sides of a muffin tin to form mini pie crusts. Refrigerate for at least 1 hour to set.", "In a large bowl, whisk the instant banana cream pudding mix with cold milk until thickened. Refrigerate for 5 minutes.", "In another bowl, whip the heavy cream with powdered sugar and vanilla extract until stiff peaks form. [cut off]"]'::jsonb, '["dessert", "banana", "no-bake", "pie"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Printout of a phone screenshot (social media post). Directions cut off at the bottom of the screenshot; the rest (assembling with banana slices, whipped cream and honey) is not in the photos.

A page of this recipe was missing from the photos.', NULL),
('No-Cook Peanut Buttery Cookie Dough Bites', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["3/4 c. chickpeas - rinsed", "3 tbls peanut butter", "1/3 cup brown sugar", "1 tsp. cream cheese", "1/2 tsp. vanilla", "1/4 tsp salt", "1/8 tsp. baking soda", "2 tbls flour", "2 tbls peanut butter chips", "2 tbls confect. sugar", "2 tbls cocoa"]'::jsonb, '["In a food processor put chickpeas, peanut butter, brown sugar, cream cheese, vanilla, salt & baking soda. Process until smooth. Add flour & chips. Put in refrigerator and chill. Then make into balls and roll into cocoa and sugar."]'::jsonb, '["dessert", "snack", "peanut butter", "no-bake", "Weight Watchers"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten card, taped onto page 2 of the Instrupix brookies printout. Handwritten at the bottom: "Nana''s from Weight Watchers" (From Nana, a Weight Watchers recipe).

Couldn''t read for sure: cream cheese amount: read as "1 tsp." but could be "1 tbsp"', NULL),
('Old Fashioned Coconut Cream Pie', NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, '["1 cup sweetened flaked coconut", "3 cups half & half", "2 eggs, beaten", "3/4 cup white sugar", "1/2 cup flour", "1/4 teas salt", "1 teas vanilla", "1 pie crust", "3 cups whipped topping"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat oven 350°. Spread coconut on a baking sheet and brown for about 5 min.", "In a sauce pan combine half & half, eggs, sugar, flour, salt & vanilla. Bring to boil over low heat, stirring constantly.", "Remove from heat, put 3/4 cup of coconut in filling. Pour filling in crust and chill for 4 hours.", "Top with whipped topping and remaining coconut."]'::jsonb, '["dessert", "pie", "coconut", "cream pie"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe card. Next to the sugar is written ''1/2 + 1/4 = 3/4''. The pie crust is presumably pre-baked.', NULL),
('Old Time Beef Tips and Gravy over Buttered Seasoned Noodles', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 1/2 lbs beef tips", "2 tablespoons veg oil", "1 tbsp butter", "3 1/2 cups beef broth = two cans (can use water also but wont have as much flavor and depth)", "2 tablespoons ketchup", "1/4 c BBQ sauce (optional.. I like Sweet Baby Rays)", "2 tablespoons Worcestershire sauce", "2 cloves minced garlic or a shake of garlic powder", "1 1/2 tsp Grill Mates Montreal Steak Spice or Soul Seasoning (optional, I add this for more flavor, not needed in original recipe)", "salt and pepper", "1 cup onions, minced (1 large onion)", "mushrooms (optional)", "3 tablespoons cornstarch and a tiny amount of water, just enough to stir it into a liquid paste", "1 bag egg noodles", "1 1/2 tbsp butter (for the noodles)", "parmesan cheese"]'::jsonb, '["First take your meat and tenderize with a jaccard.. if you don''t have one.. tenderize with forks or with a tooth edged cooking mallet.", "Place in a heavy cast iron dutch oven. Saute beef tips in veg oil and tbsp of margarine until lightly browned adding a little meat at a time as you brown... salt and pepper well, add spices and garlic, while meat is browning and add broth (or water), ketchup, worcestershire sauce.", "Stir, should be boiling....now turn down heat to simmer...", "Cook covered on simmering low heat for approximately one to two hours or till beef is tender.", "After hour is up....Add 1 cup of minced onions, cook additional hour and 25 minutes on low heat, being careful to not let all water boil out. Check time to time and stir. (Judge cooking time according to your beef, beef should be fork tender when done)", "On your LAST TEN MINUTES you will thicken gravy.. using a small cup, dissolve cornstarch in water and pour into beef mixture. Stir well and cook an additional one minute while gravy thickens. Stir uncovered, till thickens.", "Serve over seasoned buttered egg noodles with mashed potatoes and green beans as a side. Delish!", "For Seasoned Egg Noodles: Make these during last ten minutes of your gravy thickening so you can serve them hot and fresh... simply place whole bag of egg noodles into boiling salted water for 6 minutes.. take out and do not rinse.. drain. Pour in large bowl and add 1 1/2 tbsp butter, salt, pepper, and parmesan cheese. Stir and taste.. should be delicious on it''s own. Pour gravy and tips over top of hot noodles and serve."]'::jsonb, '["Cooking with Serena", "beef", "gravy", "egg noodles", "comfort food", "dutch oven"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout (via printfriendly.com) of a recipe from cookingwithserena.com, by Serena, printed 10/24/2019 (pages 1 and 2 of 9; the recipe text ends on page 2, later pages not in the photos, likely photos/comments). Directions are unnumbered paragraphs on the page; split into steps here. The ingredient list says butter but the directions say "tbsp of margarine". The 1 1/2 tbsp butter, egg noodles and parmesan for the noodles come from the noodle directions (no separate list). Original wording: "tsp and a half of Grill Mates Montreal Steak Spice" and "an shake of garlic powder".', NULL),
('Old-Fashioned Egg Salad', 'Old Fashioned Egg Salad is a delicious, versatile recipe perfect for sandwiches, salads, and more! Easy, family-friendly, and low-carb!', 6, 5, 15, '["8 large eggs", "1/2 cup mayonnaise", "1 teaspoon yellow mustard", "2 tablespoons finely chopped green onion", "2 tablespoons celery finely diced", "1/2 teaspoon salt", "1/4 teaspoon ground black pepper", "1/4 teaspoon paprika"]'::jsonb, '["To hardboil the eggs: Add the eggs to a medium saucepan and add cold water to where it is just covering the eggs.", "To hardboil the eggs: Bring water to a boil and immediately remove from heat. Cover and let the eggs stand for 15 minutes.", "To hardboil the eggs: Remove the eggs to a large bowl with ice water and let the eggs cool.", "For the egg salad: Peel and chop the eggs and place them in a medium bowl.", "For the egg salad: Add the remaining ingredients and mix well.", "For the egg salad: Spread on your favorite bread or crackers, or serve on lettuce."]'::jsonb, '["egg salad", "eggs", "sandwich", "salad", "low-carb"]'::jsonb, '["lunch"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout. Cooling time 10 minutes, total time 30 minutes. Recipe notes: Make sure your eggs are fresh for this recipe! Expired eggs will float to the top of the water when you try to cook them, but a fresh egg will sit neatly at the bottom of the pan on its side. You can make egg salad in advance. However, it''s best to store ... (cut off at the bottom of the page; the rest of the note is not in the photos).', NULL),
('One-Pan Beef Enchiladas Verdes with Mexican Cheese Blend & Hot Sauce Crema', 'Hall of Fame: Meet one of our all-star recipes, a tried-and-true favorite chosen by home cooks like you!', 2, 5, 30, '["1 long green pepper", "3 TBSP sour cream", "1 tsp hot sauce", "10 oz ground beef", "1 TBSP Southwest Spice Blend", "7.06 oz green salsa", "6 flour tortillas", "1/2 cup Mexican cheese blend"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '["HelloFresh", "beef", "Mexican", "enchiladas", "one-pan"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'HelloFresh recipe card, Hall of Fame recipe. Calories 830. Steps page (with the Bust Out pantry list) not in the photos. 4-person amounts: 2 long green peppers, 6 TBSP sour cream, 2 tsp hot sauce, 20 oz ground beef, 2 TBSP Southwest Spice Blend, 14.12 oz green salsa, 12 flour tortillas, 1 cup Mexican cheese blend. Long green pepper and hot sauce are marked spicy. **In our ongoing effort toward sustainability, we''re working on reducing plastic in your order! You may have received 4 servings of protein in one package—rest assured it contains the correct amount.

A page of this recipe was missing from the photos.', NULL),
('One-Pan Cheeseburger Lettuce Wraps with Crispy Fried Onions, Pickle & Special Sauce', 'Familiar ingredients, like ketchup, mustard, and mayonnaise, come together and transform into something truly extraordinary.', 2, 5, 15, '["1 baby lettuce", "1 sliced dill pickle", "2 TBSP mayonnaise", "1 ketchup", "2 tsp dijon mustard", "1 TBSP fry seasoning", "10 oz ground beef", "1 beef stock concentrate", "1/2 cup cheddar cheese", "1 crispy fried onions", "kosher salt", "black pepper", "1 tsp cooking oil"]'::jsonb, '["Prep: Wash and dry produce. Trim and discard root end from lettuce; separate leaves. Thinly slice 1-2 small center leaves until you have 1/3 cup shredded lettuce (2/3 cup for 4 servings). Drain pickle; roughly chop.", "Make sauce: In a small bowl, combine mayonnaise, ketchup, half the mustard, and 1/2 tsp Fry Seasoning (you''ll use more in the next step). (For 4 servings, use all the mustard and 1 tsp Fry Seasoning.) Stir in water 1 tsp at a time until sauce reaches a drizzling consistency. Set aside.", "Cook beef: Heat a drizzle of oil in a large pan over medium-high heat. Add beef*, remaining Fry Seasoning, salt, and pepper. Cook, breaking up meat into pieces, until browned and almost cooked through, 3-5 minutes. Stir in stock concentrate and 1/4 cup water (1/3 cup for 4 servings). Cook, stirring, until liquid has absorbed and beef is cooked through, 2-3 minutes. TIP: If there''s excess grease in your pan, carefully pour it out. Add half the cheese; stir until melted, 1 minute (save the rest for serving).", "Finish & serve: Divide lettuce leaves between plates. Fill with beef mixture, pickle, shredded lettuce, crispy fried onions, remaining cheese, and special sauce. Serve."]'::jsonb, '["HelloFresh", "beef", "lettuce wraps", "cheeseburger", "low carb", "American"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'HelloFresh recipe card, WK 32-2. 780 calories. Serve notice: Wait until just before serving to fill these lettuce wraps so that they don''t get soggy. Or serve the fillings family style in individual bowls and let everyone assemble their wraps at the table! *Ground beef is fully cooked when internal temperature reaches 160°. 4-person amounts: 2 baby lettuce, 2 sliced dill pickle, 4 TBSP mayonnaise, 2 ketchup, 2 tsp dijon mustard, 2 TBSP fry seasoning, 20 oz ground beef, 2 beef stock concentrate, 1 cup cheddar cheese, 2 crispy fried onions, 1 tsp cooking oil.

Couldn''t read for sure: mayonnaise 2-person amount is faded: read as "2 TBSP"; step 1 parenthetical is faded: read as "(2/3 cup for 4 servings)"', NULL),
('One-Pan Monterey Chicken Pasta', 'One-Pan Monterey Chicken Pasta is a quick weeknight dinner inspired by the Monterey Chicken at Chili''s restaurant! Chicken, pasta, BBQ sauce, cheese, and bacon make this pasta the ultimate comfort food and all in one-pan.', 6, 5, 15, '["12 ounces bowtie pasta, (or other small pasta)", "1 (14.5 ounce) can diced tomatoes with green chiles undrained", "2 1/2 cups chicken broth, (I like better than Bouillon base)", "2 cups shredded rotisserie chicken", "1/2 cup barbecue sauce", "1 cup shredded Monterey Jack or cheddar cheese", "4 strips bacon, cooked and crumbled", "2 tablespoons sliced green onions"]'::jsonb, '["In a 12-inch skillet, add the pasta, tomatoes, and chicken broth. Bring mixture to a boil. Cover and reduce to a simmer. Cook pasta for 10-15 minutes, stirring every once in a while to make sure all parts of the pasta are covered and cooking.", "Once pasta is tender, remove lid, stir in the chicken, and heat for a couple of minutes until heated through and excess liquid is evaporated.", "Stir in BBQ sauce. Sprinkle with cheese and cover with lid until cheese is melted. Sprinkle with bacon and green onions. Serve immediately!"]'::jsonb, '["The Girl Who Ate Everything", "chicken", "pasta", "one-pan", "bacon", "BBQ"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'The Girl Who Ate Everything web printout (page 1 of 2; page 2 not in the photos, but the recipe is complete on page 1). Glare covers several ingredient words; they were reconstructed from the instructions and context.

Couldn''t read for sure: "(or other small pasta)" - "other" partly under glare; "2 cups shredded rotisserie chicken" - "rotisserie chicken" partly under glare; "1/2 cup barbecue sauce" - end of "sauce" under glare; "1 cup shredded Monterey Jack or cheddar cheese" - "Jack or" under glare; "4 strips bacon, cooked and crumbled" - "and crumbled" partly under glare; "2 tablespoons sliced green onions" - "tablespoons" and "green" partly under glare; description "BBQ sauce, cheese" and "comfort food" partly under glare', 'https://www.the-girl-who-ate-everything.com/wp-json/mv-create/v1/creations/72/print'),
('One-Pan Taco Rice Dinner', NULL, 4, 5, 15, '["1 pound ground beef", "1 packet taco seasoning", "2 cups water", "2 cups Minute Rice, uncooked", "1 cup salsa", "1 cup shredded cheddar cheese"]'::jsonb, '["In a large skillet, brown and crumble [ground beef]", "Drain excess grease.", "Add in taco seasoning and water.", "Stir well and allow the mixture to co[me to a boil]", "Turn down the heat, then add in unc[ooked Minute] Rice and stir.", "Cover and cook for about 5 minutes [or until rice] is tender.", "Remove the lid and stir in salsa and [cheese]", "Turn off the heat and it''s ready to se[rve]."]'::jsonb, '["Recipe Whisper", "beef", "Mexican", "rice", "one-pan", "ground beef", "taco"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'From a Facebook post by Recipe Whisper (printed 8/17/24, pages 1 and 2 of 3 printed side by side). The right edge of the instructions is cut off on the printout; words in [square brackets] are filled in from context, not printed. Total time 20 minutes. Nutrition per serving (partly cut off): carbohydrates [cut off]g, fat 20g, fiber 2g, sugar 3g.

Couldn''t read for sure: all bracketed words in steps 1, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 are inferred (text cut off at the right margin); carbohydrates value cut off (looks like 30g or 36g)

A page of this recipe was missing from the photos.', NULL),
('One-Pot Chicken Burrito Bowls', 'One-Pot Chicken Burrito Bowl Recipe - tender chunks of chicken, homemade Mexican rice, and seasoned black beans loaded with your favorite burrito bowl toppings', 6, 10, 20, '["1 pound chicken breast cut into bite sized pieces", "3 tablespoons olive oil", "1/4 cup yellow onion diced", "1 cup extra-long grain rice uncooked", "1 14.5 oz can diced tomatoes drained", "1 15 oz can black beans drained and rinsed", "1 teaspoon garlic powder", "1 teaspoon onion powder", "2 teaspoons chili powder", "1 teaspoon cumin", "1 teaspoon smoked paprika", "2 1/2 cups low-sodium chicken broth", "lime", "1 cup colby jack cheese monterey jack or cheddar cheese", "kosher salt and pepper", "freshly diced tomatoes", "diced green onions", "sour cream", "guacamole"]'::jsonb, '["Start by sautéing onions in 2 tablespoons of olive oil until they start to soften.", "Season diced chicken with 1 teaspoon of kosher salt and 1/2 teaspoon of black pepper.", "Add chicken to pan and cook over medium high heat until chicken has started to brown.", "Move chicken to one side of pan. On the other side of the pan, add an additional tablespoon of olive oil and sauté uncooked rice for about 2 minutes, or just until some grains start to turn golden brown.", "Stir in drained black beans, drained canned tomatoes, chicken broth, garlic powder, onion powder, chili powder, smoked paprika and cumin."]'::jsonb, '["number-2-pencil.com", "chicken", "Mexican", "burrito bowl", "rice", "one-pot"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout, page 1 of 2; page 2 (remaining instructions after step 5) not in the photos. Course: Dinner. Cuisine: Mexican. Total time 30 minutes. Calories 373 kcal. Footer URL is blurry (looks like number-2-pencil.com/one-pan-chicken-burrito-bowls/).

A page of this recipe was missing from the photos.', NULL),
('Onion Bombs', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["2 lbs hamburger", "1 cup bread crumbs", "1 egg, beaten", "1 c. milk", "1/2 c. BBQ sauce", "1 tsp salt", "1/2 tsp pepper", "1/2 tsp garlic powder", "onions, cut", "1 pkg bacon", "additional BBQ sauce"]'::jsonb, '["Make into balls, then take onion and place around meat, then wrap with bacon."]'::jsonb, '["beef", "bacon", "BBQ", "meatballs", "handwritten"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe on a notebook page, printed from an Evernote note ("Untitled note", page 2 of a multi-page printout, header date blurry, early 2021). Written as "2 lbs hamburger", "onions cut", "additional BBQ". No baking/grilling time or temperature written.

Couldn''t read for sure: "1 c. milk" (amount seems large for 2 lbs meat, but reads clearly as 1 c.); printout date in header is blurry', NULL),
('Onion Crunch Chicken with Mashed Sweet Potatoes, Roasted Green Beans & Honey Dijon Dressing', NULL, 2, 10, 30, '["2 sweet potatoes", "1 crispy fried onions", "1/4 cup Monterey Jack cheese", "10 oz chicken cutlets", "1.5 oz honey Dijon dressing", "6 oz green beans", "1 1/2 TBSP sour cream", "kosher salt", "black pepper", "1 tsp olive oil", "2 TBSP butter"]'::jsonb, '["Prep & make crust: Adjust rack to middle position (middle and top positions for 4 servings) and preheat oven to 425 degrees. Wash and dry produce. Peel and dice sweet potatoes into 1/2-inch pieces. Using your hands, finely crush crispy fried onions in their bag. (TIP: Once crushed, crispy fried onions should resemble breadcrumbs.) Transfer to a small bowl; stir in Monterey Jack. Reserve 1 TBSP dressing (2 TBSP for 4 servings) in a second small bowl (you''ll use it in step 3).", "Cook sweet potatoes: Place sweet potatoes in a medium pot with enough salted water to cover by 2 inches. Bring to a boil and cook until tender, 15-20 minutes. Reserve 1/2 cup potato cooking liquid, then drain and return sweet potatoes to pot. Cover to keep warm.", "Coat chicken: Meanwhile, pat chicken* dry with paper towels and season all over with salt and pepper. Place on one side of a baking sheet. (For 4 servings, spread chicken out across entire sheet.) Evenly spread tops of chicken with a thin layer of reserved dressing. Mound coated sides with onion crust, pressing to adhere (no need to coat the undersides).", "Roast chicken & beans: Toss green beans on empty side of same sheet with a drizzle of olive oil, salt, and pepper. (For 4 servings, add green beans to a second sheet; roast green beans on top rack and chicken on middle rack.) Roast on middle rack until chicken is cooked through and green beans are browned and tender, 15-20 minutes. TIP: Check chicken periodically—if the crust browns too quickly, loosely cover with foil. Additionally, if green beans finish before chicken, remove from sheet and continue roasting chicken.", "Mash sweet potatoes: Meanwhile, mash sweet potatoes with sour cream, 2 TBSP butter (4 TBSP for 4 servings), and a big pinch of salt until smooth, adding splashes of reserved potato cooking liquid as needed. Taste and season with salt and pepper.", "Serve: Divide mashed sweet potatoes, green beans, and chicken between plates. Serve with remaining dressing on the side."]'::jsonb, '["HelloFresh", "chicken", "sweet potatoes", "green beans", "American"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'HelloFresh recipe card, WK 26-1. Calories: 720. Gold (B)rush: In step 3, we instruct you to brush the tops of your chicken with some honey Dijon dressing. We prefer to use a basting brush for the job, but if you don''t have one, simply use the back of a spoon to evenly coat. Hello Crispy Fried Onions: Crushing up this timeless topper and mixing it with cheese creates a next-level crunchy crust for chicken. *Chicken is fully cooked when internal temperature reaches 165°. 4-person amounts: 4 sweet potatoes, 2 crispy fried onions, 1/2 cup Monterey Jack, 20 oz chicken cutlets, 3 oz honey Dijon dressing, 12 oz green beans, 3 TBSP sour cream, 1 tsp olive oil, 4 TBSP butter.

Couldn''t read for sure: ''Reserve 1/2 cup potato cooking liquid'' (fraction small)', NULL),
('Orange Jello Delight', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 pkg. small orange jello", "1 cup hot water", "1 pint orange sherbet", "1 can drained mandarin oranges", "cool whip (1 cup or what ever you want for taste)"]'::jsonb, '["Dissolve jello in 1 cup hot water.", "Stir sherbet into hot mixture until dissolved.", "When starting to set up add 1 can of drained mandarin oranges and cool whip (1 cup or what ever you want for taste). Stir until creamy and let setup."]'::jsonb, '["dessert", "jello", "orange", "salad"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'From Mom (printed email, Nov 26, 2014). "I chop the oranges into small pieces."', NULL),
('Orecchiette & Pork Ragù with Shishito Peppers', 'The scooped shape of tender orecchiette pasta is perfect for catching every bite of our rich sauce of pork, tomato, charred shishito peppers, and just a touch of mascarpone cheese for creaminess.', 4, NULL, 35, '["1 1/4 lbs ground pork", "3/4 lb orecchiette pasta", "1 14-oz can whole peeled tomatoes", "1/4 cup mascarpone cheese", "2 Tbsps tomato paste", "1/4 cup grated Parmesan cheese", "1 red onion", "6 oz shishito peppers", "2 cloves garlic", "1 oz pitted Niçoise olives", "1/4 tsp crushed red pepper flakes", "1 tsp whole dried oregano", "olive oil", "salt", "pepper"]'::jsonb, '["Prepare the ingredients: Fill a large pot 3/4 of the way up with salted water; cover and heat to boiling on high. Wash and dry the peppers; cut off and discard the stems, then cut the peppers into 1/2-inch pieces. Halve, peel, and medium dice the onion. Peel and roughly chop 2 cloves of garlic. Roughly chop the olives. Combine in a bowl. Place the tomatoes in a separate bowl; gently break apart with your hands.", "Char the peppers: In a large, high-sided pan (or pot), heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil on medium-high until hot. Add the pepper pieces in an even layer and cook, without stirring, 3 to 4 minutes, or until browned. Season with salt and pepper. Continue to cook, stirring occasionally, 4 to 5 minutes, or until charred and softened. Transfer to a bowl; cover with foil to keep warm. Wipe out the pan.", "Cook the pork & make the ragù: In the same pan, heat a drizzle of olive oil on medium-high until hot. Add the pork and diced onion in an even layer. Cook, without stirring, 3 to 4 minutes, or until browned. Add the chopped garlic and olives, oregano, and as much of the red pepper flakes as you''d like, depending on how spicy you''d like the dish to be. Season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring frequently and breaking the meat apart with a spoon, 30 seconds to 1 minute, or until combined. Add the tomato paste. Cook, stirring frequently, 1 to 2 minutes, or until thoroughly combined. Add the crushed tomatoes (carefully, as the liquid may splatter) and 1/4 cup of water; season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, 4 to 5 minutes, or until the liquid is slightly thickened and the pork is cooked through. Turn off the heat.", "Cook the pasta: Meanwhile, add the pasta to the pot of boiling water. Cook, stirring occasionally, 9 to 11 minutes, or until al dente (still slightly firm to the bite). Turn off the heat. Reserving 1/2 cup of the pasta cooking water, drain thoroughly.", "Finish the pasta & serve your dish: To the pan of ragù, add the cooked pasta, charred peppers, and half the reserved pasta cooking water. Cook on medium-high, stirring constantly, 1 to 2 minutes, or until the pasta is coated (if necessary, gradually add the remaining cooking water to ensure the pasta is thoroughly coated). Turn off the heat; stir in the mascarpone. Taste, then season with salt and pepper if desired. Serve the finished pasta and ragù garnished with the parmesan. Enjoy!"]'::jsonb, '["Blue Apron", "pork", "pasta", "Italian", "ragù"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Blue Apron recipe card. Time: 25-35 minutes. Wine pairing: Fruity & Savory.

Couldn''t read for sure: ground pork ''1 1/4 lbs'' (fraction small; could be 1 1/8)', NULL),
('Outrageous Chocolate Chip Cookies', NULL, 24, NULL, NULL, '["1/2 c. granulated sugar", "1/3 c. packed brown sugar", "1/2 c (1 stick) margarine or butter, softened", "1/2 c. peanut butter", "1/2 teas. vanilla", "1 egg", "1 cup flour", "1/2 c. quick-cooking or regular oats", "1 teas. baking soda", "1/4 teas. salt", "6 oz. chocolate chips"]'::jsonb, '["Heat oven to 350°. Cream sugars, margarine, peanut butter, vanilla & egg. Mix in flour, oats, baking soda, salt, & chips. Drop dough by rounded tablespoon about 2\" apart on ungreased cookie sheet. Bake 10 to 12 minutes."]'::jsonb, '["dessert", "cookies", "chocolate chip", "peanut butter"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe card ("No. servings: 2 dozen") on an Evernote printout (Untitled note, 2/4/2021, page 2/3). The left edge of the method is cut off/faded ("Heat", "peanut", "oats", "dough", "apart" partly missing). Choc. Scotcheroos is written below it on the same page.

Couldn''t read for sure: baking soda amount partly obscured, read as "1 teas."; "oats" in the method is cut off ("ts"); chocolate chips "6 oz."', NULL),
('Oven Baked Fajitas', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 lb. chicken breasts cut into strips", "2 tbsp vegetable oil", "2 tsp. chili powder", "1 1/2 tsp. cumin", "1/2 tsp. garlic powder", "1/2 tsp. dried oregano", "1/4 tsp. seasoned salt", "1 (15 oz) tomatoes & green chilies", "1 medium onion, sliced", "1/2 red bell pepper, sliced", "1/2 green bell pepper, sliced"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat oven to 400°. Place chicken in 13x9 baking dish or crockpot."]'::jsonb, '["chicken", "fajitas", "Mexican", "Tex-Mex"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten on a notebook page ("Over Baked fajita"), Evernote printout page 2/3 dated 2/3/2021. The written directions stop after the first sentence.

Couldn''t read for sure: green bell pepper amount hidden by glare (assumed 1/2 like the red); ''chicken'' in first line partly obscured by glare; ''2 tbsp'' vegetable oil (could be tsp)', NULL),
('Pam''s Banana Bread', NULL, NULL, NULL, 40, '["2 eggs", "1 c. sugar", "1/2 butter shortening", "1 tbs baking soda", "2 c. flour", "1/2 c. sweet condensed milk, soured", "1 tbls vinegar", "1 cup bananas", "nuts"]'::jsonb, '["Bake 350 40 min."]'::jsonb, '["bread", "banana", "quick bread", "baking"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe card taped in a spiral recipe notebook. Card reads ''1/2 c sweet condensed milk - soured'' with ''1 tbls vinager'' written to the right (i.e. sour the milk with 1 tbls vinegar). ''nuts'' written in the right-hand column with no amount. Butter/shortening amount written as ''1/2'' with no unit (probably 1/2 c.). No mixing instructions on the card.

Couldn''t read for sure: ''1/2 butter shortening'' - no unit written; ''1 tbs baking soda'' (tbs vs tsp); ''1 tbls vinager'' - the ''1 tbls'' is faint/overwritten', NULL),
('Parmesan Chive Chicken & Potatoes with Mixed Greens & Honey Dijon Dressing', NULL, 2, NULL, 15, '["12 oz potatoes", "1/4 oz chives", "1 mini cucumber", "1 tomato", "2 TBSP garlic herb butter", "10 oz chicken cutlets", "4 oz cream sauce base", "3 TBSP Parmesan cheese", "2 oz mixed greens", "1.5 oz honey Dijon dressing", "kosher salt", "black pepper", "2 tsp cooking oil"]'::jsonb, '["Prep: Wash and dry produce. Quarter potatoes (peel if you prefer). Finely chop chives. Dice cucumber. Dice tomato.", "Zap: In a microwave-safe bowl, season potatoes with salt and pepper. Add garlic herb butter and cover with plastic wrap; microwave until tender and steaming, 6-7 minutes.", "Sizzle: Meanwhile, pat chicken* dry and season with salt and pepper. Drizzle oil in a hot pan; cook chicken until cooked through, 5-7 minutes per side. Turn off heat; transfer to a plate and cover with foil. Wipe out pan. Heat another drizzle of oil in same pan. Cook cream sauce, cheese, and chives, stirring, until sauce is smooth and slightly thickened, 1-2 minutes.", "Serve: In a bowl, toss mixed greens, cucumber, tomato, and dressing. Spoon sauce over chicken and potatoes. Serve with salad."]'::jsonb, '["HelloFresh", "chicken", "potatoes", "Fast & Fresh", "American"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'HelloFresh ''Fast & Fresh'' recipe card, WK 29-14. Box to plate: 15 minutes. Calories: 710. *Chicken is fully cooked when internal temperature reaches 165°. Ingredient amounts come from the steps page (2-person column); 4-person: 24 oz potatoes, 1/2 oz chives, 2 mini cucumbers, 2 tomatoes, 4 TBSP garlic herb butter, 20 oz chicken cutlets, 8 oz cream sauce base, 6 TBSP Parmesan, 4 oz mixed greens, 3 oz honey Dijon dressing, 2 tsp cooking oil.', NULL),
('Pasta Italiano Bake', 'A lasagne type recipe with a creamy layer of Miracle Whip salad dressing and parmesan cheese.', 6, NULL, NULL, '["1 lb. ground beef", "1/4 cup chopped onion", "1/4 cup chopped green pepper", "1 garlic clove, minced", "1 6-oz. can tomato paste", "1/2 cup water", "1 teaspoon salt", "1/2 teaspoon oregano leaves", "2 cups (4 ozs.) noodles, cooked, drained", "1/4 cup chopped parsley", "1/2 cup Miracle Whip salad dressing", "3/4 cup (3 ozs.) Kraft grated parmesan cheese", "2 eggs, beaten"]'::jsonb, '["Brown meat; drain. Add onion, green pepper and garlic; cook until tender. Stir in tomato paste, water and seasonings. Cover; simmer 15 minutes. Combine noodles and parsley; toss lightly. Combine salad dressing, 1/2 cup cheese and eggs; mix well. Layer noodles, salad dressing mixture and meat sauce in 10 x 6-inch baking dish; top with remaining cheese. Bake at 350°, 25 minutes."]'::jsonb, '["Kraft", "beef", "pasta", "casserole", "Italian", "baked"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Printed clipping (Kraft / Miracle Whip). There is also a handwritten copy of the same recipe on a notebook card (Evernote printout titled "Pasta Italian Bake", card headed "Pasta Italiano Bake", 2/1/2021) with the same ingredients written in short form ("1 6 oz tomato paste", "2 c. noodles, cooked", "1/2 c. miracle whip", "3/4 c. parmesan cheese") and the same directions in shortened form: "Brown meat, add onion, green peppers, and garlic, cook until tender. Stir in tomato paste, water and seasonings. Cover, simmer for 15 min. Combine noodles & parsley. Combine dressing, 1/2 of cheese & egg. Layer noodles, salad dressing mixture and meat. Bake 350° for 25 min."', NULL),
('Peanut Brittle', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 cup white Karo syrup", "1 1/2 cups white sugar", "1/4 teas salt", "2 cups raw peanuts", "2 1/4 teas (level) baking soda", "2 tbls butter cut up"]'::jsonb, '["Cook syrup, sugar and salt. Bring to boil. Then add peanuts. Wait to see the peanuts swell and to start to smell. Butter then baking soda. Turn burner off when you add butter + baking soda."]'::jsonb, '["dessert", "candy", "peanuts"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten on a recipe card in the spiral notebook. Also written on the card: "*measure everything before starting", "7 1/2 burner" (presumably the stove dial setting), "*Butter Pan*".

Couldn''t read for sure: baking soda amount "2 1/4 teas" (could be 1 1/4); title written "Peanut brittal"; "7 1/2 burner"', NULL),
('Peanut Butter Balls', 'No bake peanut butter balls are made with only five ingredients. So easy to make and the best treat for peanut butter chocolate lovers!', 40, 15, NULL, '["1 1/2 cups (400 g) no-stir creamy peanut butter (one 16 ounce jar)", "3 cups (360 g) confectioner''s sugar", "1/2 cup (113 g or 1 stick) unsalted butter, room temperature", "2 cups (50 g) Rice Krispies", "2 cups (350 g) dark chocolate chips, for dipping"]'::jsonb, '["In a stand mixer fitted with a paddle attachment, combine peanut butter and butter. Slowly add confectioner''s sugar and then Rice Krispies. Mixing just until combined.", "Place mixture in refrigerator until firm, about 45 minutes.", "Take chilled mixture and scoop a full tablespoon. Roll into 1-inch balls and place on baking sheet lined with parchment paper. Place in freezer for at least 30 minutes to prevent misshaped balls.", "When ready to dip balls, prepare a baking sheet lined with parchment paper. Place chocolate chips in a microwave-safe bowl and heat in the microwave on 50% power level. Start with 1 minute, stir the chips. Repeat on 50% power level, stirring every 20 seconds until smooth.", "Dip balls in melted chocolate and transfer to lined baking sheet. Immediately add sprinkles if desired. Once all the balls are covered in chocolate, place in fridge to firm up. Store in an air tight container in the fridge or at room temperature."]'::jsonb, '["If You Give a Blonde a Kitchen", "dessert", "candy", "no bake", "peanut butter", "chocolate", "American"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from If You Give a Blonde a Kitchen, author Haley D Williams. Chill time 1 hour 15 minutes; total time 1 hour 30 minutes. Makes 40 balls, 166 kcal each. Recipe notes: Measuring confectioners'' sugar: I''ve done this recipe with sifted and unsifted confectioners'' sugar - both work well! Just be sure to measure before sifting. Tips for melting chocolate: If the chocolate starts to firm up during the dipping process, place back in the microwave for another 20 seconds. Never add water to melted chocolate! (Faint show-through text from the back of the page is not transcribed.)', 'https://ifyougiveablondeakitchen.com/no-bake-peanut-butter-balls/'),
('Peanut Butter Cup Stuffed Brookies (Quick & Easy!)', 'This quick and easy chocolate dessert is made with just 3 store-bought ingredients plus the egg and oil you need for the brownie batter. They''re incredibly fun and simple to make in a muffin tin! This is seriously the BEST dessert recipe I''ve ever made (probably in the history of the world!). They remind me of a fancy lava cake or mini pizookie served warm with ice cream. It''s basically the marriage of a cookie, brownie and Reese''s peanut butter cup. How can you go wrong with that?', 12, NULL, NULL, '["1 (10oz) bag of brownie mix (plus the oil & egg to make the batter)", "1 (6 pack) Reese''s Peanut Butter Cups (12 cups total)", "1 (16oz) package of refrigerated cookie dough"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat your oven to 350 degrees and generously grease a regular size muffin tin.", "Prepare the brownie mix according the package directions; set aside.", "Separate the cookie dough into 12 even balls and then squish them down into the bottom of each muffin cup.", "Place a Reese''s peanut butter cup upside down on top of the cookie dough.", "Evenly distribute the brownie batter on top of each peanut butter cup until the wells are about 90% full.", "Bake for 18-20 minutes or until the brownie batter is cooked through.", "Allow them to cool for about 5 minutes before removing from the pan, and then enjoy while they are still warm."]'::jsonb, '["Instrupix", "dessert", "brownies", "cookies", "peanut butter", "chocolate"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Printed from Instrupix (6/22/2021). Recipe Notes: These are best eaten warm with vanilla ice cream on top. Yum! Place any leftovers in the microwave for about 30 seconds to reheat. You could also use an Oreo or a couple of caramels in place of the peanut butter cup. What else could you stuff in there? Page 2 of the printout is mostly covered by a taped-on handwritten card (No-Cook Peanut Buttery Cookie Dough Bites).', 'https://www.instrupix.com/easy-peanut-butter-cup-cookie-chocolate-brownies-dessert/'),
('Pecan Pie', NULL, NULL, NULL, 60, '["1 pie crust", "1 cup light corn syrup", "1 cup sugar", "3 eggs, lightly beaten", "1 stick melted butter", "1 teas. vanilla", "1 cup pecans"]'::jsonb, '["Heat oven 350°. In a bowl mix corn syrup, sugar, eggs, salt & vanilla; mix well. Pour filling into crust. Sprinkle with pecans. Bake for 1 hr. Cover the crust with foil to keep from browning."]'::jsonb, '["pie", "dessert", "pecan", "baking"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten in a spiral recipe notebook, with edits: "1 cup firmly packed brown sugar" is crossed out and "1 Cup sugar" added at the end of the list; the butter amount is crossed out (looks like "1/4 cup") and replaced with "1 Stick"; "1/2 teas. salt" is crossed out (the directions still mention salt). The baking time originally read "45 to 50 min", scribbled over with "1 hr." written above it. The directions do not say when to add the butter.

Couldn''t read for sure: oven temperature: written over, best reading 350° (could be 325° or 375°); crossed-out butter amount: best reading "1/4 cup"; crossed-out bake time: best reading "45 to 50 min"', NULL),
('Pecan-Crusted Chicken with Honey Mustard Sauce & Lemony Apple Salad', 'Hall of Fame: Meet one of our all-star recipes, a tried-and-true favorite chosen by home cooks like you!', 2, 5, 30, '["1/2 oz pecans", "1/4 cup panko breadcrumbs", "1 TBSP Fry Seasoning", "2 tsp honey", "2 tsp Dijon mustard", "2 TBSP mayonnaise", "10 oz chicken cutlets", "1 apple", "1 lemon", "2 oz mixed greens", "kosher salt", "black pepper", "1 TBSP olive oil", "1 tsp cooking oil", "1 TBSP butter"]'::jsonb, '["Prep: Adjust rack to middle position and preheat oven to 450 degrees. Wash and dry produce. Finely chop pecans (or crush in their bag with a heavy pan or rolling pin).", "Make crust: Place 1 TBSP butter (2 TBSP for 4 servings) in a medium microwave-safe bowl. Microwave until melted, 30 seconds. Let cool slightly, then stir in chopped pecans, panko, half the Fry Seasoning (you''ll use the rest later), a drizzle of olive oil, and a pinch of salt and pepper.", "Make sauce: In a small bowl, combine honey, mustard, and mayonnaise.", "Cook chicken: Pat chicken* dry with paper towels; season with remaining Fry Seasoning, salt, and pepper. Place on a lightly oiled baking sheet. Evenly spread tops of chicken with a thin layer of honey mustard sauce (save the rest for serving). Mound with pecan mixture, pressing firmly to adhere (no need to coat the undersides). Roast on middle rack until crust is golden brown and chicken is cooked through, 15-20 minutes.", "Make salad: Meanwhile, halve, core, and thinly slice apple. Quarter lemon. In a large bowl, toss mixed greens and apple with a large drizzle of olive oil and as much lemon juice as you like. Season with salt and pepper.", "Serve: Divide chicken and salad between plates. Drizzle chicken with remaining honey mustard sauce. Serve with any remaining lemon wedges on the side."]'::jsonb, '["HelloFresh", "chicken", "pecan", "salad", "oven"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'HelloFresh recipe card (WK 4-28), Hall of Fame recipe. 4-person amounts: 1 oz pecans, 1/2 cup panko, 2 TBSP Fry Seasoning, 4 tsp honey, 4 tsp Dijon mustard, 4 TBSP mayonnaise, 20 oz chicken cutlets, 2 apples, 1 lemon, 4 oz mixed greens; 1 TBSP olive oil, 1 tsp cooking oil, 2 TBSP butter. *Chicken is fully cooked when internal temperature reaches 165°. Card tip ''Gold (B)rush'': In step 4, we prefer to use a basting brush for the job, but if you don''t have one, simply use the back of a spoon.', NULL),
('Penne and Smoked Sausage', NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, '["2 cups uncooked penne pasta", "1 pound smoked sausage or smoked kielbasa, cut into 1/4-inch slices", "1 1/2 cups milk", "1 can (10 3/4 ounces) condensed cream of celery soup, undiluted", "1 1/2 cups cheddar french-fried onions, divided", "1 cup (4 ounces) shredded part-skim mozzarella cheese, divided", "1 cup frozen peas"]'::jsonb, '["Cook pasta according to package directions. Meanwhile, in a large skillet, brown sausage over medium heat for 5 minutes; drain. In a large bowl, combine milk and soup. Stir in 1/2 cup onions, 1/2 cup cheese, peas and sausage. Drain pasta; stir into sausage mixture.", "Transfer to a greased 13-in. x 9-in. x 2-in. baking dish. Cover and bake at 375° for 25-30 minutes or until bubbly. Sprinkle with remaining onions and cheese. Bake, uncovered, 3-5 minutes longer or until cheese is melted."]'::jsonb, '["sausage", "kielbasa", "pasta", "casserole"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Printed newspaper/magazine clipping (Taste of Home style) on an Evernote printout page dated 2/4/2021; a handwritten Lasagna recipe is below it on the same page. Tip printed under the recipe: "I have trouble keeping aluminum foil on my casserole dishes when transporting them to potluck dinners. Instead, I put the dishes inside a clear plastic oven bag. The bags trap any spills, don''t melt and people can see what''s inside. It''s so easy to slide the dish in and seal it with a twist tie. -Carlene H., Crossville, Tennessee" (a few words of the tip are washed out).

Couldn''t read for sure: milk amount: first digit faded, read as ''1 1/2 cups milk''; ''Yield: 6 servings'' header partly washed out', NULL),
('Pesto Chicken Focaccia Sandwiches with Tomato Dipping Sauce', 'These satisfying sandwiches feature melty fontina cheese and tender chicken (tossed in our verdant basil pesto) layered onto golden focaccia bread—first toasted in the oven, then rubbed with a whole clove of garlic to add aromatic depth of flavor. For a complementary side, we''re serving roasted broccoli simply finished with bites of smoky-sweet roasted red peppers.', 4, NULL, 50, '["4 boneless, skinless chicken breasts", "1 piece focaccia bread", "1 oz sliced roasted red peppers", "1 15-oz can crushed tomatoes", "1/3 cup basil pesto", "1 lb broccoli", "2 cloves garlic", "4 oz shredded fontina cheese", "1 Tbsp Italian seasoning (whole dried basil, sage, oregano, savory, rosemary, thyme & marjoram)"]'::jsonb, '["Prepare the ingredients: Place an oven rack in the center of the oven, then preheat to 450°F. Wash and dry the broccoli; cut off and discard the bottom 1/2 inch of the stem, then cut the broccoli into small florets. Roughly chop the peppers. Halve the bread. Peel 2 cloves of garlic. Keeping 1 clove whole, roughly chop the remaining clove.", "Roast & finish the broccoli: Line a sheet pan with foil. Place the broccoli florets on the foil. Drizzle with olive oil and season with salt and pepper. Toss to coat and arrange in an even layer. Roast 14 to 16 minutes, or until browned and tender when pierced with a fork. Reserving the sheet pan, transfer to a bowl. Stir in the chopped peppers. Cover with foil to keep warm.", "Cook & slice the chicken: Meanwhile, pat the chicken dry with paper towels. Season with salt and pepper on both sides. In a large pan (nonstick, if you have one), heat a drizzle of olive oil on medium-high until hot. Add the seasoned chicken. Cook 6 to 7 minutes per side, or until browned and cooked through.* Leaving any browned bits (or fond) in the pan, transfer to a cutting board. When cool enough to handle, thinly slice crosswise and transfer to a large bowl.", "Toast the bread: Place the halved bread, cut side up, on the reserved sheet pan. Drizzle with olive oil and season with salt and pepper. Evenly top the bottom half with the cheese. Bake 5 to 7 minutes, or until lightly browned and the cheese is melted. Remove from the oven. When cool enough to handle, carefully rub the top half with the whole garlic clove; discard the clove. Transfer both halves to a cutting board.", "Make the sauce: In the pan of reserved fond, heat a drizzle of olive oil on medium-high until hot. Add the chopped garlic. Cook, stirring frequently, 30 seconds to 1 minute, or until slightly softened. Add the tomatoes (carefully, as the liquid may splatter) and Italian seasoning. Season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, 2 to 3 minutes, or until slightly thickened. Turn off the heat. Taste, then season with salt and pepper if desired.", "Finish & serve your dish: To the bowl of sliced chicken, add the pesto. Season with salt and pepper; stir to thoroughly coat. Assemble the sandwiches using the toasted bread and pesto chicken. Using a serrated knife, cut the sandwiches into 4 equal-sized portions. Serve the finished sandwiches with the finished broccoli and sauce on the side. Enjoy!"]'::jsonb, '["Blue Apron", "chicken", "sandwich", "Italian", "pesto"]'::jsonb, '["dinner", "lunch"]'::jsonb, 'Blue Apron recipe card. Wine match: Light & Fresh. *An instant-read thermometer should register 165°F. Steps also use olive oil, salt and pepper (not in the printed ingredient list).

Couldn''t read for sure: basil pesto amount: ''1/3 cup'' (small print)', NULL),
('Philly Cheese Sandwiches', 'I''m a big fan of cheesesteaks, and in this throw-together recipe my slow cooker does all the work. It''s a win-win. —Christina Addison, Blanchester, Ohio', 8, NULL, 510, '["1 beef chuck roast (2-1/2 to 3 pounds), boneless", "1/2 tsp basil, dried", "2 garlic cloves", "1 green pepper, medium", "2 onions, medium", "1 tsp oregano, dried", "1/4 cup Worcestershire sauce", "1 red pepper, medium sweet", "8 hoagie buns", "8 slices American cheese or pepper jack cheese"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '["Taste of Home", "Pinterest", "beef", "sandwich", "slow cooker", "cheesesteak"]'::jsonb, '["lunch", "dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Taste of Home recipe saved on Pinterest (page 1 of 3). 4 reviews, 8.5 hours, serves 8. This page has only the 10 ingredients; the directions are on pages not in the photos. Title is partly cut off at the top of the pin card.

