('Rice Pilaf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["2 sticks of butter", "2 to 3 jalapeno peppers", "1 red bell pepper", "1 white onion", "angel hair pasta", "12 oz white instant rice", "4 to 5 chicken bouillon cubes", "chicken broth (to replace water in rice)"]'::jsonb, '["In a large pot cook rice - use chicken broth instead of water and add 4 chicken bouillon cubes - (make sure chicken broth + bouillon cubes are boiling and dissolved before adding rice). Set rice aside.", "Mince jalapenos, onion, and red bell pepper. In a large skillet put one stick of butter and saute the peppers and onions - when done add to rice and stir them in.", "Then crunch up angel hair pasta (pasta will be a 1/2 in long). In same large skillet put the other stick of butter, melt down and then add angel hair - you will fry it until it is caramelized (dark brown - just on the verge of burnt). (When frying, the angel hair pasta will bubble - cook past that point.) Then add angel hair to rice and mix."]'::jsonb, '["rice", "pasta", "side", "handwritten"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten on a spiral recipe-notebook page ("Recipe: Rice Pilaf"); serves/prep/cook time left blank. Written as ''angle hair'' throughout (angel hair pasta), ''bullon cubs/cubes'' (bouillon cubes), ''carmelized'', ''virge'' (verge). No amount given for the angel hair pasta. Directions are one paragraph on the card; split into 3 steps here. Small write-overs: ''one st stick'' and ''b cubes'' (corrected letters, nothing substantive crossed out).

Couldn''t read for sure: direction line 3 ''make sure chicken broth'' and line 4 ''dissolved before adding rice'': partly under glare; ''(* when dark brown'': an asterisk-like mark before ''when''; read as a parenthetical; ''1/2 in long'': handwritten ''1/2'' fraction', NULL),
