('Sloppy Joes (yummy)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 lb. ground beef", "14 oz. diced tomatoes", "1 onion, chopped", "3 tbls brown sugar", "1 medium celery (stalk)", "2 tsp. Worcestershire sauce", "1/2 ground cumin", "1 tsp chili powder", "1/2 tsp salt"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '["beef", "sloppy joes", "sandwich", "handwritten"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten notebook card (Evernote printout 2/3/2021), titled "Sloppy Joes (yummy)". Ingredients only, no directions.

Couldn''t read for sure: ''1/2 ground cumin'': unit missing and a smudge before it (could be 1 1/2; probably tsp); ''chili powder'' end of word smudged', NULL),
('Slow Cooker Cream Cheese Crack Chicken Chili', 'Slow Cooker Cream Cheese Crack Chicken Chili - this stuff is AMAZING! We''ve made it 3 times this month! We can''t get enough of it!!! Chicken, corn, black beans, chicken broth, diced tomatoes and green chiles, cumin, chili powder, onion, ranch seasoning, bacon and cheddar cheese. We served the chili with some cornbread and Fritos. PERFECT! This is already on the menu again this weekend! YUM! #crockpot #slowcooker #chicken #chili', 8, 5, 360, '["2 boneless skinless chicken breasts", "1 (11-oz) can corn, drained", "1 (15-oz) black beans, drained and rinsed", "1 (10-oz) diced tomatoes and green chilies, undrained", "2 cups chicken broth", "1 cup cooked chopped bacon", "1 (1-oz) packet ranch seasoning & salad dressing mix", "1 tsp cumin", "1 Tbsp chili powder", "1 tsp onion powder", "1 (8-oz) package cream cheese", "1 cup shredded cheddar cheese"]'::jsonb, '["Place chicken at bottom of slow cooker.", "Add corn, black beans, diced tomatoes and green chilies, chicken broth, cumin, chili powder, onion powder ranch seasoning and bacon. Stir together. Place cream cheese on top of chicken.", "Cover with lid and cook on LOW for 6-8 hours.", "Remove chicken from slow cooker and shred with 2 forks. Return to slow cooker. Stir cheddar cheese into chili."]'::jsonb, '["Plain Chicken", "chicken", "chili", "slow cooker", "cream cheese", "bacon"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from Plain Chicken (author: Stephanie @ Plain Chicken), printed 2/3/2021. Equipment: 6-qt slow cooker. Recipe note: Philadelphia brand cream cheese melts best in this recipe. Page 2: "Here is our recipe for Homemade Ranch Dressing Mix: https://www.plainchicken.com/homemade-ranch-dressing-mix/". Handwritten above the title on one of the two printouts: "Chicken enchilada soup". Two printouts of this recipe were photographed (identical text). Printed ingredient typo "boneles sskinless" corrected to "boneless skinless".', 'https://www.plainchicken.com/slow-cooker-cream-cheese-crack-chicken/'),
('Slow Cooker Creamy Garlic Chicken and Veggies', 'A one pot crockpot meal! Tender chicken, potatoes and broccoli! Served with the creamiest garlic sauce ever!', 6, 15, 375, '["6 bone-in, skin-on chicken thighs", "1 1/2 teaspoons smoked paprika", "kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper, to taste", "2 tablespoons unsalted butter", "2 pounds baby red potatoes, halved", "1/4 cup white wine", "1/4 cup chicken stock", "2 shallots, chopped", "3 cloves garlic, minced", "1 teaspoon dried thyme", "3 cups broccoli florets", "1/2 cup heavy cream", "1 1/2 tablespoons freshly squeezed lemon juice", "1 tablespoon cornstarch"]'::jsonb, '["Season chicken with paprika, salt and pepper, to taste.", "Melt butter in a large cast iron skillet over medium high heat. Add chicken, skin-side down, and sear both sides until golden brown, about 2-3 minutes per side; drain excess fat and set chicken aside.", "Place potatoes into a 6-qt slow cooker. Stir in wine, chicken stock, shallots, garlic and thyme; season with salt and pepper, to taste. Add chicken to the slow cooker in an even layer.", "Cover and cook on low heat for 5-6 hours, or until the chicken is completely cooked through, reaching an internal temperature of 165 degrees F. Add broccoli during the last 30 minutes of cooking time.", "Remove chicken, potatoes and broccoli from the slow cooker, cover and keep warm.", "In a small bowl, whisk together heavy cream, lemon juice and cornstarch. Stir into the slow cooker. Cover and cook on high heat for an additional 10-15 minutes, or until the sauce has thickened.", "Serve chicken, potatoes and broccoli immediately with cream sauce."]'::jsonb, '["Damn Delicious", "chicken", "slow cooker", "potatoes", "broccoli", "one pot"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from Damn Delicious (2 pages). Rated 4.9 stars (18 ratings) on the site. Total time 6 hours 30 minutes. Some words are washed out on the printout (see uncertain list).

Couldn''t read for sure: description: ''Tender'' is washed out (best reading ''Tender chicken''); ingredient ''baby red potatoes, halved'': ''potatoes'' partly washed out; step 7: last words washed out; best reading ''immediately with cream sauce''', 'https://damndelicious.net/2017/10/17/slow-cooker-creamy-garlic-chicken-and-veggies/'),
('Slow Cooker Ground Beef Stew', 'Ground Beef Stew is made in the slow cooker and it will make your house smell amazing! Kid friendly ground beef, potatoes, carrots in a richly seasoned tomato beef broth base. Serve with rolls or bread to soak up all the goodness.', 6, 20, 420, '["1 lb lean ground beef", "1 sweet onion finely diced", "1 teaspoon salt", "1 1/2 cups chopped Yukon gold or red potatoes peeled or unpeeled, about", "1 1/2 cup chopped baby carrots cut each baby carrot into 3-4 pieces", "3 cups reduced sodium beef broth", "1 can (10 oz) tomato soup", "1 can (6 oz) tomato paste w/ garlic, oregano, basil", "3 cloves garlic", "2 tablespoons Lipton Beefy Onion Soup Mix", "1 teaspoon dried parsley", "1 teaspoon dried Italian seasoning", "1 1/2 cups frozen peas", "cooking spray"]'::jsonb, '["Spray the insert of the slow cooker with cooking spray.", "In a skillet pan, over medium-high heat, brown and crumble the ground beef, onion, and salt. Once beef is no longer pink, drain the excess grease, and add it into the slow cooker.", "Add the chopped potatoes & carrots, beef broth, tomato soup, tomato paste, garlic, beefy onion soup mix, parsley, and Italian seasoning. Stir everything together.", "Put the lid on the slow cooker and cook on LOW heat for 7 hours. 1 hour before the cook time is done, add the frozen green peas. Let cook for the remaining cook time.", "* The stew may seem like it''s not thick enough, but as it sits after cooking (even after a few minutes) it will thicken up really nicely."]'::jsonb, '["Together as Family", "beef", "ground beef", "stew", "slow cooker", "American", "soup"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from Together as Family (author: Jessica), printed 2/3/2021. Course: Dinner; Cuisine: American; 247 kcal per serving. Page 1 of 2; page 2 (notes) was a separate photo. Text cut off at bottom of page 1: "** If you will be gone all day and will not be able to add the peas in 1 hour before the cook time you have two options. Add the peas in at the beginning with everything else. Yes the ..." (continues on page 2).', 'https://togetherasfamily.com/slow-cooker-hearty-ground-beef-stew/'),
('Slow Cooker Ham and Bean Soup', 'Ham and bean soup is a perfect cold weather meal. It is especially great if you have some leftover ham to use up. Make a pot and some cornbread today!', 12, 720, 480, '["2 pounds dry great northern beans", "2 tsp garlic powder", "1 1/2 tsp salt", "1 tsp pepper", "1 T chopped parsley", "1 bay leaf", "1 meaty ham bone", "8 cups water", "1 large onion, chopped", "1-2 cups ham, in about half inch cubes", "optional: 1/4 teaspoon cloves"]'::jsonb, '["Soak beans overnight. Drain and rinse.", "Add beans, spices, ham bone and water to your slow cooker. (I used a 6 quart insert)", "Cook on low for about 7-8 hours.", "Remove ham bone and bay leaf. Stir in onion and chopped ham. Continue to cook for another 30 minutes to an hour. (This give you time to make your cornbread!)", "For a thicker soup, remove a cup or so of the cooked beans. Mash them then stir them back into the pot."]'::jsonb, '["Cooking With Carlee", "ham", "beans", "soup", "slow cooker"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from Cooking With Carlee, printed 1/12/2021. Prep time 12 hours includes overnight soaking; total time 20 hours. Page 1 of 2; page 2 not in the photos (recipe looks complete on page 1). No URL visible on this page.', NULL),
('Slow Cooker Kielbasa Hash Brown Casserole', 'Super easy. It''s a dump meal. Total cost about $12 or less... this one feeds a lot.', NULL, NULL, 360, '["1 package kielbasa or smoked sausage (I use Ekrich Sausage) cut in chunks as shown in photo", "1 32 oz bag frozen hashbrowns", "1 small onion diced up", "2 cups of cheddar", "1/2 cup of sour cream", "1/2 cup of milk", "1 10oz can of cream mushroom or chicken soup", "salt and pepper", "minced garlic", "onion powder"]'::jsonb, '["Add sausage, hash browns, onion and cheese in a greased slow cooker (I use crockpot liners for easy clean up), then mix soup, milk, sour cream together.", "I add salt and pepper, minced garlic, & onion powder to the mixture to taste, then pour over sausage and hash browns.", "Next sprinkle about 1/2 cup more cheese on top.. cook on low for 6 hours or high for about 3-4 hours.", "Serve with salad, or roasted veggies for a complete meal, and maybe Texas garlic toast!"]'::jsonb, '["All Grandma''s Cooking Recipes", "Facebook", "sausage", "kielbasa", "potatoes", "slow cooker", "casserole", "dump meal"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Title supplied (the Facebook post has no title). Facebook post in the group "All Grandma''s Cooking Recipes" (page 1 of 3 printed); from Isabel Fleshman (group moderator). Uses about 1/2 cup more cheddar for the topping beyond the 2 cups listed. Cook on low 6 hours or high about 3-4 hours.', NULL),
('Smoked Queso Dip', 'Smoked queso dip kicks regular cheese dip a big notch with tons of flavor. This recipe features a silky smooth cheese base, spicy jalapeno and sausage and delicious smoky flavor from cooking.', 15, 5, 120, '["1 lb spicy ground sausage browned & strained of grease", "1 jalapeno seeded & diced, optional", "1/2 large white onion diced", "32 oz block Velveeta cheese cubed", "2 cans diced tomatoes with green chilies drained", "1 tbsp minced garlic"]'::jsonb, '["Add all of the ingredients to a (disposable) 9x13\" aluminum pan.", "Smoke at 250 degrees for 2 hours. Stir the queso 1/2 way through cooking.", "Use pot holders to carefully remove the pan from the smoker.", "Stir the dip a final time until everything''s smooth and evenly combined.", "Serve immediately, with chips for dipping."]'::jsonb, '["4 Sons R Us", "dip", "appetizer", "sausage", "smoker", "Tex-Mex"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Web printout by Meaghan @ 4 Sons R Us, page 1 of 2 (page 2, the rest of the nutrition info not in the photos). Course: Appetizer, Dip, Snack. Cuisine: American, Mexican, Tex Mex. 239 kcal. Recipe notes: Queso, especially this velveeta cheese based dip, begin to harden & congeal rather quickly. To keep it smooth & creamy for longer serving, transfer it to a slow cooker and leave it covered on the warm setting.', NULL),
('Smoked Sausage Cajun Alfredo', 'Smoked Sausage Cajun Alfredo - Only 5 ingredients - smoked sausage, pasta, cajun seasoning, heavy cream and parmesan - ready in under 15 minutes! No prep! Very similar to our all-time favorite Chicken Lazone, but with smoked sausage. OMG! AMAZING! Make this tonight! We ate it two nights in a row - it was that good!', 4, 5, 10, '["1 (14-oz) package turkey smoked sausage, cut into 1/4-inch slices", "8 ounces pasta", "2 cups heavy cream", "1 Tbsp Cajun seasoning", "1/2 cup grated Parmesan cheese"]'::jsonb, '["Prepare pasta according to package directions; drain and set aside.", "Saute sausage in a large skillet over medium-high heat for 5 minutes, turning occasionally.", "Add cream and Cajun seasoning; bring to a boil. Reduce heat; simmer gently for 3-4 minutes or until mixture begins to thicken.", "Remove from heat, stir in Parmesan cheese. Add pasta to sauce and toss."]'::jsonb, '["Plain Chicken", "sausage", "pasta", "Cajun", "alfredo", "quick"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'From Plain Chicken (web printout 1/2, printed 12/8/23). Author: Plain Chicken. Yield: 4 people. Recipe notes: To cut down on the calories, I used turkey smoked sausage. It tasted great and we couldn''t tell any difference from the regular smoked sausage. Page 2/2 not in the photos (the recipe is complete on page 1).

Couldn''t read for sure: Total Time value is hidden by glare (prep 5 + cook 10 = 15 mins); ''8- ounces pasta'' printed with a stray hyphen', 'https://www.plainchicken.com/smoked-sausage-cajun-alfredo/'),
('Smoky Spanish Rice with Shrimp plus Peas, Parsley & Aioli', NULL, 2, 10, 35, '["1 clove garlic", "1 lemon", "4 oz grape tomatoes", "1/4 oz parsley", "3/4 cup Arborio rice", "4 oz roasted red pepper spread", "1 tsp smoked paprika", "1 tsp turmeric", "2 seafood stock concentrates", "2 TBSP mayonnaise", "10 oz shrimp", "4 oz peas", "kosher salt", "black pepper", "4 tsp olive oil"]'::jsonb, '["Prep: Wash and dry produce. Peel and mince garlic. Quarter lemon. Halve tomatoes. Roughly chop parsley.", "Cook rice: Heat a large drizzle of olive oil in a large pan over medium-high heat. Stir rice, red pepper spread, half the paprika (you''ll use the rest later), half the turmeric (all for 4 servings), and half the garlic into pan; cook, stirring, until fragrant, 30-60 seconds. Stir in 3 cups water (6 cups for 4), stock concentrates, and salt. Bring to a boil. Cook, stirring occasionally, until liquid has evaporated and rice is tender, 15-20 minutes. (TIP: For a paella-like crust, cook rice undisturbed. Add a splash more water if liquid evaporates before rice is fully cooked.) Keep covered off heat until ready to serve.", "Make aioli: While rice cooks, in a small bowl, combine mayonnaise, a squeeze of lemon (two squeezes for 4 servings), and a pinch of garlic to taste. Add water 1 tsp at a time until aioli reaches a drizzling consistency. Season with salt and pepper.", "Season shrimp: Rinse shrimp* under cold water, then pat dry with paper towels. Season all over with remaining paprika, salt, and pepper. Set aside.", "Cook shrimp mixture: When rice is almost done, heat a large drizzle of olive oil in a second large pan over high heat. Once pan is hot, add tomatoes and cook, undisturbed, until lightly charred, 1-2 minutes. Add seasoned shrimp and stir to combine. Cook, stirring occasionally, until shrimp are opaque and cooked through, 3-4 minutes.", "Finish & serve: Fluff rice with a fork; stir in peas. Season with salt and pepper to taste. Divide Spanish rice between plates and top with shrimp mixture. Drizzle with aioli and sprinkle with parsley. Serve with remaining lemon wedges on the side. TIP: Serve directly from pan for a family-style paella experience."]'::jsonb, '["HelloFresh", "shrimp", "seafood", "Spanish", "rice", "paella-style"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'HelloFresh recipe card, WK 4-12. Calories: 720. Crunch Time: For added texture, in Step 2 let the tender rice cook undisturbed the last few minutes to form a delicious crust. Hello Aioli: a creamy, garlic-based mayo perfect for drizzling and dipping. *Shrimp are fully cooked when internal temperature reaches 145°. 4-person amounts: 2 cloves garlic, 2 lemons, 8 oz grape tomatoes, 1/2 oz parsley, 1 1/2 cups Arborio rice, 8 oz roasted red pepper spread, 2 tsp smoked paprika, 1 tsp turmeric, 4 seafood stock concentrates, 4 TBSP mayonnaise, 20 oz shrimp, 8 oz peas, 4 tsp olive oil.', NULL),
('Sour Cream Swiss Steak', 'One year, after we''d purchased half a beef from a local cattle raiser, I went on a full-scale search for new and different recipes. This is one I found—my family loved it from the very first bite. I''ve shared it with friends at work, too (I''m a waitress). They agree it''s a nice change from regular Swiss steak.', NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1/3 cup all-purpose flour", "1 1/2 teaspoons each salt, pepper, paprika and ground mustard", "3 pounds boneless round steak, cut into serving-size pieces", "3 tablespoons vegetable oil", "3 tablespoons butter", "1 1/2 cups water", "1 1/2 cups (12 ounces) sour cream", "1 cup finely chopped onion", "2 garlic cloves, minced", "1/3 cup soy sauce", "1/4 to 1/3 cup packed brown sugar", "3 tablespoons all-purpose flour", "additional paprika, optional"]'::jsonb, '["In a shallow bowl, combine flour, salt, pepper, paprika and mustard; dredge the steak. In a large skillet, heat oil [... text lost at the page break ...] water, cover and simmer for 30 minutes.", "In a bowl, combine the sour cream, onion, garlic, soy sauce, brown sugar and flour; stir until smooth. Transfer steak to a greased 2-1/2-qt. baking dish; add sour cream mixture. Cover and bake at 325° for 1-1/2 hours or until tender. Sprinkle with paprika if desired."]'::jsonb, '["Evernote", "beef", "steak", "Swiss steak", "baked"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'From Barb Benting, Grand Rapids, Michigan (Evernote printout, pages 2/3 and 3/3, dated 2/2/2021). The directions break across the two pages and a line or so is missing: page 2 ends "...In a large skillet, heat oil" (that line is cut off) and page 3 begins "...water, cover and simmer for 30 minutes." Presumably the steak is browned in the oil and butter, then the 1 1/2 cups water added, but that middle text is not visible. The yield at the end ("Yield: ...") is cut off. Page 1/3 was not in the photos.

Couldn''t read for sure: Middle of step 1 between ''heat oil'' and ''water, cover and simmer for 30 minutes'' is missing at the page break; Yield / servings cut off; ''cut into serving-size pieces'': ''cut'' is hidden by a stain (best reading)', NULL),
('Sourdough Bread', NULL, NULL, NULL, 48, '["100 g starter", "350 g water", "500 g flour", "10 g salt"]'::jsonb, '["Morning: in a glass bowl, 100 grams starter, 350 grams water (stir together), 500 grams flour (mix all), 10 grams salt.", "Cover with T-towel and let sit for 1 hour.", "Then start stretch & folds, 4 rounds 30 min apart (can be longer than 30 min).", "When stretch & folds are done, cover the dough with T-towel and let rise 3-4 hours.", "Time to shape your dough, then put in fridge in basket and cover with T-towel over night.", "Next morning, set oven to 450° with dutch oven in.", "Pull out dough and flip it over onto parchment paper. Put a small amount of flour on top and make your cuts.", "Pull out dutch oven and place dough and parchment paper in dutch oven. Cover with lid and bake for 30 min.", "Then uncover and set oven to 400° for 18 min.", "Pull out of Dutch Oven"]'::jsonb, '["bread", "sourdough", "dutch oven", "artisan bread"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten on loose-leaf paper; no title on the page (title supplied). Original spellings: ''Started'' (starter), ''Flower'' (flour), ''T-towl'' (tea towel), ''Strech'' (stretch), ''foe'' (for). The last line ''Pull out of Dutch Oven'' is at the bottom edge of the page; the recipe may continue on another page not in the photos.

Couldn''t read for sure: ''10 g salt'' in the top list (the ''0'' is overwritten; ''10 grams'' confirmed below)

A page of this recipe was missing from the photos.', NULL),
('Sourdough Pizza Crust (screenshot)', 'If you have an active sourdough starter, then you can make the world''s best sourdough pizza recipe. It''s so simple that you may never eat take-out pizza again!', 4, 360, 20, '["2 1/2 cups bread flour (10 oz, 300g)", "3/4 cup water (6 oz, 170g)", "1 cup sourdough starter (8 oz, 225g)", "1 tsp salt (0.25 oz, 7g)"]'::jsonb, '["Into a large bowl, pour the water measurement. Add the sourdough starter, bread flour measurement, and the salt.", "If you don''t have a sourdough starter, you can combine 2 oz water and 2 oz flour [cut off]"]'::jsonb, '["pizza", "sourdough", "Italian", "American", "dough"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Phone photo of a web-page printout (page 1 of 2). Course: Main Course; Cuisine: American, Italian. Equipment: baking stone or baking steel, Dutch whisk optional, parchment paper for transferring pizzas to the oven, pizza peel. Instructions cut off after step 2; page 2 not in the photos. Footer URL too small to read.

Couldn''t read for sure: first words of the description (''If you have an active'') are faint

A page of this recipe was missing from the photos.', NULL),
('Sourdough Pizza Crust (printed)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, '["1 cup active sourdough starter", "1 1/2 cups warm water", "4 cups bread flour", "1 teaspoon salt", "2 tablespoons olive oil"]'::jsonb, '["In a large mixing bowl, combine the sourdough starter and warm water.", "Add the bread flour and salt to the bowl, and mix until a shaggy dough forms.", "Drizzle the olive oil over the dough, and knead it in the bowl until the dough becomes smooth and elastic.", "Cover the bowl with a clean kitchen towel and let the dough rise at room temperature for 4-6 hours, or until it has doubled in size.", "Once the dough has risen, punch it down and divide it into two equal portions for two pizzas.", "On a floured surface, shape each portion of dough into a round ball and let it rest for 15-20 minutes.", "Preheat your oven to the highest temperature (usually around 500°F or higher) and prepare your pizza toppings.", "Press out the dough into the desired pizza shape, add your favorite toppings, and bake in the preheated oven for 10-12 minutes, or until the crust is golden brown and the cheese is bubbly."]'::jsonb, '["pizza", "sourdough", "Italian", "dough"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Printed page (no source shown). A different recipe from the ''Sourdough Pizza Crust Recipe'' screenshot. Makes two pizzas.

Couldn''t read for sure: ''warm water'', ''flour'', ''salt'', ''olive oil'' partly obscured by a stain but clear from the steps', NULL),
('Southern Apple Pie', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["2 gal cinnamon cider", "2 2-liter ginger ale", "11 cinnamon sticks", "1 pt green apple pucker", "1/5 (fifth) 100 proof Southern Comfort", "1/5 (fifth) pure grain alcohol - Everclear or 190 proof", "sugar to taste (about 1-1.5 cup + 2/3 cup)"]'::jsonb, '["Mix cider, ginger ale and cinnamon sticks and boil min.", "Cool for 1 hr (must be cool!).", "Add green apple pucker, Southern Comfort and grain alcohol; stir.", "Add sugar to taste, about 1-1.5 cup + 2/3 cup."]'::jsonb, '["drink", "alcoholic", "punch", "apple", "cinnamon"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten card taped in the notebook (photo is sideways). Steps are written as arrows between the ingredients: "mix + boil min", "cool for 1 hr (must be cool!)", "stir", "Add sugar to taste ≈ 1 - 1.5 cup + 2/3 cup". The boil time is not given.

Couldn''t read for sure: 2 gal (digit overwritten); 11 cinnamon sticks; ''boil min'' (number of minutes not written)', NULL),
('Southwestern-Style Mahi-Mahi Tacos with Roasted Corn Slaw', NULL, 2, NULL, 20, '["1/2 tsp smoked paprika", "1 1/2 fl oz chipotle ranch dressing", "8 oz slaw mix", "6 small flour tortillas", "3 oz fire roasted corn kernels", "1/4 oz cilantro", "2 fl oz chili lime dressing", "1 lime", "2 tsp garlic pepper", "12 oz mahi-mahi fillets", "olive oil", "salt"]'::jsonb, '["Prepare Ingredients and Make Slaw: All cook times are approximate based on testing. If using any fresh produce, thoroughly rinse and pat dry. Ingredient(s) used more than once: garlic pepper. Halve lime. Cut one half into wedges and juice the other half. Stem and tear cilantro. Add corn to a microwave-safe bowl. Microwave uncovered until heated through, 30-60 seconds. Remove corn from microwave. Add slaw mix, half the garlic pepper (reserve remaining for mahi-mahi), a pinch of salt, and chili lime dressing (to taste) to bowl with corn. Stir until combined and set aside.", "Prepare the Mahi-Mahi: Pat mahi-mahi dry and, on a separate cutting board, cut into 2\" pieces. Season all over with smoked paprika and remaining garlic pepper.", "Cook the Mahi-Mahi: Place a medium non-stick pan over medium heat and add 1 tsp. olive oil. Add mahi-mahi to hot pan. Cook until mahi-mahi reaches a minimum internal temperature of 145 degrees, 3-4 minutes per side. Fish thickness can vary; if you receive a thinner fillet, we recommend checking for doneness sooner. Remove from burner. Transfer mahi-mahi to a mixing bowl and toss with chipotle ranch dressing (to taste) and 2 tsp. lime juice.", "Warm Tortillas and Finish Dish: Wrap tortillas in a damp paper towel and microwave until warm, 30-60 seconds. Plate dish as pictured on front of card, filling tortillas with mahi-mahi and topping with slaw and cilantro. Squeeze lime wedges over to taste. Bon appétit!"]'::jsonb, '["Home Chef", "fish", "mahi-mahi", "tacos", "Mexican", "Southwestern", "Express Plus"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Home Chef Express Plus card. Prep & Cook Time 15-20 min; cook within 3 days; difficulty easy; spice level medium. Customize It Options (default 12 oz mahi-mahi fillets used above): 12 oz boneless skinless chicken breasts; 12 oz salmon fillets. Customize It Instructions: If using chicken breasts, pat dry and on a separate cutting board, cut into 1" dice. Season all over with smoked paprika and remaining garlic pepper. Follow same instructions as mahi-mahi in Step 3, cooking until chicken reaches minimum internal temperature, 5-7 minutes. If using salmon fillets, pat dry and season flesh side with smoked paprika and remaining garlic pepper. Follow same instructions as mahi-mahi in Step 3, cooking skin-side up first, until salmon reaches minimum internal temperature, 4-6 minutes per side. Once salmon cools, remove and discard skin and flake into 2" pieces. Minimum internal temperatures: 145° steak, pork, lamb, seafood; 160° ground beef, ground pork; 165° chicken, ground turkey. Handwritten check marks next to the chipotle ranch dressing and chili lime dressing on the ingredient list. Step 3 opening words are faded in the photo.

Couldn''t read for sure: Step 2 ''cut into 2" pieces'' (number faded; could be 1"); Step 3 ''Place a medium non-stick pan'' and ''1 tsp. olive oil'' and ''a minimum'' (faded)', 'https://www.homechef.com/25416'),
('Spaghetti Salad', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 lb. cooked spaghetti", "1/2 can Parmesan cheese", "1/2 bottle salad supreme or salad dressing", "sundried tomatoes", "2 chopped cucumbers", "1 (8 oz) Zesty Italian dressing", "1/2 green pepper", "1 onion"]'::jsonb, '["Cook spaghetti, add rest of the ingredients. Stir well."]'::jsonb, '["salad", "pasta", "side"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten "Here''s what''s cookin''" card on an Evernote printout (page 2 of 3). "2 chopped tomatoes" is crossed out and replaced with "Sundried tomatoes". "1 (8 oz) Zesty Italian dressing" is added in different handwriting at the end of the cucumber line; it may replace the salad supreme line.

Couldn''t read for sure: the ''1/2 bottle salad supreme or salad dressing'' line may be crossed out; sundried tomatoes amount not given', NULL),
('Spaghetti Sauce', NULL, 8, NULL, 150, '["4 lbs lean ground beef", "1 lb Italian sausage", "1 large onion, chopped", "2 cloves garlic, minced", "2 28 oz. cans whole tomatoes", "2 6 oz. cans tomato paste", "1 15 oz. can tomato sauce", "1 cup beef broth", "2 1/2 teas. salt", "1/2 teas. pepper", "2 teas. sugar", "1 teas. dried basil", "1 1/2 teas. dried oregano", "2 bay leaves", "1 tbls. Worcestershire sauce", "3/4 cup Parmesan cheese"]'::jsonb, '["Brown beef & sausage. Add onions & garlic & cook until limp. Stir in tomatoes, paste, sauce, broth, salt, pepper, sugar, basil, oregano, bay leaves & Worcestershire. Simmer uncovered about 2 1/2 hrs. Add cheese. Continue to simmer, stirring often."]'::jsonb, '["sauce", "Italian", "beef", "sausage", "pasta", "handwritten"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe card. No. servings: 8-10. Handwritten note by the title: "watch salt measurement - can be to salty". Variation (handwritten on the card): "Don''t use tomato sauce, add pesto (basil) in jar about 1/4 of jar. To spice up added red pepper." Handwritten conversions at the bottom: "2 tablespoons fresh basil = 1 teas dried basil; 4 teas fresh oregano = 1 1/2 teas dried oregano". The line above the card title ("Cream or whipped cream.") is the end of a different recipe, not part of this one.

Couldn''t read for sure: ground beef amount: best reading "4 lbs" (could be 1 or 2 lbs; first digit is faded); "1 large onion" ("large" is faded); "2 cloves garlic" ("cloves" is faded); servings "8-10" (faint, at edge); "1/4 of jar" in the variation note', NULL),
('Spaghetti Squash Burrito Bowls', 'A hearty vegetarian dinner for two of roasted spaghetti squash halves stuffed with a flavorful southwestern veggie and cheese filling.', 2, 20, 50, '["1 small spaghetti squash, about 30 ounces or 1.8 lb whole", "1/2 teaspoon olive oil", "salt and black pepper", "1 to 2 teaspoons olive oil", "1 small zucchini, diced", "half a bell pepper, diced", "1/4 red onion, diced", "1/2 teaspoon dried oregano", "1/4 teaspoon ground cumin", "salt and black pepper", "3/4 cup cooked black beans, drained and rinsed if using canned", "1/2 cup corn kernels, drained well if using canned", "1/2 cup salsa", "2 ounces cheese, shredded and divided"]'::jsonb, '["Cook The Squash: Preheat your oven to 425°F. If using a toaster oven select the “BAKE” setting and use the bottom rack placement. Lightly oil a baking sheet or line with a silicone baking mat.", "Squash (step 2): Use a sharp knife to carefully stab the squash a few times on each side, then microwave 4 to 5 minutes. Watching out for steam, slice the squash in half and scoop out the seeds.", "Squash (step 3): Rub each half with oil and season well with salt and black pepper. Place squash on the pan and cook until fork-tender, about 30 to 45 minutes, depending on the size of your squash.", "Squash (step 4): Remove squash from the oven and cool for at least 5 minutes. Then, scrape a fork along the flesh to create spaghetti-like strands (leave a little behind to keep the ''bowl'' intact for stuffing later).", "Prepare Filling: While the squash cooks, heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat. Add the onion, zucchini, bell pepper, cumin, oregano, salt and pepper. Cook, stirring frequently until the vegetables have softened, about 8 to 10 minutes.", "Prepare Filling: Remove skillet from heat, add black beans, corn, and salsa. Stir well, taste, and adjust seasoning as desired.", "Assembly: Add the loose spaghetti strands and half of the cheese to the skillet mixture, stir well. Load up the squash bowls with the filing and top with the remaining cheese.", "Bake The Bowls: Bake uncovered at 350°F until warmed through and melty, about 10 minutes.", "Bake The Bowls: Then Broil for 1 to 2 minutes until the cheese is bubbly and browned.", "Bake The Bowls: Serve warm with your favorite burrito toppings."]'::jsonb, '["Toaster Oven Love", "vegetarian", "spaghetti squash", "Mexican", "burrito bowl", "toaster oven"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Toaster Oven Love printout, pages 1 and 2 of 3, joined. Recipe notes: You can store the assembled boats in a covered container in the fridge for 2 to 3 days. To rel[heat, bake] at 350°F until warmed through and the cheese is melted about 25 minutes. (Right edge of that line is cut off.) Nutritional information is an estimate of one bowl without any toppings. Yield: 2 bowls; serving size: 1 spaghetti squash burrito bowl. Per serving: calories 390, total fat 17.1g, saturated fat 7.2g, cholesterol 29mg, sodium 630mg, carbohydrates 51.4g, fiber 6.1g, sugar 5.4g, protein 15.7g. Cuisine: American. Category: Toaster Oven Meals. © Brie Norris. Recipe page: toasterovenlove.com/spaghetti-squash-burrito-bowls/.

Couldn''t read for sure: notes: the reheating sentence is cut off at the right edge after ''To rel''', 'https://toasterovenlove.com/wp-json/mv-create/v1/creations/51/print'),
('Spanish-Spiced Tilapia & Farro with Aioli & Pan Con Tomate', 'We''re calling on the bold flavors of Spanish cuisine by seasoning flaky tilapia with traditional spices like paprika, coriander, and more—all plated over a hearty bed of farro and vegetables. Served alongside is our take on pan con tomate (a staple dish of toasted bread topped with garlic and fresh tomato).', 4, NULL, 50, '["4 tilapia fillets", "1 cup semi-pearled farro", "1/2 lb grape tomatoes", "2 scallions", "1 pinch saffron", "2 Tbsps mayonnaise", "1 Tbsp Spanish spice blend (smoked paprika, ground cumin, ground coriander, dried Mexican oregano, cayenne pepper & ground cinnamon)", "2 small baguettes", "1 oz sliced roasted red peppers", "2 cloves garlic", "1 lemon", "2 Tbsps sherry vinegar", "6 oz shishito peppers"]'::jsonb, '["Prepare the ingredients & make the lemon aioli: Place an oven rack in the center of the oven, then preheat to 450°F. Fill a medium pot 3/4 of the way up with salted water; cover and heat to boiling on high. Wash and dry the fresh produce. Thinly slice the scallions, separating the white bottoms and hollow green tops. Roughly chop the roasted peppers. Halve the baguettes. Halve the tomatoes; place in a bowl and season with salt and pepper. Quarter and deseed the lemon. Peel 2 cloves of garlic; leaving one clove whole, using a zester, finely grate the remaining clove into a paste (or use the small side of a box grater). In a bowl, combine the mayonnaise, the juice of 2 lemon wedges, and up to half the garlic paste. Taste, then season with salt and pepper if desired. Cut off and discard the stems of the shishito peppers; cut crosswise into 1-inch pieces. Wash your hands, knife, and cutting board immediately after handling.", "Char the shishito peppers: In a large pan (nonstick, if you have one), heat a drizzle of olive oil on medium-high until hot. Add the shishito pepper pieces in an even layer. Cook, without stirring, 4 to 5 minutes, or until charred. Add the sliced white bottoms of the scallions; season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, 1 to 2 minutes, or until softened. Transfer to a bowl; cover with foil to keep warm. Wipe out the pan.", "Cook & finish the farro: Add the farro and saffron to the pot of boiling water. Cook, uncovered, 18 to 20 minutes, or until tender. Turn off the heat. Drain thoroughly and return to the pot. Add the charred shishito peppers, chopped roasted peppers, the juice of the remaining lemon wedges, and a drizzle of olive oil; stir to combine. Taste, then season with salt and pepper if desired.", "Cook the fish: Meanwhile, pat the fish dry with paper towels. Season on both sides with salt, pepper, and enough of the spice blend to coat (you may have extra). In the same pan, heat a drizzle of olive oil on medium-high until hot. Add the seasoned fish. Cook 3 to 4 minutes per side, or until browned and cooked through.* Leaving any browned bits (or fond) in the pan, transfer to a plate and cover with foil to keep warm.", "Toast the baguettes: Meanwhile, place the halved baguettes, cut side up, on a sheet pan. Drizzle with olive oil; season with salt and pepper. Bake 7 to 9 minutes, or until lightly browned. Transfer to a cutting board. Rub the cut sides of the toasted baguettes with the whole garlic clove; discard the clove.", "Make the pan con tomate & serve your dish: In the pan of reserved fond, heat a drizzle of olive oil on medium-high until hot. Add the seasoned tomatoes. Cook, stirring frequently and pressing with the back of a spoon, 2 to 3 minutes, or until softened. Add the vinegar (carefully, as the liquid may splatter), remaining garlic paste, and 1/4 cup of water; season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring frequently, 1 to 2 minutes, or until slightly thickened and the tomatoes are broken down. Turn off the heat. Taste, then season with salt and pepper if desired. Top the toasted baguette with the cooked tomatoes and a drizzle of olive oil. Carefully cut each piece in half. Serve the finished farro with the cooked fish and pan con tomate. Top the fish with the lemon aioli. Garnish with the sliced green tops of the scallions. Enjoy!"]'::jsonb, '["Blue Apron", "fish", "tilapia", "Spanish", "farro"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Blue Apron recipe card. Wine match: Light & Fresh. Did You Know? (shishito peppers): While generally a more mild variety, these can occasionally be quite spicy. *An instant-read thermometer should register 145°F. Steps also use olive oil, salt and pepper (not in the printed ingredient list).', NULL),
('Spiced Pumpkin Waffles', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["2.5 c. flour", "1 tbls baking powder", "2 teas. cinnamon", "1 teas. ginger", "1/2 teas. baking soda", "1/2 teas. salt", "1/2 teas. ground nutmeg", "1/2 teas. cloves", "4 eggs", "2 cups buttermilk", "1 c. pumpkin puree", "1/2 c. brown sugar", "1/2 c. butter", "1 teas. pure vanilla extract"]'::jsonb, '["Combine flour, baking powder, cinnamon, ginger, baking soda, salt, nutmeg + cloves, set aside.", "Mix the rest in batter and then put dry in mixer."]'::jsonb, '["waffles", "pumpkin", "breakfast"]'::jsonb, '["breakfast"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten notebook page. The same page is also partly visible (sideways, left edge) in photo c544bc26.

Couldn''t read for sure: title ''Spiced'' is faint; 2.5 c. flour (first digit faint, could be 3.5); ''mix the rest in batter'' (word could be ''butter'')', NULL),
('Spicy Chicken Stir-Fry with Carrots & Green Beans', 'This easy stir-fry brings together tender bites of chicken, green beans, and carrots with a unique sauce made with soy glaze, sesame oil, and our own black bean-chile sauce—for savory flavor and a layer of subtle heat in every bite.', 4, NULL, 30, '["18 oz chopped chicken breast", "1 cup long grain white rice", "3/4 lb carrots", "6 oz green beans", "1 Tbsp sesame oil", "1/4 cup rice flour", "1 Tbsp rice vinegar", "3 Tbsps soy glaze", "1/3 cup Asian-style sautéed aromatics", "1/3 cup savory black bean-chile sauce"]'::jsonb, '["Prepare the ingredients & make the sauce: Wash and dry the fresh produce. Peel the carrots; thinly slice on an angle. Halve the green beans. In a bowl, whisk together the soy glaze, sesame oil, vinegar, and black bean-chile sauce.", "Cook the rice: In a medium pot, combine the rice, a big pinch of salt, and 2 cups of water; heat to boiling on high. Once boiling, reduce the heat to low. Cover and cook, without stirring, 12 to 14 minutes, or until the water has been absorbed and the rice is tender. Turn off the heat and fluff with a fork. Cover to keep warm.", "Cook the vegetables: Meanwhile, in a large pan (nonstick, if you have one), heat the sautéed aromatics on medium-high until hot. Add the sliced carrots; season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, 3 to 4 minutes, or until slightly softened. Add the halved green beans; season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, 3 to 4 minutes, or until the vegetables are lightly browned and softened. Transfer to a bowl. Wipe out the pan.", "Coat & brown the chicken: Pat the chicken dry with paper towels. Place in a bowl; season with salt and pepper. Add the flour and toss to thoroughly coat. In the same pan, heat a thin layer of oil on medium-high. Once the oil is hot enough that a pinch of flour sizzles immediately when added, add the coated chicken in an even layer (discarding any excess flour before adding). Cook, without stirring, 3 to 4 minutes, or until lightly browned. Continue to cook, stirring occasionally, 2 to 3 minutes, or until browned.", "Finish & serve your dish: To the pan, add the cooked vegetables and sauce (carefully, as the liquid may splatter). Cook, stirring frequently, 1 to 2 minutes, or until coated and the chicken is cooked through. Turn off the heat. Serve the finished chicken and vegetables over the cooked rice. Enjoy!"]'::jsonb, '["Blue Apron", "chicken", "stir-fry", "Asian", "rice", "spicy"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Blue Apron recipe card. Steps also use oil (a thin layer for browning the chicken), salt and pepper. Wine pairing: Crisp & Minerally. Nutrition per serving (as prepared): Calories 640, Total Carbohydrates 80g, Dietary Fiber 5g, Added Sugars 14g, Total Fat 20g, Saturated Fat 4.5g, Protein 36g, Sodium 1590mg.

Couldn''t read for sure: carrots amount: best reading ''3/4 lb'' (small print); aromatics amount: best reading ''1/3 cup''', NULL),
('Spicy Chicken Stir-Fry with Gai Lan & Sweet Peppers', 'This easy stir-fry combines tender bites of chicken and vegetables with a unique sauce made with soy glaze, sesame oil, and our own black bean-chile sauce—for savory flavor and a layer of subtle heat in every bite. A simple bed of jasmine rice is perfect for catching all of the flavorful sauce.', 4, NULL, 30, '["1 1/8 lbs chopped chicken breast", "1/2 lb sweet peppers", "1 Tbsp sesame oil", "1 Tbsp rice vinegar", "2 Tbsps ghee", "1/2 cup Asian-style sautéed aromatics", "1 cup jasmine rice", "3/4 lb gai lan", "1/4 cup rice flour", "3 Tbsps soy glaze", "1/3 cup savory black bean-chile sauce"]'::jsonb, '["Cook the rice: In a medium pot, combine the rice, a big pinch of salt, and 2 cups of water; heat to boiling on high. Once boiling, reduce the heat to low. Cover and cook, without stirring, 12 to 14 minutes, or until the water has been absorbed and the rice is tender. Turn off the heat and fluff with a fork. Cover to keep warm.", "Prepare the ingredients & make the sauce: Meanwhile, wash and dry the fresh produce. Cut off and discard the bottom 1/2 inch of the gai lan stems; thinly slice, separating the stems and leaves. Cut off and discard the stems of the peppers; remove the cores, then quarter lengthwise. Transfer to a bowl; add the sliced gai lan stems. In a separate bowl, whisk together the soy glaze, sesame oil, vinegar, and black bean-chile sauce.", "Cook the vegetables: In a large pan (nonstick, if you have one), heat the sautéed aromatics on medium-high until hot. Add the prepared peppers and gai lan stems; season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, 4 to 5 minutes, or until lightly browned and softened. Add the sliced gai lan leaves; season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring frequently, 1 to 2 minutes, or until wilted. Transfer to a bowl and cover with foil to keep warm. Rinse and wipe out the pan.", "Start the stir-fry: Pat the chicken dry with paper towels. Place in a bowl; season with salt and pepper. Add the flour and toss to thoroughly coat. In the same pan, heat the ghee on medium-high until melted. Once the ghee is hot enough that a pinch of flour sizzles immediately when added, add the coated chicken (discarding any excess flour) in an even layer. Cook, without stirring, 3 to 4 minutes, or until lightly browned. Continue to cook, stirring occasionally, 2 to 3 minutes, or until browned.", "Finish the stir-fry & serve your dish: To the pan, add the cooked vegetables and sauce (carefully, as the liquid may splatter). Cook, stirring frequently, 1 to 2 minutes, or until combined and the chicken is cooked through. Turn off the heat. Taste, then season with salt and pepper if desired. Serve the finished stir-fry over the cooked rice. Enjoy!"]'::jsonb, '["Blue Apron", "chicken", "stir-fry", "Asian", "rice", "spicy"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Blue Apron recipe card. Did You Know? The Asian-style sautéed aromatics are a flavorful mix that combines garlic, ginger, onions, and scallions. Wine pairing: Zesty & Tropical. Steps also use salt and pepper.

Couldn''t read for sure: subtitle partly obscured by glare: best reading ''with Gai Lan & Sweet Peppers''', NULL),
('Spicy Fish & Guacamole Tacos with Roasted Potatoes & Tomatillo Sour Cream', 'We''re bringing bold, smoky flavor to these tacos by searing flaky fish with a coating of Mexican-style spices before tucking them into warm tortillas alongside a spicy, crunchy slaw and guacamole for cooling contrast. We''re pairing a side of roasted potatoes with a creamy tomatillo-poblano dipping sauce to round out the dish with even more vibrant flavor.', 4, NULL, 35, '["21 oz wild Alaskan pollock fillets", "1/2 lb green cabbage", "1 1/4 lbs red potatoes", "1/3 cup tomatillo-poblano sauce", "2 Tbsps ghee", "1/2 cup guacamole", "1/4 cup mayonnaise", "8 flour tortillas", "1 lime", "1/4 cup sour cream", "1/4 cup rice flour", "2 tsps chipotle chile paste", "1 Tbsp Mexican spice blend (ancho chile powder, smoked paprika, garlic powder, ground cumin & dried Mexican oregano)"]'::jsonb, '["Prepare & roast the potatoes: Remove the ghee from the refrigerator to bring to room temperature. Place an oven rack in the center of the oven, then preheat to 450°F. Wash and dry the fresh produce. Cut the potatoes into 1/4-inch-thick rounds. Place on a sheet pan. Drizzle with olive oil and season with salt and pepper. Toss to coat; arrange in an even layer. Roast 21 to 23 minutes, or until browned and tender when pierced with a fork. Remove from the oven.", "Prepare the remaining ingredients: Meanwhile, in a large bowl, combine the mayonnaise and up to half the chile paste, depending on how spicy you''d like the dish to be. Cut out and discard the core of the cabbage; thinly slice the leaves. Transfer to the bowl of chile mayo; season with salt and pepper and stir to coat. Quarter the lime. In a bowl, combine the guacamole and the juice of 2 lime wedges; season with salt and pepper. In a separate bowl, combine the sour cream and tomatillo-poblano sauce. Season with salt and pepper.", "Coat & cook the fish: On a large plate, combine the flour and spice blend; season with salt and pepper. Pat the fish dry with paper towels. Transfer to a cutting board; halve each fillet crosswise. Season with salt and pepper on both sides. Thoroughly coat the seasoned fish in the seasoned flour. In a large pan (nonstick, if you have one), heat half the ghee and 1 teaspoon of olive oil on medium-high until hot. Working in two batches, add the coated fish (shaking off any excess flour before adding). Cook 2 to 3 minutes per side, or until browned and cooked through* (adding the remaining ghee and 1 teaspoon of olive oil between batches). Transfer to a paper towel-lined plate.", "Warm the tortillas: Meanwhile, if you prefer to use the microwave, wrap the tortillas in a damp paper towel; microwave on high 1 minute, or until heated through. If using the oven, wrap the tortillas in foil and place directly onto an oven rack; warm 7 to 9 minutes, or until heated through. Transfer the warmed tortillas to a work surface and carefully unwrap.", "Finish the tacos & serve your dish: Assemble the tacos using the warmed tortillas, seasoned guacamole, cooked fish, and cabbage slaw. Serve the finished tacos with the roasted potatoes, tomatillo sour cream, and remaining lime wedges on the side. Enjoy!"]'::jsonb, '["Blue Apron", "fish", "tacos", "Mexican", "pollock"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Blue Apron recipe card. Wine match: Floral & Aromatic. Step 3 has an asterisk after "cooked through" but its footnote is not printed on the photographed steps page. Steps also use olive oil, salt and pepper (not in the printed ingredient list).', NULL),
('Squash Casserole', NULL, 6, NULL, 30, '["1/2-1 large onion, chopped", "4-8 tablespoons butter", "1-2 cups cooked squash, drained, with all water squeezed out", "2 1/2 cups crushed Ritz crackers, plus additional for topping", "1/2-1 cup sour cream", "1 teaspoon House Seasoning (see page 160)", "1 cup grated Cheddar cheese"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat oven to 350 degrees. Sauté onion in butter for 5 minutes. Remove from pan and mix all ingredients together. Pour into buttered casserole dish and top with cracker crumbs. Bake for 25 to 30 minutes."]'::jsonb, '["The Lady & Sons", "squash", "casserole", "side", "vegetarian", "Southern"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'From The Lady & Sons cookbook, page 76 (Vegetables and Side Dishes). Handwritten edits on the page: the printed amounts were crossed out and replaced by hand: onion ''1 large'' changed to ''1/2-1''; butter ''4 tablespoons (1/2 stick)'' marked ''4-8''; squash ''2 cups'' crossed out with ''12'' written (probably ''1-2''); Ritz crackers ''1/2 cup'' overwritten with ''2 1/2'' (unclear); sour cream ''1/2 cup'' changed to ''1/2-1''. Printed VARIATION: For a different taste in this casserole, layer slices of cooked red potatoes in the bottom of the casserole dish, followed by squash mixture; repeat layers. Top with about 1 cup Ritz crumbs tossed with melted butter. (Right edge of the variation text is slightly cut off.) The next recipe on the page, Sherry-Glazed Sweet Potatoes, is cut off at the bottom of the photo.

Couldn''t read for sure: handwritten squash amount: written ''12'' over crossed-out ''2 cups''; best reading ''1-2'' (could be ''12''); handwritten Ritz amount: ''2 1/2'' written over printed ''1/2''; could be ''2/3'' or ''2 1/3''; printed original sour cream amount under the handwriting: best reading ''1/2 cup''', NULL),
('Steak and Shrimp Kabobs', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 cup teriyaki sauce", "1 can pineapple juice", "1/2 cup brown sugar", "6 garlic cloves", "1/4 teas worcestershire sauce", "1/8 teas. pepper", "1 pound of shrimp", "1 pound of mushroom", "2 large green peppers", "2 medium onions", "1 1/2 teas. cornstarch"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '["shrimp", "steak", "kabobs", "grilling", "teriyaki"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe card ("Recipe for steak and shrimp kabobs"), ingredients only, no directions. No amount of steak is listed on the card.

Couldn''t read for sure: title spelled ''kabatis'' on the card, read as kabobs; 2 large green peppers (could be 3); 1/4 teas worcestershire sauce', NULL),
('Steaks & Black Bean-Butter Sauce with Roasted Vegetables & Gochujang Potatoes', 'We''re putting an Asian-style twist on the classic steakhouse dish by topping seared steaks with a rich combination of black bean sauce—a favorite condiment in Chinese cuisine—and butter. To round out the dish we''re making two hearty sides of gochujang-roasted potatoes and a trio of green beans, scallions, and broccoli finished with sweet soy glaze.', 4, NULL, 45, '["4 steaks", "6 oz green beans", "2 scallions", "1 Tbsp sesame oil", "2 Tbsps rice vinegar", "1 Tbsp light brown sugar", "1 tsp black & white sesame seeds", "1 1/4 lbs golden potatoes", "1 lb broccoli", "1 Tbsp gochujang", "2 Tbsps black bean sauce", "2 Tbsps butter", "2 Tbsps soy glaze"]'::jsonb, '["Prepare the ingredients & start the sauce: Preheat the oven to 450°F. Wash and dry the fresh produce. Large dice the potatoes. Cut off and discard the bottom 1/2 inch of the broccoli stem; cut the broccoli into small florets. Cut the scallions into 1-inch pieces. Cut off and discard the stem ends of the green beans. In a bowl, whisk together the black bean sauce, sugar, 1/2 cup of water, and half the vinegar (you will have extra). Season with salt and pepper.", "Roast the potatoes: In a large bowl, whisk together the sesame oil and as much of the gochujang as you''d like, depending on how spicy you''d like the potatoes to be. Add the diced potatoes; season with salt and pepper. Stir to thoroughly coat. Transfer to a sheet pan; arrange in an even layer. Roast 24 to 26 minutes, or until browned and tender when pierced with a fork. Remove from the oven.", "Roast & finish the vegetables: Meanwhile, on a separate sheet pan, combine the broccoli florets, scallion pieces, and prepared green beans. Drizzle with olive oil and season with salt and pepper. Toss to coat; arrange in an even layer. Roast 16 to 18 minutes, or until browned and tender when pierced with a fork. Remove from the oven. Evenly top with the soy glaze; carefully toss to coat.", "Cook the steaks: Meanwhile, pat the steaks dry with paper towels; season with salt and pepper on all sides. In a large pan, heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil on medium-high until hot. Add the seasoned steaks. Cook, turning occasionally, 8 to 10 minutes for medium-rare, or until browned and cooked to your desired degree of doneness.* Leaving any browned bits (or fond) in the pan, transfer to a cutting board and let rest at least 5 minutes.", "Finish the sauce & serve your dish: Meanwhile, add the sauce to the pan of reserved fond (carefully, as the liquid may splatter). Cook on medium-high, stirring frequently and scraping up any fond, 3 to 5 minutes, or until slightly thickened. Turn off the heat. Stir in the butter until melted and combined. Taste, then season with salt and pepper if desired. Find the lines of muscle (or grain) on the rested steaks; slice crosswise against the grain. Serve the sliced steaks with the roasted potatoes and finished vegetables. Top the steaks with the finished sauce. Garnish with the sesame seeds. Enjoy!"]'::jsonb, '["Blue Apron", "beef", "steak", "Asian", "Korean", "potatoes"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Blue Apron recipe card. Handwritten on the front of the card: "A+ 100%". Wine match: Rich & Decadent. *An instant-read thermometer should register 145°F. Steps also use olive oil, salt and pepper (not in the printed ingredient list).', NULL),
('Steaks & Tomatillo Sour Cream with Zucchini, Peppers & Roasted Potatoes', 'This steakhouse-style recipe gets a bold lift in two ways: an irresistibly creamy tomatillo-poblano sauce that tops the steaks and the smoky spice blend (which stars two kinds of paprika) we''re using to coat the roasted potatoes served underneath. It''s all complete with the trio of sautéed veggies that''s folded into the smoky potatoes.', 4, NULL, 50, '["4 steaks", "2 zucchini", "4 oz sweet peppers", "2 cloves garlic", "1/3 cup tomatillo-poblano sauce", "1 Tbsp red wine vinegar", "1 1/4 lbs golden potatoes", "1 red onion", "2 scallions", "1/2 cup sour cream", "1 Tbsp smoky spice blend (smoked paprika, sweet paprika, ground yellow mustard, garlic powder & onion powder)"]'::jsonb, '["Prepare the ingredients: Place an oven rack in the center of the oven, then preheat to 450°F. Wash and dry the fresh produce. Medium dice the potatoes. Halve, peel, and medium dice the onion. Medium dice the zucchini. Combine the diced onion and diced zucchini in a bowl. Cut off and discard the stems of the peppers; remove the cores, then large dice. Peel and roughly chop 2 cloves of garlic. Thinly slice the scallions, separating the white bottoms and hollow green tops. In a bowl, combine the diced peppers, chopped garlic, and sliced white bottoms of the scallions. In a separate bowl, whisk together the sour cream and tomatillo-poblano sauce. Taste, then season with salt and pepper if desired.", "Roast the potatoes: Line a sheet pan with foil. Place the diced potatoes on the foil. Drizzle with 1 tablespoon of olive oil and season with salt, pepper, and enough of the spice blend to coat (you may have extra). Toss to thoroughly coat; arrange in an even layer. Roast 20 to 22 minutes, or until browned and tender when pierced with a fork. Carefully transfer to a large bowl. Cover with foil to keep warm.", "Cook the steaks: Meanwhile, pat the steaks dry with paper towels; season with salt and pepper on all sides. In a large pan, heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil on medium-high until hot. Add the seasoned steaks. Cook, turning occasionally, 8 to 10 minutes for medium-rare, or until browned and cooked to your desired degree of doneness.* Leaving any browned bits (or fond) in the pan, transfer to a cutting board and cover with foil to keep warm. Let rest at least 5 minutes.", "Cook the vegetables: In the pan of reserved fond, heat 2 teaspoons of olive oil on medium-high until hot. Add the diced onion and zucchini in an even layer. Cook, without stirring, 2 to 3 minutes, or until lightly browned. Add the prepared pepper mixture and vinegar; season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally and scraping up any fond, 4 to 6 minutes, or until the vegetables are browned and softened. Turn off the heat.", "Finish & serve your dish: To the bowl of roasted potatoes, add the cooked vegetables and a drizzle of olive oil. Stir to combine. Taste, then season with salt and pepper if desired. Find the lines of muscle (or grain) on the rested steaks; slice crosswise against the grain. Serve the finished vegetables topped with the sliced steaks and tomatillo sour cream. Garnish with the sliced green tops of the scallions. Enjoy!"]'::jsonb, '["Blue Apron", "beef", "steak", "potatoes", "Southwestern"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Blue Apron recipe card. *An instant-read thermometer should register 145°F. Steps also use olive oil, salt and pepper. Wine pairing: Rich & Decadent.', NULL),
('Sticky Honey Garlic Sesame Steak Strips with Jasmine Rice and Bok Choy', NULL, 2, NULL, 35, '["1 lime", "1/2 fl. oz. honey", "1 tsp. Asian garlic, ginger & chile seasoning", "3 fl. oz. garlic sesame sauce", "2 garlic cloves", "1/4 tsp. red pepper flakes", "3/4 cup jasmine rice", "2 heads of baby bok choy", "10 oz. steak strips", "olive oil", "salt", "pepper"]'::jsonb, '["Cook the Rice: If using any fresh produce, thoroughly rinse and pat dry. Bring a small pot with rice and 1 1/2 cups water to a boil. Once boiling, reduce to a simmer, cover, and cook until rice is tender, 15-18 minutes. Remove from burner. Add half the Asian garlic, ginger & chile seasoning (to taste) and fluff rice with a fork to combine. Add remaining seasoning, if desired. Cover and set aside. While rice cooks, continue recipe.", "Prepare the Ingredients: Remove any discolored outer leaves from bok choy and trim ends. Cut stems into 1/4\" slices and coarsely chop leaves, keeping stems and leaves separate. Halve lime. Quarter one half and juice the other half. Mince garlic. Pat steak strips dry. Coarsely chop, then separate pieces. Season all over with 1/4 tsp. salt and a pinch of pepper.", "Cook the Bok Choy: Place a large non-stick pan over medium-high heat and add 1 tsp. olive oil. Add bok choy stems to hot pan and stir occasionally until softened, 5-7 minutes. Add garlic, bok choy leaves, 1/4 tsp. salt, and a pinch of pepper. Stir often until leaves are just wilted, 1-2 minutes. Add 1 Tbsp. lime juice and bring to a simmer. Once simmering, remove from burner. Transfer bok choy to a plate and tent with foil. Keep pan over medium-high heat.", "Cook the Steak Strips: Add 1 tsp. olive oil and steak strips to hot pan and stir occasionally until no pink remains and steak strips reach a minimum internal temperature of 145 degrees, 4-6 minutes. Stir in garlic sesame sauce and honey. Bring to a simmer. Once simmering, stir occasionally until sauce coats steak strips, 1-2 minutes. Remove from burner.", "Finish the Dish: If desired, combine steak strips with bok choy. Plate dish as pictured on front of card, topping rice with bok choy and steak strips, and garnishing with red pepper flakes (to taste). Squeeze lime quarters over dish to taste. Bon appétit!"]'::jsonb, '["Home Chef", "beef", "steak", "Asian", "rice bowl"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Home Chef meal kit card (homechef.com/21135). Prep & Cook Time: 25-35 min. Cook within 6 days. Difficulty: Intermediate. Spice level: Medium (the Asian garlic, ginger & chile seasoning and red pepper flakes are marked with chile icons). Customize It Options: 10 oz. steak strips (default); 8 oz. shrimp; 10 oz. diced boneless skinless chicken breasts; 20 oz. steak strips - double portion. Customize It Instructions: If using 20 oz. steak strips, follow same instructions as 10 oz. steak strips, working in batches if necessary. If using diced chicken breasts, pat dry and season all over with 1/4 tsp. salt and a pinch of pepper. Follow same instructions as steak strips in Step 4, stirring occasionally until chicken reaches minimum internal temperature, 5-7 minutes. If using shrimp, pat dry and season all over with 1/4 tsp. salt and a pinch of pepper. Follow same instructions as steak strips in Step 4, cooking until shrimp reach minimum internal temperature, 2-3 minutes per side.', NULL),
('Stuffed Pepperoni Pizza Crescent Rolls', 'This Stuffed Pepperoni Pizza Crescent Rolls Recipe is a kid friendly appetizer or after school snack that is not only easy to make, but it tastes amazing too!', 8, 10, 14, '["1 tube crescent rolls", "1 package mini pepperoni", "1 cup mozarella cheese shredded", "2 tbsp butter melted", "1/4 tsp garlic salt", "1 tbsp chives chopped"]'::jsonb, '["Pre-heat your oven to 375°", "Separate your crescent rolls into individual triangles and lay on your baking sheet lined with a silicone mat or parchment paper (not required but it helps them not burn on the bottom).", "Add your favorite toppings to the wide end and top with shredded mozzarella cheese.", "Fold the ends inwards to keep your toppings in place and roll shut.", "Bake at 375° for 12-14 minutes. They are done when the tops are a nice golden brown color.", "Remove from the oven and brush with melted butter. Sprinkle garlic salt over the top and serve with your favorite dipping sauce!"]'::jsonb, '["The Best Blog Recipes", "pepperoni", "pizza", "appetizer", "snack", "Italian", "kid friendly"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from The Best Blog Recipes (footer: thebestblogrecipes.com/wprm_print/recipe/48468, printed 11/8/22), author Shauna. Course: Appetizer, Dinner. Cuisine: American, Italian. 254 kcal. Total time 24 mins. Page 1 of 2; page 2 not in the photos (page 1 already has all ingredients and all 6 steps; page 2 may hold notes).

Couldn''t read for sure: footer URL recipe number ''48468'' (slightly blurry)', NULL),
('Stuffed-Meatball Rigatoni Bake with a Parmesan & Panko Crust', NULL, 2, 10, 35, '["1/2 cup mozzarella cheese", "1/2 cup panko breadcrumbs", "10 oz ground beef", "1 TBSP Tuscan heat spice", "6 oz rigatoni pasta", "14 oz marinara sauce", "3 TBSP Parmesan cheese"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '["HelloFresh", "beef", "meatballs", "pasta", "Italian", "bake"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'HelloFresh recipe card front only; steps page not in the photos (Bust Out pantry list is also on the steps page). Calories: 1170. Hello Tuscan Heat Spice: Our blend of aromatic Italian-style herbs also packs a peppery punch. **In our ongoing effort toward sustainability, we''re working on reducing plastic in your order! You may have received 4 servings of protein in one package—rest assured it contains the correct amount. 4-person amounts: 1 cup mozzarella, 1 cup panko, 20 oz ground beef, 2 TBSP Tuscan heat spice, 12 oz rigatoni, 28 oz marinara sauce, 6 TBSP Parmesan.

