('Summertime Frozen Fruit Slush', NULL, 25, NULL, NULL, '["1 1/2 cup sugar", "2 cups water", "1 can (6 oz) frozen orange juice concentrate", "1 lg. can crushed pineapple (plus all liquid)", "1 small can (or 1 1/2 cup) apricot nectar", "1 lg. packet of frozen strawberries", "4-5 bananas, sliced into small bites"]'::jsonb, '["Boil 1 1/2 cup sugar and 2 cups water. Once it comes to a quick boil (about 1 min) remove from heat. Set to the side.", "Add these ingredients together: 1 can (6 oz) frozen orange juice concentrate (it''s the smallest can in the frozen department), 1 lg. can crushed pineapple (plus all liquid!), 1 small can (or 1 1/2 cup) apricot nectar, 1 lg. packet of frozen strawberries (I thaw just enough to cut up each strawberry into small slices), 4-5 bananas - sliced into small bites.", "Add all the fruit and juice above to the boiled sugar/water mixture. Mix by hand. I use a measuring cup w/a handle to dip into this mix and pour into those plastic cups left over from your wedding. Makes approx. 25 - 9 oz sized Hefty plastic tumblers. I put filled cups in a 13x9 cake pan (1/3 - 1/2 full) to freeze in freezer.", "Once plastic cups freeze - I take off cake pan & put them 10-12 in gallon freezer bags! Thaw slightly when ready to use."]'::jsonb, '["drink", "dessert", "frozen", "fruit", "slush", "family recipe"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten letter-style recipe (Evernote printout dated 2/4/2021; card dated 11-22-?). "(this was a family recipe which we ate alot on farm!)". The last step comes from handwritten notes written sideways in the left and right margins. Makes approx. 25 9-oz cups.

Couldn''t read for sure:; year in date "11-22-??" illegible; left margin "gallon freezer bags": "freezer" partly cut off; right margin note: best reading "Thaw slightly when ready to use. (Save cups.)"', NULL),
('Sun-dried Tomato Pesto with Bowtie Pasta', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 pound uncooked bowtie pasta", "1 (8-oz) jar sun-dried tomatoes in olive oil", "8 oz. peppered bacon, or bacon with 1/4 t. black pepper", "1 (10-oz) jar basil pesto", "1 c. grated Romano", "black pepper"]'::jsonb, '["Cook pasta according to package directions. Drain tomatoes, reserving some of the oil. Cut tomatoes into julienne strips.", "Cook bacon in a large skillet over medium-high heat until crisp. Drain and crumble.", "Drain pasta, shake off excess water and place in a large bowl. Add tomatoes and pesto; mix well. Add bacon and Romano and toss well. For a moister consistency, add some of reserved sun-dried tomato oil. Season ..."]'::jsonb, '["pasta", "bacon", "pesto", "Italian"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Printed newspaper clipping by Kathy Dicharo(?), Bryan, Texas, taped beside Farmer''s Casserole in a notebook (Evernote printout dated 2/4/2021). The clipping is cut off at the bottom of the photo: the last step ends at ''oil. Season ...'' (probably ''Season with black pepper''), and anything after that is missing. A dark stain covers the pesto ingredient line.

Couldn''t read for sure: ''(8-oz) jar'': size blurry; pesto line mostly stained: best reading ''1 (10-oz) jar basil pesto''; ''grated Romano'': ''Ro'' stained; author surname blurry (Dicharo?); end of last step cut off

A page of this recipe was missing from the photos.', NULL),
('Sweet & Sour Meatballs', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["2 eggs", "1 onion", "3/4 c. bread crumbs", "1/2 tsp. salt", "1 lb hamburger", "1 tblsp oil for the pan", "1 3/4 c. tomato juice", "1/2 c. brown sugar", "10 ginger snaps", "1/8 c. vinegar", "1/2 tsp onion salt"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '["beef", "meatballs", "sweet and sour", "handwritten"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe on a lined notebook page, printed from an Evernote note ("Untitled note", page 2 of 3, dated 2/4/2021). Meatballs: eggs, onion, bread crumbs, salt, hamburger, oil for the pan. "For sauce": tomato juice, brown sugar, ginger snaps, vinegar, onion salt. No directions were written. Title written as "Sweet & Sour meatballs"; "vinager" spelled as written.

Couldn''t read for sure: "1 tblsp oil for the pan" (handwriting); "1/8 c. vinegar" (written "vinager")', NULL),
('Sweet Potato and Sausage Hash', NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, '["1 tbsp coconut oil", "1 large sweet potato, cubed", "salt, pepper, garlic powder, cumin, cinnamon, to taste", "3 Whole 30 compliant pre-cooked sausage link (or chicken sausage)", "1 large red bell pepper, sliced", "1 red onion, sliced", "avocado, for garnish", "parsley, for garnish"]'::jsonb, '["Heat 1 tbsp coconut oil in large skillet over medium high heat. Add sweet potatoes and seasonings. Cook with pan covered for ~10 minutes, stirring occasionally.", "Add peppers and onions and more salt. Cover and cook for 10 more minutes; stirring occasionally.", "When potatoes are cooked through (check by stabbing them with a fork), add a sliced sausage link to pan. Sautee uncovered for 5 minutes.", "Garnish with avocado slices and parsley."]'::jsonb, '["Whole30", "sausage", "sweet potato", "hash", "breakfast", "paleo"]'::jsonb, '["breakfast"]'::jsonb, 'From a "Winter Whole30 Recipes" handout (Breakfast section). Source: wholefoodblog. Printed garnish line: "Garnish: Avocado, parsley".', NULL),
('Swiss Steak (crock pot)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["2 lbs. round steak", "1 1/4 tsp. salt", "1/4 tsp. pepper", "1 med. onion, sliced in rings", "2 tbsp. shortening (bacon grease)", "1 med. green bell pepper, cut in 1 in. pieces", "1 1-lb. can tomatoes, cut up (can use food processor to cut up)", "1 cup water", "2 cloves garlic", "1/4 cup water (for gravy)", "2 tbsp. cornstarch or flour (for gravy)"]'::jsonb, '["Cut meat into 1\" cubes. Brown in oil (I use bacon grease). Add onion and garlic. Fry until onions are limp. Add water, then remaining ingredients. Cook in crock pot.", "Can serve over rice, or mashed potatoes, or french fries. Thicken sauce for gravy as follows. In 1/4 cup water, add 2 tbsp. cornstarch or flour. Blend. Slowly stir into sauce. Simmer till thickened, about 10 min."]'::jsonb, '["beef", "steak", "Swiss steak", "slow cooker", "crock pot"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Printed email (dated Thu, Aug 12, 2010) taped into the recipe notebook (Evernote printout 2/2/2021). The right edge of the email is cut off: the gravy sentence ends "...about 10 min. Do..." with the rest missing. Signed off "Enjoy" / "Love ya." No crock pot time or setting is given.

Couldn''t read for sure: ''In 1/4 cup water'' (''water'' partly cut off at right edge); Sentence after ''about 10 min.'' starting ''Do...'' is cut off', NULL),
('Taco Pasta Salad', 'This delicious summertime salad is loaded with seasoned meat, taco toppings and cheese. Serve this easy side dish with your favorite BBQ recipes.', 8, 20, 10, '["6 cups rotini pasta cooked", "1 lb ground beef", "1 tsp garlic powder", "1 cup salsa divided", "1/4 cup extra virgin olive oil divided", "1/2 tbsp cumin", "1 tsp chili powder", "1 tsp oregano", "1 cup cherry tomatoes cut in half", "1 red pepper diced", "3 green onions sliced", "1 1/2 cups cheddar cheese shredded", "1/2 cup cilantro chopped", "salt and pepper to taste"]'::jsonb, '["In a medium skillet over medium-high heat, add 1 tablespoon of extra virgin olive oil. Once the skillet is hot, add ground beef, garlic powder and 3 tablespoons of salsa. Cook until the meat is browned (about 8 to 10 minutes).", "Place the beef in a bowl and let it cool.", "Add the cooked pasta to a large salad bowl. Add the beef mixture, tomatoes, red pepper, green onion, cilantro and cheddar cheese. Mix to combine.", "Add the rest of the olive oil, salsa, cumin, chili powder, oregano, salt and pepper. Stir until everything is combined. Chill in the fridge until ready to serve. Serve cold."]'::jsonb, '["Simply Stacie", "pasta salad", "salad", "Mexican", "beef", "side"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Printed from Simply Stacie (Taco Pasta Salad by Simply Stacie). Author: Stacie Vaughan. Course: Salad. Cuisine: Mexican. Total time 30 minutes. 479 kcal per serving. URL in footer too blurry to copy (simplystacie.net/taco-pasta-salad).', NULL),
('Taco Soup', NULL, NULL, NULL, 60, '["1 lb ground beef chuck", "1 large chopped onion", "1 pkg. taco seasoning mix", "1 pkg. Hidden Valley Ranch dressing mix", "1 (16 oz) can pinto beans", "1 (16 oz) can chili beans", "1 (16 oz) can whole kernel corn", "1 (16 oz) can stewed tomatoes", "1 can Rotel", "1 can refried beans", "1 tbls chilli powder", "2 spoonful of garlic"]'::jsonb, '["Brown meat and onion and drain grease. Transfer to a large pot and add taco seasoning and all other ingredients (without draining). Let simmer for about 1 hour."]'::jsonb, '["Pinterest", "beef", "soup", "Mexican"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Pinterest printout (page 1/3). Handwritten below the recipe: "1 can Refried Beans, 1 tbls chilli powder, 2 spoonful of Garlic" (added to ingredients). The Pinterest pin URL is printed in the footer but the pin number isn''t fully legible.', NULL),
('Taco Tater Casserole', 'This Tater Taco Casserole is a Mexican mixture of taco meat, beans, corn, and cheese topped with tater tots and enchilada sauce.', 8, NULL, 45, '["1 lb ground beef", "1 (15 oz) can black beans", "1 (12 oz) package corn, frozen", "1 (4 oz) can Old El Paso diced green chiles", "1 clove garlic", "1 onion, small", "1 (28 oz) package tater tots, frozen", "1 (1 oz) package Old El Paso taco seasoning mix", "3 cups Mexican blend cheese", "1 (10 oz) can Old El Paso red enchilada sauce", "salsa"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat oven 375°.", "Brown meat with onion & garlic.", "Add salsa, taco seasoning, black beans & corn, 2 cups of cheese.", "Put into pan, arrange tater tots & pour enchilada sauce over the top of the casserole.", "Bake 30-40 min."]'::jsonb, '["Pinterest", "The Girl Who Ate Everything", "beef", "casserole", "Mexican", "tater tots"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Pinterest printout (page 1/3, 9/16/21) of a pin from the-girl-who-ate-everything.com (41 reviews, 45 minutes, serves 8). The pin lists only ingredients; the steps are handwritten on the page: "Preheat oven 375°. Brown meat with onion & garlic. Add salsa, taco seasoning, black beans & corn, 2 cups of cheese. Put into pan arrange tater tots & pour enchilada sauce over the top of the casserole. Bake 30-40 min." Salsa is in the handwritten steps but not the printed list (no amount given). The handwritten steps don''t mention the green chiles or the last cup of cheese. Pinterest pin URL is in the footer but the number isn''t fully legible.

Couldn''t read for sure: oven temperature handwritten ''375°'' (could read 315°); ''taco seasoning'' partly hidden by glare; ''2 cups of cheese'' partly hidden by glare; ''arrange'' (written ''a range'')', NULL),
('Tex-Mex Beef and Potatoes', NULL, 6, 10, 20, '["1 lb. ground beef", "1 medium red or green pepper, chopped (about 1 cup)", "1 medium onion, chopped (about 3/4 cup)", "1 pkg. (1 1/4 oz.) Taco Bell Home Originals taco seasoning mix", "1/2 cup water", "4 cups frozen Southern-style hash browns (cubed, not shredded, variety)", "1 pkg. (10 oz.) frozen corn", "1/2 lb. (8 oz.) Velveeta pasteurized prepared cheese product, cut up"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat oven to 350°F. Brown meat with peppers and onions in large skillet on medium-high heat, stirring occasionally to break up the meat; drain. Return meat mixture to skillet.", "Add taco seasoning mix and water; stir until well blended. Stir in potatoes, corn and Velveeta. Spoon into a 13 x 9-inch glass baking dish; cover with foil.", "Bake 20 min. Uncover; stir gently. Bake, uncovered, an additional 15 min. or until heated through."]'::jsonb, '["Velveeta", "beef", "potatoes", "Tex-Mex", "casserole"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Velveeta (Kraft) recipe card on an Evernote printout page (2/1/2021). Makes 6 servings, about 1-1/3 cups each. The card says Prep: 10 minutes / Cook: 20 minutes, although the bake is 20 + 15 minutes.

Couldn''t read for sure: Text is dark and faded; ''13 x 9-inch glass baking dish'' best reading; ''about 1-1/3 cups each'' best reading', NULL),
('The Best Banana Pudding', 'This Banana Pudding is a no-cook pudding recipe made with sweetened condensed milk, cream cheese and pudding, fresh bananas and Nilla wafers!', 12, 25, NULL, '["8 ounce block cream cheese, softened to room temperature", "14 ounce can sweetened condensed milk", "5 ounce package instant vanilla pudding mix, larger box", "3 cups milk, 2 % or higher", "2 teaspoon vanilla extract", "8 ounce tub whipped topping (COOL WHIP), thawed", "11 ounce box Nilla wafers", "5-7 bananas, peeled and sliced"]'::jsonb, '["In a large bowl, beat the cream cheese with an electric mixer on medium speed until smooth and fluffy.", "Add in sweetened condensed milk, pudding mix, milk and vanilla extract.", "Mix until combined well.", "Finally, stir in half of the whipped topping.", "To layer: place one-third of the vanilla wafers in a layer on the bottom of a trifle dish, large bowl or a 9x13 baking dish.", "Add a layer of bananas.", "Then pour one-third of the pudding mixture on top (enough to cover all the bananas).", "Continue with two more layers.", "Top with remaining whipped topping."]'::jsonb, '["The Country Cook", "dessert", "banana pudding", "no-bake", "American"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Web printout from The Country Cook (Author: Brandie @ The Country Cook), printed 9/5/22, page 1 of 2. Title on page: "The Best Banana Pudding (+Video)". Course: Dessert. Cuisine: American. Total time 25 minutes. Calories 458 kcal. Page 2 (possible further steps or notes) is not in the photos. Footer URL is too faint to read reliably (thecountrycook.net/wprm_print/...).

A page of this recipe was missing from the photos.', NULL),
('The Best Steak Fajitas', 'The absolute BEST Steak Fajitas you''ve ever had! This is my take on the tex-mex steak fajitas. Marinated for hours in lime juice, garlic, and cumin — so good you''ll never use another recipe again!', NULL, 195, 15, '["1/3 cup lime juice", "1/4 cup pineapple juice (no sugar added)", "2 tablespoons Worcestershire sauce", "3 tablespoons olive oil", "1 tablespoon minced garlic", "2 teaspoon ground cumin (or more to taste)", "2 teaspoon chili powder (or more to taste)", "1 teaspoon kosher salt", "1 teaspoon smoked paprika", "1/2 teaspoon black pepper", "1/2 teaspoon red pepper flakes (or more to taste)", "1/4 cup chopped cilantro", "1 1/2 - 2 pounds skirt or flank steak", "1 tablespoon oil (high heat)", "2 medium white onions, sliced", "1 large poblano, ribs and seeds removed then sliced", "2-3 bell peppers, thinly sliced (any color you please!)"]'::jsonb, '["Steak marinade: Combine the ingredients for the marinade in a large shallow bowl. Give it a taste and check for seasonings, adjust to preference. Coat the steak with the marinade and let sit covered in the refrigerator for at least 2-4 hours and ideally overnight. Remove from the refrigerator 30 minute prior to cooking.", "Set a large cast iron skillet or pan over high heat and let heat up for a couple of minutes. Add the steak to the pan and fry on each side for about 3-5 minutes or longer if you''d like it more done. Feel for desired firmness. The 3 minutes/side will yield a medium rare doneness. If the pan becomes too hot, reduce the heat to medium high. Remove the steak from the pan and allow to rest for several minutes tented with a piece of foil. Slice the meat against the grain into thin slices. I like to do so on an angle so the meat slices are tender and thin.", "Fajita veggies: Add the remaining tablespoon of oil to the pan over high heat, add in the onions, poblano, and bell peppers. Let the veggies begin to sizzle and toss as necessary, cook for a total of 2-3 minutes or longer if you prefer them softer, season with a pinch of salt and pepper. If your pan is small, cook the veggies in a few batches so they don''t steam.", "Assembly: Serve them in tortillas or on rice bowls topped with your favorite toppings!"]'::jsonb, '["ketodietforhealth.com", "beef", "steak", "Mexican", "Tex-Mex", "fajitas", "keto"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Web printout (3 pages) from ketodietforhealth.com, by Admin, March 23, 2023. Marinade ingredients are listed under ''Steak Marinade'', the rest under ''Fajitas''. Optional toppings: guacamole, salsa, cilantro leaves, salsa verde, sour cream, black beans, rice, tortillas, cilantro-lime rice, sautéed corn, tomatoes, lettuce, shredded cheese, etc. Total time 3 hours 30 minutes (prep includes marinating). The page also prints a ''Free Keto Meal Plan'' link (lowcarbkitchen.us), repeated as instruction step 5; omitted from steps.

Couldn''t read for sure: sourceUrl: header shows ''ketodietforhealth.com/the-best-steak-fajitas-1001a/'' without the https:// prefix (prefix added)', 'https://ketodietforhealth.com/the-best-steak-fajitas-1001a/'),
('Three Cheese Shells', NULL, NULL, NULL, 25, '["1 package jumbo pasta shells", "3 cups ricotta cheese", "3 cups shredded cheese", "1/2 cup grated Parmesan cheese", "1/2 cup chopped green pepper", "2 tablespoon dried basil", "2 eggs, lightly beaten", "2 garlic cloves", "1/2 teas seasoned salt", "1/4 teas pepper", "2 jars spaghetti sauce"]'::jsonb, '["Bake at 350° for 20-25 min."]'::jsonb, '["pasta", "stuffed shells", "cheese", "Italian", "vegetarian"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe card ("Recipe for: Three cheese shells"), faint; Evernote printout. Only the ingredient list and "350° - 20-25 min." are written; no other steps.

