('Turkey Casserole', NULL, NULL, NULL, 30, '["1 1/4 c. spaghetti pieces", "1/4 c. minced pimento", "1/4 c. diced green pepper", "1/2 c. turkey or chicken broth", "1/8 teas. pepper", "1/2 c. onion", "1 1/2 c. chicken", "1 can cream of mushroom soup", "1/8 teas. celery salt", "grated cheddar cheese", "Parmesan cheese"]'::jsonb, '["Bake at 350° - 25 to 30 min."]'::jsonb, '["chicken", "turkey", "pasta", "casserole"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten notebook page (Evernote printout dated 2/3/2021) under a printed note label ''Chicken spaghetti''. The handwritten title''s first word is partly hidden by glare; it reads ''Tu?ke Casserole'' and is best read as ''Turkey Casserole'' (it could be ''Tuna Casserole'', but the ingredients are turkey or chicken, not tuna; the printed label calls it ''Chicken spaghetti''). The ''1/2 c. turkey or chicken'' line ends in a stain; ''broth'' is a guess since chicken is listed again separately. Only direction written: ''350° - 25 to 30 min''.

