('Um'' Um'' Good Chili', NULL, NULL, NULL, 300, '["3 lbs ground beef (80/20)", "2 cups finely chopped onions", "2 cups finely chopped green pepper", "2 cloves minced garlic (approx 1 TBS)", "1 (28 oz) can diced tomatoes, finely blended", "1 (11.5 oz) can tomato juice", "12 oz water", "4 cans Mexican style chili beans", "1/2 cup jalapeno juice (strained - no seeds)", "2 TBS chili powder", "1 1/2 tsp ground cumin", "2 tsp salt, or to taste", "1 tsp pepper"]'::jsonb, '["Stage 1: Brown all ingredients in Stage 1 (ground beef, onions, green pepper, garlic) in skillet over medium heat. Drain off excess grease.", "Stage 2: Mix all ingredients in Stage 2 (tomatoes, tomato juice, water, chili beans, jalapeno juice).", "Stage 3: Mix all ingredients in Stage 3 (chili powder, cumin, salt, pepper).", "Mix Stage 2 & 3 together.", "Add Stage 2 & 3 to Stage 1 and cook for 4 to 5 hours on high or 6 to 7 hrs on medium."]'::jsonb, '["beef", "chili", "slow cooker", "soup"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Printed recipe sheet with handwritten edits (applied above where clear):
- Handwritten above Stage 1: "P?? 3 lbs" (first word illegible) and "(80/20)" written next to the printed "3 LBS GROUND BEEF".
- Printed "2 CANS MEXICAN STYLE CHILI BEANS": the 2 is written over by hand, best reading 4 (could be 3).
- Printed "2 1/2 TBS CHILI POWDER": the "2 1/2" is struck through with a check mark; the amount appears to be reduced to 2 TBS (uncertain).
- Printed "1 TEASPOON CAYENNE PEPPER OR TO TASTE" is crossed out (X and strike-through), so it''s left out of the ingredients.
- Handwritten note by the beans: "* make sure beans don''t already have chili pepper in them" with an arrow to "or cayenne pepper".
- Handwritten after the jalapeno juice line: "(strained - no seeds)".
- A handwritten column of reduced amounts runs down the right side (a smaller batch): beef 2 lbs, onions 1 (cup), green pepper 1 (cup), garlic 1, diced tomatoes 14 oz, tomato juice 6 oz, water 6 oz.
The printed sheet gives no servings. Cook time = 4-5 hours on high (or 6-7 hrs on medium).

Couldn''t read for sure: handwritten word before ''3 lbs'' at top: illegible (looks like ''Pu..''); beef reads ''(80/20)''; chili beans can count overwritten: best reading 4, could be 3; chili powder: struck-through ''2 1/2'', reading 2 TBS remains; ''1 teaspoons pepper'' partly obscured', NULL),
('Vanilla Cinnamon Sugar Swirl Cupcakes', 'A vanilla and cinnamon base cupcake with a vanilla and cinnamon buttercream frosting', 16, NULL, 31, '["3 egg whites", "2 cup all purpose flour", "1 tsp baking powder", "1/4 tsp baking soda", "10 3/4 tsp cinnamon", "4 cups powdered sugar", "1/2 cup shortening", "1 1/2 cup sugar", "3 1/2 tsp vanilla", "1/2 cup butter, salted", "1/2 cup butter", "5/8 cup milk", "1/2 cup sour cream"]'::jsonb, '["For cupcakes: Preheat oven to 350 degrees.", "Mix together flour, cinnamon, sugar, baking soda, and baking powder in mixing bowl. I use my electric mixer.", "Add butter (room temperature), egg whites, sour cream, vanilla, and milk - Mix until smooth (no lumps).", "Add cupcake liners to cupcake pan.", "Combine cinnamon and sugar in a small bowl.", "Place 1 tbsp of batter into each cupcake liner", "Sprinkle 1/4 tsp of cinnamon sugar mixture on top of cupcake batter.", "Repeat steps until liners are half way full.", "Sprinkle a little more cinnamon sugar mixture on top of half-filled liners", "Bake for 16-18 minutes, or until a toothpick comes out with minimal crumbs", "Allow to cool for a few minutes", "Remove cupcakes and continue cooling on wire rack.", "For the frosting: Mix room temperature butter and shortening until smooth.", "Add 1 tsp of vanilla, mix until well blended", "Add powdered sugar one cup at a time and mix until well blended. (Mixture will be stiff)", "Mix in cinnamon until well blended."]'::jsonb, '["Mama Needs Cake", "dessert", "cupcakes", "cinnamon", "vanilla", "baking"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Joined from two printouts (both printed 11/2/21): a Pinterest pin page 1/3 (mamaneedscake.com, 141 reviews, 31 minutes, serves 16; ingredient list as Pinterest aggregates it: totals, not split by cupcake/frosting) and page 2/3 of the Mama Needs Cake recipe print (instructions). Page 1/3 of the Mama Needs Cake print (with the original split ingredient list; its last line ''2 tbsp milk'' shows at the top of page 2) is not in the photos. Pinterest URL printed in the footer: https://www.pinterest.com/pin/9288742972290530/ (last digits slightly blurry).

Couldn''t read for sure: ''10 3/4 tsp cinnamon'' as printed on Pinterest (likely an aggregated total); ''5/8 cup milk''; Pinterest pin number 9288742972290530

