('Vegetable Egg Frittata', NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, '["6 eggs", "1/3 cup full fat coconut milk", "1/2 tsp garlic powder", "1/2 tsp dried parsley", "1/2 tsp dried oregano", "1/2 tsp salt", "1/4 tsp ground black pepper", "2 tbsp extra-virgin olive oil", "1/2 small red onion, diced", "2 cloves garlic, peeled and minced", "1/2 pound 90% lean ground pork", "1/2 large tomato, chopped", "2-3 cups raw greens, such as spinach and kale"]'::jsonb, '["Preheat oven to 375 degrees.", "In a large bowl, whisk together eggs, coconut milk, garlic powder, parsley, oregano, salt and pepper; set aside.", "Heat olive oil over medium heat in a large cast iron skillet or other oven safe pan.", "Add onions and garlic; sauté for 3 minutes until onion starts to turn translucent. Add ground pork and cook, breaking into crumbles, until browned, 4 to 5 minutes.", "Add mushrooms and tomatoes; sauté for 2 minutes.", "Add greens and sauté until wilted. Turn off heat.", "Whisk eggs until frothy and pour into skillet.", "Bake for 15-20 minutes or until center is cooked through."]'::jsonb, '["Whole30", "eggs", "pork", "frittata", "breakfast", "paleo"]'::jsonb, '["breakfast"]'::jsonb, 'From a "Winter Whole30 Recipes" handout (Breakfast section). Source: adapted from www.teamnutritionius.com. RD Tip: Make this meal on the weekend, so all you have do in the morning is heat up in the microwave. Top with mashed avocado and cheese and serve with a side of fruit for a well-balanced meal of healthy fat, protein and carbohydrates! Note: step 5 mentions mushrooms, which are not in the printed ingredient list.', NULL),
('Vegetable Soup', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["1 soup bone", "1 pkg. of stew meat", "onion", "salt & pepper", "1 tbs of whole allspice", "cabbage", "potatoes", "carrots", "onion", "celery", "corn - 1/4 pkg.", "green beans", "3 pkgs. of Herb-Ox bouillon"]'::jsonb, '["Boil together the soup bone, stew meat, onion, salt & pepper and whole allspice.", "Take meat & bone out & strain.", "Add: cabbage, potatoes, carrots, onion, celery, corn, green beans and bouillon."]'::jsonb, '["soup", "beef", "vegetable"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe, photocopied faintly (Evernote printout, page 2/3, 2/4/2021). On the card, a bracket next to "1 soup bone" and "1 pkg of stew meat" says "boil together". The written lines are: 1 soup bone; 1 pkg of stew meat (boil together); onion; salt & pepper; 1 tbs of whole all spice; take meat & bone out & strain; Add: cabbage, potatoes, carrots, onion, celery, corn - 1/4 pkg, green beans, 3 pkgs of Herb-Ox(?) bouillon. A stray diagonal line runs across the lower part of the card (looks like a copy mark, not a crossing-out). No amounts for most vegetables.

Couldn''t read for sure: "1 tbs of whole all spice": amount read as 1 tbs (could be "1 tbls"); "take meat & bone out & strain" (faint); "potatoes" and "carrots" (faint); last line read as "3 pkgs. of Herb-Ox bouillon" (written like "3 pkgs of hab ox bullion")', NULL),
('Walking Strawberry Pretzel Salad', 'When it comes to easy, fun and unique treats, this Walking Strawberry Pretzel Salad is a hand-held version of the classic potluck dessert!', 12, 15, 0, '["3.4 ounce package instant cheesecake pudding mix", "2 cups cold milk", "12 1 ounce bags mini pretzels", "21 ounce can strawberry pie filling", "1 cup frozen whipped topping (Cool Whip), thawed", "2 tablespoon crushed pretzels, for garnish (optional)"]'::jsonb, '["Place the pudding mix and the cold milk in a large bowl.", "Whisk together for 2 minutes until it starts to thicken. Place the bowl in the refrigerator for 5 minutes to set.", "While the pudding sets, gently crush up the pretzels in the bottom of each bag before opening. This step is optional but I find this easier to eat if the pretzels are a little crushed first.", "Snip off the tops of the pretzel bags and roll down the bags on top. Place them on a serving tray or in a large casserole dish so the bags can be propped up.", "Evenly distribute the pudding among the bags.", "Evenly distribute the strawberry pie filling among the bags.", "Then top with the whipped topping.", "Garnish with the crushed pretzels and serve! Make sure you have spoons on hand for your [cut off]"]'::jsonb, '["The Country Cook", "dessert", "strawberry", "no-bake", "potluck", "American"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Web printout, page 1 of 2 (printed 7/6/22). Author: Brandie @ The Country Cook. Course: Dessert; Cuisine: American. 241 kcal per serving. Page 2 (end of step 8 and any recipe notes) not in the photos.

A page of this recipe was missing from the photos.', 'https://www.thecountrycook.net/wprm_print/80838'),
('World''s Finest Pie Crust', NULL, NULL, NULL, 15, '["3 c. flour", "1 cup lard", "1 1/2 teas salt", "1/3 c. water"]'::jsonb, '["Measure out flour & salt. Have lard room temperature. Blend all together. Add water.", "400° on oven, cook 15 min and check every 5 min."]'::jsonb, '["pie crust", "pastry", "baking", "dessert"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'Handwritten recipe card.', NULL),
('Zesty Beef & Gnocchi with Zucchini & Romano Cheese', 'In this easy dish, plump gnocchi and sautéed zucchini are paired with a hearty beef and tomato sauce spiced with hot Calabrian chile paste. Two creamy additions—smooth crème fraîche and mascarpone cheese—add cooling contrast that perfectly tames the sauce''s heat.', 4, NULL, 30, '["1 1/8 lbs ground beef", "17.6 oz gnocchi", "2 Tbsps tomato paste", "2 Tbsps mascarpone cheese", "1 1/2 tsps Calabrian chile paste", "2 cloves garlic", "2 zucchini", "2 Tbsps crème fraîche", "1/4 cup grated romano cheese"]'::jsonb, '["Prepare the ingredients: Fill a large pot 3/4 of the way up with salted water; cover and heat to boiling on high. Wash and dry the zucchini; halve lengthwise, then thinly slice crosswise. Peel and roughly chop 2 cloves of garlic.", "Cook the zucchini: In a large pan (nonstick, if you have one), heat a drizzle of olive oil on medium-high until hot. Working in two batches, add the sliced zucchini in an even layer. Season with salt and pepper. Cook, without stirring, 3 to 4 minutes, or until lightly browned. Transfer to a plate; cover with foil to keep warm. Wipe out the pan.", "Cook the beef & make the sauce: In the same pan, heat a drizzle of olive oil on medium-high until hot. Add the beef; season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring frequently and breaking the meat apart with a spoon, 4 to 5 minutes, or until lightly browned. Carefully drain off and discard any excess oil. Add the chopped garlic, tomato paste, and as much of the chile paste as you''d like, depending on how spicy you''d like the dish to be. Season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring constantly, 1 to 2 minutes, or until thoroughly combined and the beef is cooked through. Add 1 cup of water (carefully, as the liquid may splatter); season with salt and pepper. Cook, stirring frequently, 2 to 3 minutes, or until the sauce is thickened. Turn off the heat.", "Cook the gnocchi: Meanwhile, add the gnocchi to the pot of boiling water. Cook 2 to 3 minutes, or until the gnocchi float to the top of the pot. Turn off the heat. Drain thoroughly and return to the pot.", "Finish & serve your dish: To the pot of cooked gnocchi, add the cooked zucchini, cooked beef and sauce, crème fraîche, and mascarpone. Stir to thoroughly combine. Taste, then season with salt and pepper if desired. Serve the finished beef and gnocchi garnished with the romano. Enjoy!"]'::jsonb, '["Blue Apron", "beef", "gnocchi", "pasta", "Italian", "spicy"]'::jsonb, '["dinner"]'::jsonb, 'Blue Apron recipe card. Did You Know? Calabrian chile paste is made in Calabria, a region of Italy known for its bright red, hot peppers. Steps also use olive oil, salt and pepper. Wine pairing: Bold & Spicy.

Couldn''t read for sure: ground beef amount: best reading ''1 1/8 lbs'' (small fraction)', NULL);
